(14, 44, 468, 1, NULL, '2004-06-22', '2004-09-04', '2005-08-04', '4', '2435', '321211', '46550000', '158', '100000', 'Plywood', '114729', '7344', '0', '0', '0', '0', '0', '0', '2-day audit. \'Excellent Report\', \'Absolutely Helpful\', \'Great to get an outside perspective\'. They are still working to complete moving their production to the new site. This is scheduled to be completed by October 2005. They have been able to implement some recommendations. They expect to go after quite a few more once the full process is up and running.', 'Our dust collection system AR was one influence on their decision  to engage a consulting firm to perform a full study of the dust collection system to identify further opportunities to improve  efficiency.', '', '104067', 0, '0000-00-00', '', ''),
(15, 45, 469, 1, NULL, '2004-06-23', '2004-08-24', '2005-08-29', '4', '2431', '321911', '15000000', '115', '', 'Door & Window Frame Parts', '10200', '4080', '0', '0', '0', '0', '0', '0', 'Our original contact was no longer at Woodgrain. I was put in contact with ScottI Laroque. He  scanned through the report and decided he should spend some quality time looking through it. The team obviously put a lot of effort into this project.\n When this was done this plant was running with a crew size approxamiately 60% bigger than we currently have at this time. This will obviously translate to longer pay back periods for many of the projects. He does not believe  anybody there really did anything but forward this report on to \\\'higher authorities\\\' and it probably got set aside.\n Unfortunately it looks like at the moment the entire follow-up on this report had been dropped and nothing was implemented. Money got very tight so no investments were made. Even the no cost recommendations were dropped, likely as no-one involved in bringing us in to prepare the report was around to act on it. They have an a intern working there this summer and will also ask him to review this and do some follow up.', '', '', '0', 0, '0000-00-00', '', ''),
