(44, 74, 498, 2, NULL, '2005-09-15', '2006-01-31', '2007-07-17', '6', '3582', '333312', '3500000', '36', '50000', 'Laundry Equipment', '80', '2000', '295', '100', '', '100', '', '', 'Production Manager mostly interested in productivity opportunities.  I offered the possibility of a continuing partnership in the form of future partial assessments on focus areas or opportunities, subject of course to USDOE approval.', 'Comments to be entered by interviewer only !', '', '3600', 0, '0000-00-00', '', ''),
(45, 75, 499, 1, NULL, '2006-01-26', '2006-06-07', '2008-10-20', '5', '2051', '311812', '50000000', '120', '230000', 'Bread', '27903', '7332', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Quite helpful.', 'Decided to go even harder after steam costs. Will determine required steam and compare to actual use, to provide more feedback to operators making steam injection decisions.', '', '12000', 0, '0000-00-00', '', ''),
(46, 76, 500, 1, NULL, '2006-04-28', '2006-09-19', '2007-08-21', '5', '3577', '334119', '25000000000', '3000', '2000000', 'Electronic Computer', '', '8760', '0', '400', '', '100', '', '126', 'A key value of the assessment was the opportunity to brainstorm with IAC team and facilities engineers all together. The fresh outside perspective helped them generate new ideas of areas to focus.', '', '', '87500', 0, '0000-00-00', '', ''),
(47, 77, 501, 1, NULL, '2006-03-24', '2006-07-06', '2008-09-30', '5', '5143', '311513', '309000000', '570', '300000', 'Cheese', '114000000', '8', '4478', '200', '44860', '150', '1750', '125', 'As we have little in the way of sub-metering, I\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'m unable to measure specific reductions from individual projects.  However, despite increasing production levels, our overall energy consumption is constant to slightly down, so the cumulative effect of our efforts is reducing our energy use per unit of production.\n  \n In a plant such as ours, the level of complexity is often too much for an outside person to digest in a day or two.  This is true of professional consulting engineers, and particularly so with college-level students.  It might be better to focus on particular systems rather than try to bite off the whole plant.  These could be:\n  \n     Process heating and boiler systems.\n     Process cooling and refrigeration systems.\n     Compressed air.\n     HVAC.\n     Lighting (electrical).\n     Pumps and blowers (electrical).\n     Water conversation (hot or cold water down the drain usually has an energy component to it).\n  \n The ideas were generally useful.  Cost estimates were not.  The level of detail in the reports was far more than we need.  Since most of it was appendix, it was easy to ignore and yet have for reference, if needed.', '', '', '265260', 0, '0000-00-00', '', ''),
(48, 78, 502, 1, NULL, '2006-06-05', '2006-09-08', '2007-12-12', '7', '2421', '321113', '42500000', '145', '1742400', 'Dimensional Lumber', '55000000', '4000', '7175', '500', '6900', '15', '2875', '100', '', '', '', '57200', 0, '0000-00-00', '', ''),
(49, 79, 503, 2, NULL, '2006-06-26', '2006-09-30', '2007-07-10', '5', '2033', '311422', '35000000', '290', '653400', 'Fruit Puree', '80000', '6336', '1306', '75', '', '', '', '100', 'Assessment process better than last time.  More commitment from plant, including engineering intern dedicated to project.  Were able to cut and paste sections of report into justification to implement projects', 'Comments to be entered by interviewer only !', '', '75500', 0, '0000-00-00', '', ''),
