(84, 114, 538, 1, '', '2008-07-23', '2008-08-18', '2009-08-13', '6', '5142', '424420', '250000000', '550', '170000', 'Frozen pizzas, Canned goods', '31000000', '1664', '300', '', '', '', '200', '', 'Could Not Contact', '', '', '0', 1, '0000-00-00', '', ''),
(85, 115, 539, 1, '', '2008-07-28', '2008-11-21', '2009-08-13', '', '3357', '331319', '250000000', '50', '250000', 'High Voltage Cable', '146800', '8760', '4025', '', '', '', '335', '', 'Could Not Contact', '', '', '0', 1, '0000-00-00', '', ''),
(86, 116, 540, 2, '', '2008-08-11', '2009-01-08', '2009-08-04', '6', '2869', '325199', '29000000', '32', '49000', 'Process Chemicals', '40000000', '8760', '577.5', '', '', '', '50', '', '8/09: Plant was sold to Ashland ~Sept 2008, shortly after assessment.  Due to condition of the industry \\\'capital has ben cut back to $0 shortly after our audit in Portland.  Paybacks for any projects had to be well under 1 yr to even be considered.\\\'', 'Comments to be entered by interviewer only !', '', '0', 0, '0000-00-00', '', ''),
(87, 117, 541, 1, NULL, '2008-08-21', '2008-10-23', '2009-07-01', '', '2834', '325412', '14000000', '75', '9400', 'Peptides, Amino Acids', '55000', '8160', '753', '100', '6900', '110', '371', '110', 'My feedback is strongly positive.  From the opening discussions with Joe to the report follow-up by Carl, I was impressed with what was offered.  Initially I was apprehensive that the students would focus on just some low-hanging fruit (e.g., stop air leaks, turn off lights, stop water drips), but the final package provided real projects that will save energy and money.  The report recommendations have been discussed in our senior management meeting and Environmental Management System Review meetings several times.  The final report was well structured and gave us the starting data we needed to help prioritize the projects for implementation.\n \n At this point I am unsure if we will be implementing the other recommendations in the next year.  As a team we prioritized the first recommendation (burning solvent waste) and are putting all our resources into making this happen.  Please check back later on the other items.', '', '', '0', 0, '2012-11-01', '', ''),
(88, 118, 542, 1, '', '2008-09-09', '2008-12-30', '2012-05-11', '7', '3448', '332311', '30000000', '170', '140000', 'steel buildings', '40', '8', '1784.5', '', '', '', '63', '', 'I first got hold of our original contact, Roger Schramm. He told me he left that site soon after he received the report. He said it provided good information and shared it and my earlier implementation queries  with his replacement. His replacement has since also left and Joe Hanson is now the Plant Manager. I sent the a copy of the report to Joe. He said nothing was implemented because of all the management changes at the site, but they are now working to cut energy costs and it would be worth following up with him again. ', 'Joe Hanson 509-444-7149', '', '0', 1, '0000-00-00', '', ''),
(89, 137, 561, 1, '', '2010-06-24', '2010-08-19', '2012-10-12', '4', '2037', '311411', '285000000', '522', '310000', 'French Fries', '1500000', '8400', '', '', '93644', '250', '1862', '160', 'The assessment was helpful and the report was very easy to follow and to utilize for support to get capital funding.   I do feel that there is a lot to analyze in a short amount of time ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â‚¬Å“ if there were opportunity to extend the assessment, that could be a plus.\n\n\nThe electricity incentives have provided very good paybacks for energy reduction. Our focus has been to implement those while the incentives are available. The cost to  implement AR2 was much higher than contained in the assessment. BETC may help with this one too ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â‚¬Å“ or may be combined with another project to get it done', '', '', '0', 0, '0000-00-00', '', ''),
(90, 138, 562, 2, '', '2010-08-03', '2010-10-05', '2012-10-22', '5', '2431', '321911', '12000000', '70', '141530', 'Remanufactured Lumber Products', '', '2250', '', '150', '', '', '', '120', 'Having the IAC Team there kicked off a new perspective on energy at the plant. We understand our energy bill better now, and how to keep in control. ', 'Split our finger joint plant into cells. Now equipment with each cell only runs when that cell is active. We also discovered that our heat system can bring the facility and materials up to a suitable production temperature in a few hours. Now we turn the heat off over the weekend and only turn it on in time to be at temperature when production starts.', '', '0', 0, '0000-00-00', '', ''),
(91, 139, 563, 2, '', '2010-08-04', '2010-11-08', '2012-10-30', '5', '2421', '321113', '25000000', '125', '565000', 'Wood Boards and Chip', '1150000', '8400', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'The OSU Assessment was very helpful and your Staff and Students were very cooperative,  professional and a pleasure to work with.   The OSU visit and report was influential in helping us make some of these decisions and enforced our own beliefs.   WSFPI Staff and Management are always communicating with other biomass-fired Power Plant Owner / Operators about upgrades that can benefit our common interests.   Overall, the comments and feedback that I received from my associates at WSFPI were all positive about the OSU Assessment amd recommendations made in the report.', '', '', '219000', 0, '0000-00-00', '', ''),
(92, 140, 564, 1, '', '2010-08-17', '2010-11-30', '2012-10-15', '5', '2435', '321211', '42000000', '228', '180000', 'Plywood', '125000000', '8760', '6884', '400', '0', '0', '910', '110', 'Been slow market since assessment. Reduced hours. Down to 2 shifts from 3. Has impeded implementation', '', '', '0', 0, '0000-00-00', '', ''),
