(691, 728, 748, 1, '', '2013-03-27', '2013-07-18', '2014-06-16', '6', '4952', '222132', 'N/A', '150', '2000000', 'Reclaimed Water', '115 MGD', '8760', '28961', '48961', '6000', '10', '700', '100', 'Thus far none of the recommendations of have been implemented.  They are still considering AR 1& 6.', 'None.', NULL, '$0', 0, '0000-00-00', 'None.', ''),
(692, 729, 749, 1, 'Andreas Winardi - Puget Sound Energy', '2013-03-26', '2013-07-17', '2014-02-26', '6', '9511', '924110', '2337095', '9', '165700', 'Treated Wastewater', '1.9 MGD Average', '8760', '646.5', '', '', '', '60', '120', 'Unfortunately due to budgetary constraints, the following projects did not come to fruition. In 2013 is was discovered that we had severe structural failures on one of our two anaerobic digester covers. We were currently in the process of working with Trane an Energy Services Company to coordinate and contract for the projects. The digester cover became a priority and forced a deferment of the projects until sometime in the future. As we are replacing one cover in 2014 and one in 2015, it would not be until 2016 or later that the energy conservation projects will be brought back to the table.\n \nHowever, with that said, staff did  investigate feasibility and implemented some of the recommended operation considerations that were provided as part of the energy assessment.  Here is a brief history of items identified:\n ', '2.0 Also, please take into consideration that the conversations that were had during collection of data and review of the report influenced staff to look at energy conservation in a different way. Staff are more aware of energy usage based on process control changes and have implemented various methodologies to reduce energy last year with little to no capital outlay.  The South Kitsap Water Reclamation Facility has reduced its electrical energy consumption by 29% compared to usage in 2012.  ', '', '', 0, '2017-01-01', '', ''),
(693, 730, 745, 2, '', '2013-03-20', '2013-07-12', '2014-07-03', '6', '2421', '321113', '9000000', '56', '1220000', 'Lumber', '24000000', '2040', '1600', '200', '0', '0', '275', '92', 'Audit was a good experience and helpful for the company.  Owner would like to see more research into available incentives and more recommendations that are geared around capturing available incentives.', 'Several changes have taken place since the report including system rewiring and controls improvement that is likely to result in additional savings not included in the report.', NULL, '11000', 0, '2015-07-03', 'Facility investigated and implemented some recommendations at the facility but stayed close to the systems we considered.', ''),
(694, 731, 745, 2, 'Alan Meyer - Pacific Power', '2013-03-28', '2013-06-07', '2014-07-03', '6', '3532', '333131', '5000000', '6', '290000', 'Pellets', '31000', '8760', '250', '75', '', '', '', '', 'Trip was satisfying to facility staff.  Reaffirmed the savings and maintenance mentality at facility.', 'No spin off occurred due to this report.', NULL, '139996', 0, '2015-07-03', 'No replication occurred due to this report.', ''),
(699, 733, 182, 1, 'Alex C', '2013-04-29', '2013-07-09', '2014-07-08', '6', '2037', '311411', '85000000', '385', '207119', 'Freeze Dried Foods', '8453', '8760', '4310.5', '450', '6900', '125', '300', '100', 'Your visit and report helped change the culture around here related to energy. Things are moving now.\n\nFocused first on Refrigeration because of the significant savings. Getting ready to install the refrigeration controls now that we have ETO incentives approved. Taking advantage of ETO Refrigeration Operator Coaching(ROC). Also implementing maintenance management software. All of this has left little time for technical staff to pursue your other recommendations yet. Expect to once we get these projects put away.', 'Working with Energy Trust of Oregon for Refrigeration Operator Coaching(ROC). Allowing us to get our discharge pressure down. Estimate we are saving 20k kWh a day on refrigeration costs including savings from this.\n\nLooking at moving to electric from desiccant drying for cost savings. Looking at it this now. Expect it to be acted on in the next year but have not had time yet. ', '', '', 0, '2015-12-01', '', ''),
(700, 734, 248, 1, 'Alex C', '2013-05-10', '2013-07-22', '2014-07-08', '6', '2037', '311411', '39000000', '70', '84620', 'Freeze Dried Food', '3858', '8760', '3738', '600', '2159', '125', '200', '100', 'Your visit and report helped change the culture around here related to energy. Things are moving now.\n\nFocused first on Refrigeration because of the significant savings. Getting ready to install the refrigeration controls now that we have ETO incentives approved. Taking advantage of ETO Refrigeration Operator Coaching(ROC). Also implementing maintenance management software. All of this has left little time for technical staff to pursue your other recommendations yet. Expect to once we get these projects put away.', 'Working with Energy Trust of Oregon for Refrigeration Operator Coaching(ROC). Allowing us to get our discharge pressure down. Estimate we are saving 20k kWh a day on refrigeration costs including savings from this.\n\nLooking at moving to electric from desiccant drying for cost savings. Looking at it this now. Expect it to be acted on in the next year but have not had time yet. ', '', '', 0, '2015-12-01', '', ''),
(701, 735, 753, 4, 'IAC', '2013-05-24', '2013-07-17', '2014-05-28', '5', '2899', '325998', '8000000', '10', '9300', 'Sodium Hydrosulfite', '19000000 pounds', '6240', 'N/A', '100 ', 'N/A', 'N/A', '150', '95', 'Generally helpful but company disappointed by lack of implementable recommendations.  Report was easy to read.', 'None.', '', 'N/A', 0, '2015-05-28', 'None.', ''),
(702, 737, 528, 2, '', '2013-06-27', '2013-08-27', '2014-09-30', '', '2421', '321918', '42000000', '229', '20000', 'Secondary Wood Product', '20 million board ft.', '6230', '5355', '200', '', '', '150', '120', 'The analysis and focus has been good. We are considering projects mostly with a 1 year or less payback. We have shared the learningÃ¢â‚¬â„¢s across the organization. This facility is currently working with the Energy Trust of Oregon to better understand and implement energy savings to this facility and others.', '', NULL, '56674', 0, '2015-07-01', '', ''),
(703, 738, 844, 1, 'Pacific Power - Christina Kruger', '2013-08-13', '2013-10-09', '2015-04-24', '5', '2493', '321219', '24000000', '64', '170000', 'Fiber Cement Siding', '39000000 sq. ft.', '8064', '5300', '600', '40000', '150', '200/150', '90', 'They have a lot of new stuff. They have been bought by a different company and is now called Plycem USA - Allura. They havent done much since they are financially unstable and unable to concentrate on the recommendations. A lot of things have changed. They might be able to do something in about a year or so.', 'none', NULL, '', 0, '2016-04-24', 'none', ''),
(704, 739, 750, 4, '', '2013-06-26', '2013-08-24', '2014-07-08', '5', '2621', '322121', '22792643', '55', '135738', 'Paper', '41630 tons', '8760', '2600', '1000', '30000', '145', '100', '85', 'Facility staff found the report very helpful in generating feasible opportunities that they are following up on.', '1.15, the boiler VFD recommendation encouraged the facility to investigate additional savings opportunities with their boilers.', '', '87511', 0, '2015-07-08', '2, facility is investigating the aeration system recommendation to confirm that it works at their facility and will recommend it to sister facilities.', ''),
(705, 740, 763, 4, '', '2013-06-24', '2013-08-19', '2014-07-16', '5', '2051', '311812', '18000000', '49', '40000', 'Baked Goods', '40000000', '8112', '610', '125', '', '', '220', '100', 'Assessment visit had a lot of value and was insightful for facility staff.  Report had good detail and sufficient technical content.', '1.5 Inspired some work with the local utility.', NULL, '24099', 0, '2015-07-16', '1, facility only has one plant so no recommendations were extended to other sister plants.', ''),
(706, 741, 751, 4, '', '2013-06-25', '2013-08-21', '2015-02-04', '6', '2092', '424420', '27150000', '160', '95000', 'Seafood Products', '1249200 lb', '4680', '905', '', '', '', '0', '', 'Worked with Cascade Energy at the Same Time. Interested in that report. Costs and savings.  Sat  down with Rick Last week and sort.\n\nChanged management Tony Hass instead of Gene.\n\nDealing with company maintenance people - seems like a bother - but brings up issues in a different light than the day to day. Helpful and enjoyed everyone that.\n\n', '', NULL, '', 0, '2016-02-15', '', ''),
(707, 742, 754, 1, '', '2013-06-24', '2013-08-23', '2014-11-07', '5', '2421', '321912', '45000000', '103', '75000', 'Green Stud Lumber', '90 MMBFT', '4200', '8525', '250', '', '', '400', '100', 'The report was very helpful.  We are currently involved in a High Performance Energy Management program with ESI and Bonneville.  We used your report among others to establish areas of emphasis for improving energy efficiency.  We are currently concentrating on our compressed air system, specifically leak elimination.  We will certainly consider implementing your suggestions for the air systems if economic conditions allow.', '', NULL, '', 0, '2015-05-01', '', ''),
(708, 736, 766, 2, '', '2013-05-31', '0000-00-00', NULL, '4', '0172', '111332', '8000000', '6', '22000', 'Wine', '55000 Cases', '2080', '', '', '', '', '', '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, '0000-00-00', NULL, ''),
(709, 743, 761, 1, '', '2013-07-08', '2013-09-07', '2015-04-22', '5', '2043', '311230', '7000000', '300', '122000', 'Breakfast Cereal', '875000 boxes', '8760', '1440', '', '', '', '160', '', 'Scott - Site Electrician - only person left to talk to - Mobile: 541-228-2780\n\nChanged ownership just as we audited. Bill James and engineer and maintenance manager let go with new owner ship. Gave copy of study to new maintenance supervisor and health and safety  regarding fans. That\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'s as far as it went. Still in a whirlwind of new policies - not sure what the ultimate goals - could talk to acting supervisor - Maintenance Supervisor. - Michale Castorena - Email: mcastorena@attunefoods.com  and have him give a call. \n\n(Tricky dealing with fans and air distribution because of allergen issues, fan issues. ', 'Adding exhaust fans vfds and energy efficient.  \n\nWanting to work on correcting controls and settings on compressed air. The VFD and standard air compressor are not staged well for lead and lag operation. The pressures are also not well set. 100 PSI on standard and 125 PSI on VFD - (issue with air starvation at far end)a lot of variation in what lines run air demand fluctuates wildly.', NULL, '', 0, '0000-00-00', '', ''),
