(713, 746, 752, 3, '', '2013-07-25', '2013-09-11', '2015-02-12', '5', '1479', '212393', '13300000', '10', '287469', 'Sulfur', '84000 tons', '4940', '130', '40', '200', '50', '30', '90', 'The report was helpful and easy to read, just really long but it was summarized well.  In the future we need to be more careful about exposure to arc flash as our electrician did not take proper precautions and analysts should be trained on arc flash precautions.', '', NULL, '9765', 0, '0000-00-00', 'We have been sharing our experience with LED lighting with sister plants and have recommended your program for energy audits at other locations.', ''),
(714, 747, 768, 3, 'Puget Sound Energy', '2013-07-23', '2013-09-24', '2015-01-27', '5', '3728', '335991', '99 million', '600', '116114', 'Tools', '197223', '8760', '1000', '100', '0', '0', '100', '125', 'Ms. Straight said the assessment was helpful. They now what projects they can do in the future.The report was fairly easy to read.', '', '', '', 0, '2015-07-01', '', ''),
(715, 748, 769, 3, 'PSE - Andreas Winardi', '2013-07-24', '2013-09-18', '2015-03-20', '', '3728', '335991', '99000000', '450', '160000', 'Production Units', '365689', '8760', '440', '540', '', '', '100', '127', 'Report very helpful. No feedback for when we were here on site because Jessica was not with the company (previous contact Darren Wilson has left the company).', '', '', '0', 0, '0000-00-00', 'Planning on using this report for Hwy 20 plant to reduce freezer costs, consolidating freezer at Hwy 20 plant because of this recommendation.', ''),
(716, 749, 773, 1, '', '2013-08-14', '2013-11-01', '2015-11-23', '5', '2436', '321212', '26884000', '150', '400000', 'Softwood Veneer', '352679 msf', '6800', '2362.5', '', '130000', '625', '450', '90', 'General feedback regarding the Energy Assessment Report format:\nPros\n-          Appeared comprehensive – it covered the major areas that utilize steam and energy supplied by the Boiler;\n\n-          Providing actual dollar amount cost savings appeared to be useful information for operational personnel;\n\n \nCons\n-          Verifying that all Boiler MACT Energy Assessment requirements were met, as specified in 40 CFR 63, Subpart JJJJJJ, was difficult;\n\n-          The Appendices may not have been particularly useful and appeared to add unnecessary bulk to the report.\n\n ', 'none', '1', '', 0, '0000-00-00', 'none', '1'),
(717, 752, 687, 2, 'OMEP', '2014-01-08', '2014-04-14', '2015-09-15', '4', '2431', '321213', '2200000', '34', '65000', 'moulding', '150000', '1550', '1140', '', '', '', '265', '', 'The person that I was in contact during the implementation cost said that most of the recommendations were practical. The only reason they have not been implemented is because their is no capital. The person explained that after the audit, the facility had to decrease their operational hours and lay off workers. There average operational hours decreased from 32 to 20 per week. ', 'N/A', '', '1200', 0, '2015-03-15', 'N/A', ''),
(718, 754, 131, 1, 'Clark PUD - Sam Walker - Larry Blaufus', '2013-10-11', '2013-12-24', '2015-04-28', '', '2231', '313210', '24000000', '290', '300000', 'Woolen Textiles', '1500000 yards', '8760', '1950', '', '', '', '160', '', 'Jan 4, 2014 email: I have briefly reviewed the recommendations in the draft report.  The report is thorough and contains a lot of useful information.  All of the recommendations will be reviewed and considered based on their individual costs and merits.  We eagerly look forward to receiving the completed report.\n \nAR No. 1, Upgrade Air Compressor Controls, contains one error.  The mills fire sprinkler system consists of 18 risers or separate systems.\nOf the 18, only 9 are dry systems requiring pressurization at 40 psi with compressed air.  Air is supplied to each riser from the s compressed air system, i.e. the 100 hp Gardner Denver.  There is no dedicated air compressor for the fire system.\n \nAR No. 2, Shut off Exhaust Fans, has been discussed previously and will be easy to implement.\n \nAR No. 3, Flash Steam Recovery, has a good return and makes sense.  It may require replacing some or all of the existing condensate receivers.\n \nAR No. 4, Upgrade Lighting, is in progress.  We have signed a letter of agreement with Clark PUD to complete the exterior lighting conversion to LED by 4/1/14.  We have also considered motion controls for the Dyehouse basement in the past and will probable go ahead.  It will require reconfiguring the existing lighting circuit layout.\n \nThe Other Measures Considered, are food for thought and may fit in with long term planning such as replacing the continuous washer in Finish with a more water efficient process.\n ', '1.25 The forklift \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Other Measure Considered\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" is in the process of being implemented. One of the four propane forklifts has been replaced with the first electric forklift in response to the recommendation. One more forklift is scheduled for replacement by an electric forklift during the next budget cycle.  We have also replaced a propane forklift at the Pendleton, Oregon mill with an electric due to the recommendation.\n\nAnother recommendation was to insulate non insulated areas of steam piping.  This is an on-going effort.', NULL, 'NaN', 0, '0000-00-00', '', ''),
(719, 755, 755, 1, 'Sean McCaffery ', '2013-10-10', '0000-00-00', NULL, '5', '2037', '311411', '', '', '', 'Fruit Products', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, '0000-00-00', NULL, ''),
(720, 756, 764, 1, '', '2013-10-14', '2013-12-13', '2015-08-12', '4', '3599', '33271', '$15 Million', '70', '45000', 'Machined Parts', '325000', '4160', '800', '40', '', '', '75', '118', 'None of the measures were implemented do to lack of internal projects at the facility. The facility has only been focusing on operations and not internal improvement projects. ', '', '', '0', 0, '2015-08-12', '', ''),
(721, 753, 782, 1, '', '2013-07-24', '0000-00-00', NULL, '4', '2084', '312130', '72000000', '49', '52170', 'wine', '200000', '1728', '', '', '', '', '', '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, '0000-00-00', NULL, ''),
(722, 758, 31, 1, 'Karl Haapala', '2013-11-07', '2014-02-12', '2015-06-11', '4', '2037', '311411', '30000000', '250', '83000', 'Frozen Vegetables, Grains, Legumes, and Fruit', '', '6432', '180', '', '', '', '65', '', 'Hi Brad,\n\nI am sorry that I havent gotten back to you until now. \n\nWe have not implemented any of the cost savings ideas that were generated.  Each of these items is contained on our engineering task list, but due to engineeriong resources we have not been able to implement.  Our resources have been required to focus on items more closely related to keeping our processing plants running.  The analysis was well done and beneficial in that it helped us to understand what opportunities exist for improvement and savings.  We plan to further review each and implement as resources become available.\n\nKind regards,\n\nThane Ashcraft\n\nStahlbush Island Farms, Inc.\n\nCell: 541-230-4944', 'No recommendations implemented yet.', '1', '', 0, '2015-12-11', 'No recommendations implemented yet.', '1'),
(723, 750, 587, 1, '', '2013-07-24', '0000-00-00', NULL, '4', '2084', '312130', '', '', '52170', 'Wine', '200000', '2856', '', '', '', '', '', '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, '0000-00-00', NULL, ''),
(724, 759, 759, 1, 'PSE', '2013-12-16', '2014-02-14', '2015-06-26', '4', '4952', '221320', '0', '67', '653400', 'Wastewater Treatment', '4197500 Thousand Gallons', '8760', '5000', '500', '0', '0', '150', '116', 'Implemented these cool Nest Thermostat.\nWorking on that for self-reporting mechanism.\nOccupancy sensors.\n\nOther things done:\nRaising set well flow. Need extra room to absorb flow in winter, but summer can calm down.\nPut together an energy team, looking for opportunities and implementing.\n', 'Created an energy analyzing team on site.', '2', '75000', 0, '2016-06-26', 'Use Photocell Controls.', '2'),
(725, 760, 494, 1, 'Clark County Food Project', '2014-02-28', '2014-05-01', '2015-08-12', '4', '2083', '311213', '', '105', '75000', 'Malted Barley', '120000', '6240', '3629', '', '', '', '125', '', 'Implemented ARs 1 and 4', '', '', '518000', 0, '2015-05-20', 'Implemented AR\'s 1 and 4', ''),
(726, 761, 807, 4, 'Facility Request', '2014-03-26', '2014-06-17', '2015-09-16', '4', '2087', '311930', '', '36', '82000', 'Fountain Syrup', '12166435', '2250', '500', '30', '', '12', '100', '110', 'Implemented 2/5. Two weren\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'t implemented because the facility will be replacing the equipment soon. ', 'The facility did replace some equipment that analysts had identified as opportunities, though not exactly what we recommended. ', '2', '3367', 0, '0000-00-00', 'The facility did not replicate on more equipment or at another facility', '0'),
(727, 762, 760, 4, 'Corporate Coca Cola', '2014-03-25', '2014-06-17', '2015-09-01', '6', '2086', '312111', '', '450', '305000', 'Cases Distributed Annually', '22672500', '5800', '', '200', '27600', '110', '400', '100', 'Ann Macdonald has a new role in the facility: her new title is called director, program management(EHS) system of the future and that I should contact Ronald Jacobsen who is the maintenance manager\nNew role: diecor, program management(EHS) system of the future\nMaintenance managers: ronald jacobsen: it was a pleasure working with the team and we look forward to hopefully working together again in the future', 'We did reduce our air leaks and use of the air compressors. While investigating this project we came across a few things that we were not aware of that changed this project around. One thing we did was remove air knives that were on the lines or add air blowers that were tied to the line controls to run only when the line was running. The other part was we found out that an air line was run to our pH neutralization system to mix the waste water up. This was an added feature and run off a ball valve. The purpose was to open the compressed air line when an agitator failed. We found that this had been left on always. We have added controls to this that when an agitator faults a solenoid valve is opened and compressed air is sent to the system. Although we did not implement the project from the assessment we would not have found this without the OSU Energy Assessment.', '2', '', 0, '0000-00-00', '', '0'),
(728, 765, 183, 1, '', '2014-05-14', '2014-07-18', '2015-07-17', '5', ' 2436', '321212', '65 Million', '300', '900000', 'Plywood ', '2 Million lbs', '6864', '0', '', '', '', '450', '', 'The contact suggested that the report and process was a good way to quantify thing with more proof. He also appreciated the suggestions from analysts and the center director put things in good perspective and offered viable solutions. Further, it was a good eye opener for the maintenance and electrician crews.\n\nIn terms of the report the contact thought for a couple things the format and layout were a little hard to follow when he was wondering where some information came from.', 'From this experience they have been actively shutting off equipment for the weekends including the air compressor.', '1', '', 0, '2017-04-20', '', ''),
(729, 764, 812, 4, '', '2014-03-24', '2014-06-06', '2015-04-28', '5', '3714', '336390', '13185000', '114', '97250', 'Bus Components', '16354', '4250', '200', '60', '', '', '110', '150', 'Overall: Facility was selected as a candidate for BPA audit. Energy measures were put on hold while the BPA assessment builds an accurate picture of the facilitys energy use.\nDecrease hot dip tank hours - on hold\nReduce air leaks - currently working on\nHydronic coils - currently doing an HVAC condition assessment. Condition assessment will drive projects more so than energy.\nInstall high speed doors - Cost did not justify savings\nSolar tracking skylights - Lisa tried to get a pilot project with minimal expense. Internal politics of company killed this project.\nInsulate Dip tank lids - will consider when replacing dip tanks. \nIncrease heat recovery effectiveness on RTUs - fell off of radar\nTurn off compressors on nights and weekends - on hold\nRetro-fit Low/Unload compress with VFD controls - on hold.\n\nLisa really enjoyed working with us - regrets the BPA politics situation. West base (or east) would be another candidate for an energy audit. Lisa would be happy to have us audit again, but is primarily interested in our assessment of compressed air systems. \n\n', '1.5', '', '10969', 0, '2017-01-01', '1 AR3: A pilot program for the LED lighting and zoning AR will be tested in the north base facility.', ''),
(730, 767, 5, 1, '', '2014-06-23', '2014-08-21', '2015-07-27', '4', '2421', '321113', '140000000', '450', '450000', 'Dimensional Lumber', '', '2080', '9245', '', '', '', '1300', '', '7/27/2015\nHi Brad,\n\n Sorry for the delayed response. We have not implemented any of the recommendations at this time.\n\nWe are in the process of looking at upgrading air compressor controls at both sites.\n\nThe primary reason is that we have been busy upgrading the plant sites and upgrading controls packages and machinery.\n\nThanks,\n\nBrian', 'No recommendations implemented yet.', '1', '', 0, '2016-02-01', 'No recommendations implemented yet.', '1'),
(731, 768, 827, 1, '', '2014-06-24', '2014-08-22', '2015-07-27', '', '2436', '321211', '70000000', '317', '450000', 'Plywood and LVL', '120000000 Not Available', '4992', '5675', '530', '', '', '518', '', '7/27/2015\nHi Brad,\n\n Sorry for the delayed response. We have not implemented any of the recommendations at this time.\n\nWe are in the process of looking at upgrading air compressor controls at both sites.\n\nThe primary reason is that we have been busy upgrading the plant sites and upgrading controls packages and machinery.\n\nThanks,\n\nBrian', 'No recommendations implemented yet.', '1', '', 0, '2016-02-01', 'No recommendations implemented yet.', '1'),
(732, 769, 814, 1, 'Dave Kunz - ODEQ', '2014-04-25', '0000-00-00', '0000-00-00', '5', '3646', '335122', '30000000', '95', '87500', 'Custom Light Fixtures', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 0, '0000-00-00', '', ''),
(733, 770, 813, 1, '', '2014-06-26', '2014-08-20', '2015-08-25', '', '2082', '312120', '', '150', '125000', 'Beer', '500000 Barrels', '7488', '2033.5', '', '', '', '350', '', '', '', '', '', 0, '2016-06-30', '', ''),
(734, 771, 810, 4, '', '2014-06-27', '2014-08-07', '2015-06-12', '4', '4952', '221320', '3100000', '5', '544500', 'Thousand Gallons Treated Wastewater', '912500', '8760', '890', '150', '0', '0', '0', '0', 'Energy Trust also audited them making similar findings. They have not implemented any of the measures because they have not designated a person accountable for taking and processing the recommendations. The have been updating their PLCs and they define our recommendations as  not on hold and not out of the plate yet', '', '', '', 0, '2015-12-12', '', ''),
(735, 772, 818, 1, 'Met Nate at NWFPA conf, Jan 2014', '2014-04-24', '0000-00-00', '0000-00-00', '5', '2082', '312120', '6000000', '85', '16000', 'Craft Beer', '341000 gallons/yr', '3120', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 0, '0000-00-00', '', ''),
(736, 774, 521, 1, 'Ellen Porter RFP Corporate', '2014-08-12', '2015-12-06', '2015-07-30', '6', '2493', '321212', '120000000', '390', '6423000', 'Plywood', '316955697000 sqft', '8712', '150000', '600', '75000', '75', '500', '90', 'They were very satisfied with the report. They felt the recommendations were not super detailed, and there were some holes in the data just because we only had a day to collect data. They found the report as a helpful start to look deeper into the recommendations.  Jose said that he was moving on in the next month and that Whitney Wilson would be taking over his position.', 'They implemented two OMCs adding a light to the glue kitchen and turning the sprinklers of in the rainy season. They were also looking into a third OMC of installing a VFD on the stoker fan.', '1', '142697', 0, '2016-02-12', 'Couldn\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'t say anything about other facilities.', '0.0'),
(737, 775, 548, 2, 'Diana Knous', '2014-07-24', '2014-10-02', '2015-05-20', '5', '2435', '321211', '134000000', '514', '1000000', 'Plywood', '292705000 s.f', '8760', '1710', '', '', '', '685', '80', 'Jeremy really liked the formatting of the report. He liked that the executive summary provided a good introduction to the report but also liked that the ARs provided good analysis while not being too long. He also appreciated that the OMCs had cost/savings analysis as well. He liked how we planned the day but he wants us to acknowledge that sometimes it is hard to get the right audience in front of the group. He liked that we split up into groups of 2-3 and thought our assessment team was a good size.', '', '', '', 0, '2016-05-20', '', ''),
(738, 773, 554, 2, '', '2014-07-25', '2014-10-29', '2015-07-14', '5', '2439', '321213', '112000000', '152', '625707', 'Engineered Wood Facility', '35 Million linear feet 4 Million board-feet', '8760', '13403.15', '250', '75000', '75', '500', '100', '-The facility has not got around to the major recommendations due to installing a new jet dryer. A follow up date has been assigned to find out if they went through with AR 1, 2, 3, 4.\n-They found the report very helpful and that the process was exactly what they expected to see. Report is thorough and and presents information in a manner where you can get more details about what you are looking for. In terms of the information quality the report is fair and correct. They were impressed with what analysts were able to obtain with what they had presented and that the meat of the issues were discussed.', '', '', '0', 0, '2017-09-01', '', ''),
(739, 776, 823, 4, 'Brian Switzer there contacted us', '2014-08-29', '2014-11-24', '2015-08-03', '5', '2051', '311812', '52175000', '170', '130000', 'Baked Goods', '52046000 lbs', '5616', '', '75', '13800', '12', '225', '105', '', '', '', '', 0, '0000-00-00', '', ''),
(740, 777, 431, 1, 'Website Form', '2014-10-09', '2014-12-16', '0000-00-00', '4', '2952', '324122', '100000000', '87', '100599', 'Asphalt Shingles', '1400000', '6240', '', '100', '', '', '200', '100', 'Outside vendor is coming in to analyze fan associated with AR No. 4. Likely to be implemented - will follow up in coming weeks to check if this will be implemented. \n\n\nFollow up on 8/19/2015 to get action plan for AR No. 4 (will probably changed to \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"implemented\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" status), try to refine/increase savings for replication no. 1, as well as spin off savings for recommendation no. 5 and 7.\n\nLeft voicemail and sent email on 6/24/2015. Will follow up on 6/26/2015 if no reply.\n\nPaul emailed some feedback on 8/3/2015. Looks like one or two more emails/phone calls needed to fill in some missing information before Rutger upload.', 'AR No. 1 seems like spinoff as well. we recommended maintaining cooling capacity but doing so more efficiently, they are taking steps to increase cooling capacity. \n\nAR No. 5 and 7 seem to be spin off - a large project to replace the current oil heaters in underway.\n\n\n', '2', '6091', 0, '2016-08-19', '', '1'),
(741, 779, 431, NULL, 'Website Form', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, '0000-00-00', NULL, ''),
(742, 781, 545, 4, '', '2015-07-30', '0000-00-00', '2017-01-04', '6', '2493', '321212', '184000000', '615', '476600', 'Hardwood and Softwood Plywood', '325422000', '8061', '4707', '600', '500000', '600', '350', '100', '', '', '', '351500', 0, '0000-00-00', '', ''),
(743, 782, 331, 1, 'Karl H.', '2014-10-21', '2015-01-13', '2015-04-01', '6', '3312', '331110', '', '350', '400000', 'Cast Steel', '', '3120', '6400', '250', '0', '0', '600', '95', 'In general, a really impressive report. The team did an outstanding job.\n\nPage 7 correction. Fans interlocked with equip - only run 20% to 60% of the time.', 'Demand Reduction - OMC implemented. Shifted all melting to swing and graveyard. Worth $30K a month ($360K annually).\n', '1.3', '', 0, '0000-00-00', '', ''),
(744, 778, 826, 1, '', '2014-11-14', '2015-02-16', '2016-01-20', '6', '3339', '331410', '60000000', '300', '130000', 'Titanium Castings', '1125686 lbs.', '7478', '1500', '250', '0', '0', '600', '100', '', '', '', '', 0, '0000-00-00', '', ''),
(745, 783, 832, 1, '', '2015-02-25', '2015-05-11', '2016-11-21', '5', '2051', '311812', '5000000', '300', '71200', 'Commercial Bakery', '1000000', '8712', '10000', '400', '13800', '12', '450', '100', 'Lots of opportunities with ETO to come and perform lighting analysis and other energy assessments following our report.', '', '0', '21727', 0, '0000-00-00', '', '0'),
(746, 784, 836, 1, 'Karl - Jeff Mason ', '2015-02-02', '2015-04-03', '2016-02-12', '7', '3398', '332811', '100 million (less than)', '50', '53000', 'Commercial heat treatment', '25 million lbs', '8760', '', '', '', '', '100', '120', 'after the OSU we did significant research on sub-metering, which is something we now plan to implement. WeÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢ve been delayed due to cost. We donÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢t want to rent sub-meters. We plan to purchase sub-meters that will integrate with new furnace utilization software. WeÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢re really excited about this.\n\nLED lighting in the new buildingÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â‚¬Âafter further research we were able to purchase LED lights for the new building. We were assisted my some energy incentives that made the upgrade from T5 to LEDÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s a net increase of $0. They are installed, and due to the sensors that were installed with the lights as well as some translucent panels that provide natural light, they rarely turn on during the daytime.\n\n ', '', '1', '', 0, '0000-00-00', '', '1');
INSERT INTO `Audits` (`AuditId`, `ProjectId`, `LocationId`, `AuditorId`, `LeadSource`, `AuditDate`, `ReportDate`, `ImplementationDate`, `StudentCount`, `SIC`, `NAICS`, `Sales`, `EmployeeCount`, `FacilityArea`, `KeyProduct`, `ProductionQuantity`, `FacilityHours`, `TotalMotorHP`, `MaxMotorHP`, `SteamCapacity`, `SteamPressure`, `AirCapacity`, `AirPressure`, `ImplementationComments`, `ImplementationSpinoff`, `SpinoffNumber`, `ImplementationSavings`, `Unavailable`, `FollowUpDate`, `ImplementationReplication`, `ReplicationNumber`) VALUES
(747, 785, 831, 1, '', '2015-01-27', '2015-04-28', '2016-05-05', '6', '2631', '322130', '400000000', '290', '4356000', 'Containerboard - Paper', '590000 swt.', '8592', '18000', '5000', '268263894.4', '850', '2450', '90', 'Facility appreciated having a new set of eyes on the process. They liked how we had a focus on electrical losses too. They thought that not having familiarity with the industry was a barrier and that they wish more recommendations came out of it.\n\nThey think its a great learning experience and would like to support the relationship. Our report was very thorough. Our headsets were great for communication and that our equipment we brought was very helpful for measurements. ', 'The facility is replacing the compressor with a more efficient compressor than recommended.\n\nThey are going to use more insulated bricks inside the lime kiln rather than insulating the exterior of the tank', '.3', 'NaN', 0, '0000-00-00', 'They have now started thinking about LED lighting and have gotten other sister plants on board to install them when other fixtures fail. Also, they have have had increased communication on their aeration basin with other facilities.', '.5'),
(748, 786, 831, 1, 'Tracie Tran', '2015-01-28', '2015-04-28', '2016-05-05', '6', '2631', '322130', '400000000', '290', '4356000', 'Containerboard manufacture', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'See Power and Fiber', 'Removing air blower agitiation process with more productive process.', '', '86870', 0, '0000-00-00', 'See Power and Fiber', ''),
(749, 787, 833, 1, 'Contacted us', '0000-00-00', '0000-00-00', '0000-00-00', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', NULL, '', 0, '0000-00-00', '', ''),
(750, 788, 821, 2, 'Kristina Kruger- PPL Medford area', '2015-06-29', '2015-11-16', '2016-07-22', '', '3861', '325992', '1000000', '350', '237000', 'X-Ray film', '50 million sq m rolls and 28 million sq m fin', '8760', '3314', '', '13000', '', '950', '', 'The assessment went okay. It gave them good information they can use when it comes to VFD\\\'s. They felt that combining the information from our assessment with information from a state level assessment really got them far.\n\nAs far as OMC\\\'s, they are working on getting a quote for installing an economizer on the boiler, but they are having trouble with it because they cannot tie it to the roof. ', 'They are implementing more VFD\\\'s in other spots than specified. ', '.2', '0', 0, '2018-07-22', '', ''),
(751, 789, 835, 4, 'Carley Lettero', '2015-04-16', '2015-07-16', '2016-04-21', '5', '4952', '221320', '8875000', '10', '830000', 'Treated Water', '71000000000 gal', '8760', '1371', '125', '0', '0', '50', '80', 'I think the process of getting another set of eyes on the plant allowed for our staff to revisit ideas that may have been shelved previously.  The items identified in this study are similar to others studies performed on the plant which can help support staff requests for larger capital upgrades. ', 'One thing that would be interesting and a potential improvement would be to engage other engineering students at OSU to generate solutions to opportunities identified such as OMC No. 5 in the report.  Staff had already identified (but not penciled out the potential savings or determined replacement equipment) all of the ARÃ¢â‚¬â„¢s except No. 3 prior to the assessment so identifying solutions for more complex issues such as dewatering solids to the digester would have had more value in our situation.  ', '1', '', 0, '0000-00-00', '', '0'),
(752, 790, 840, 1, '', '2015-04-20', '2015-06-26', '2016-04-25', '5', '3291', '327910', '55000000', '106', '126500', 'Abrasive Compounds', '3450 tons', '4160', '423', '', '', '', '315', '100', '', '', '1', '', 0, '2017-04-25', '', '1'),
(753, 791, 839, 4, '', '2015-05-13', '2015-07-24', '2017-01-10', '5', '3821', '334516', '17000000', '120-130', '50000', 'Laboratory Equipment', '5777', '8760', '255', '230', '0', '0', '25', '108', '', '', '', '', 0, '0000-00-00', 'They are now installing a much larger evaporator (approximately twice the cost) to deal with the acid wash as well as all rinse waters as well.\n\nThey also are looking into compressed air leaks after our recommendation to reduce Argon leaks', '2'),
(754, 792, 850, NULL, 'Diana Knous - PPL', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, '0000-00-00', NULL, ''),
(755, 793, 545, 4, '', '2015-07-27', '0000-00-00', '2017-01-04', '6', '2493', '321219', '65000000', '175', '750000', 'Particleboard', '148000000 sq. ft - 3/4\"', '6240', '10000', '600', '0', '0', '1550', '95', '', '', '', '', 0, '0000-00-00', '', ''),
(756, 794, 856, 1, '', '2015-07-01', '2015-09-24', '2016-04-29', '6', '2032', '311991', '10000000', '250', '220000', 'Soup', '72000000 lb', '5200', '732700', '300', '22300', '100', '200', '88-115', 'The report was very detailed. We did not take the time to prove or disprove all of the calculations, but it apparent the assessment was well thought out.\n\nÃƒÆ’Ã†â€™Ãƒâ€ Ã¢â‚¬â„¢ÃƒÆ’Ã¢â‚¬Â ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢ÃƒÆ’Ã†â€™Ãƒâ€šÃ‚Â¢ÃƒÆ’Ã‚Â¢ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã…Â¡Ãƒâ€šÃ‚Â¬ÃƒÆ’Ã¢â‚¬Â¦Ãƒâ€šÃ‚Â¡ÃƒÆ’Ã†â€™Ãƒâ€ Ã¢â‚¬â„¢ÃƒÆ’Ã‚Â¢ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â‚¬Å¡Ã‚Â¬Ãƒâ€¦Ã‚Â¡ÃƒÆ’Ã†â€™ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã…Â¡ÃƒÆ’Ã¢â‚¬Å¡Ãƒâ€šÃ‚Â·         Positive; The team engaged and listened to ideas and input from the plant. The assessment reinforced a couple of project ideas we had (Flash Steam Recovery, Thermosiphoning), and also did the diligence to disprove a couple of ideas (AGV lifts, Solar Panels)\n\nCritique; The time to get the report back seemed to take longer than originally communicated. This caused us to miss a budget planning cycle. At the end of the day, I donÃƒÆ’Ã†â€™Ãƒâ€ Ã¢â‚¬â„¢ÃƒÆ’Ã¢â‚¬Â ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢ÃƒÆ’Ã†â€™ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã…Â¡ÃƒÆ’Ã¢â‚¬Å¡Ãƒâ€šÃ‚Â¢ÃƒÆ’Ã†â€™Ãƒâ€ Ã¢â‚¬â„¢ÃƒÆ’Ã¢â‚¬Å¡Ãƒâ€šÃ‚Â¢ÃƒÆ’Ã†â€™Ãƒâ€šÃ‚Â¢ÃƒÆ’Ã‚Â¢ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã…Â¡Ãƒâ€šÃ‚Â¬ÃƒÆ’Ã¢â‚¬Â¦Ãƒâ€šÃ‚Â¡ÃƒÆ’Ã†â€™ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã…Â¡ÃƒÆ’Ã¢â‚¬Å¡Ãƒâ€šÃ‚Â¬ÃƒÆ’Ã†â€™Ãƒâ€ Ã¢â‚¬â„¢ÃƒÆ’Ã¢â‚¬Å¡Ãƒâ€šÃ‚Â¢ÃƒÆ’Ã†â€™Ãƒâ€šÃ‚Â¢ÃƒÆ’Ã‚Â¢ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã…Â¡Ãƒâ€šÃ‚Â¬ÃƒÆ’Ã¢â‚¬Â¦Ãƒâ€šÃ‚Â¾ÃƒÆ’Ã†â€™ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã…Â¡ÃƒÆ’Ã¢â‚¬Å¡Ãƒâ€šÃ‚Â¢t think it would have changed when we did the projects.\n\n', '', '1', '', 0, '2018-05-02', 'Finally, we did use the momentum of this visit to engage a 3rd party (via Campbells WHQ) to prepare a holistic energy conservation plan that directs the heat from the ammonia compressors to heat process water. The preliminary report is encouraging from an energy savings, water savings, and as a source for making/storing hot water for the process. The idea is currently tabled until we have the hot water demand to support the project.\n\n \nSo again, thank from us to your team for the time and diligence in analyzing the energy efficiency opportunities. We reference your material when assessing and developing our strategic capital plan and our Sustainability Plan.', '2'),
(757, 795, 859, 2, '', '2015-07-01', '2015-09-29', '2018-10-04', '6', '2033', '311421', '$50-70M', '76-150', '65340', 'Fruit Puree', '6.5 million', '6336', '2550', '200', '45455', '125', '200', '120', 'Listed in Rutgers as Non- Responsive', '', '', '', 0, '0000-00-00', '', ''),
(758, 796, 520, 2, 'Called them', '2015-06-30', '0000-00-00', '2016-04-29', '', '2064', '311340', '300000000', '1000', '1074000', 'Fruit and Candy', '5000000', '5000', '2060', '375', '23000', '160', '100', '125', '', '', '0', '', 0, '2018-04-29', '', '0'),
(759, 797, 501, 1, '', '2015-07-16', '0000-00-00', '2017-01-03', '6', '5143', '311511', '500000000', '350', '339010', 'Dairy Products', '10000000', '8760', '1500', '300', '1000', '125', '540', '100', 'As you can see, none of these are complete yet, so we canÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢t provide feedback about savings estimate accuracy.  My experience through 2 or 3 OSU audits is that the energy savings estimates are fairly accurate, while the investment estimates are usually significantly low.  This is somewhat understandable as good project estimates require a thorough understanding of the scope, and then a check on current market prices to get an accurate estimate.  As the primary goal of the audit is to identify the opportunities and determine how big they are, I do not see this fault as a major problem.  With opportunities defined, we can dig in further and more accurately determine the investment required.\n \nI value the work of the OSU EEC, and I can confidently say that the process has contributed to millions of dollars of savings for TCCA over the years.  I look forward to working with one of your teams again in the future', 'No spinoff', '1', '', 0, '2017-01-04', 'No replication.', '1'),
(760, 798, 860, 1, 'Jackson Wynne', '2015-06-30', '2015-09-23', '2016-08-19', '6', '2092', '424420', '0 (cost center)', '34', '28000', 'Packaged Seafood', '28000000 pounds per year', '7800', '1000', '200', '0', '0', '20', '88', 'The facility had recent personnel and management changes which impacted the implementation of these recommendations. This was the second time he has worked with us. It was a good study that gave him things to think about. He appreciated our help and effort. Everyone worked really hard, and Pavel went above and beyond. ', 'No spinoff. ', '0', '', 0, '2018-08-19', 'The Automated Tub Washing and the Photovoltaic Arrays are the replications from this report. They are being introduced to sister facilities within the company. ', '1.'),
