(169, 324, 1555, 2, 1, 9911, '2012-11-19', 'Asked about reprograming plastic heating controls. He have me the names of two men who could do it: Michael Grant (Pacific Measurement Controls, Seatle 425 -338-5706); Steve Powers (Powers Automation, Bend OR. *White pages)\n', NULL, 702, NULL),
(170, 324, 1556, 2, 1, 9911, '2012-11-20', 'asked about current heat controls. He suggested networking controllers.', NULL, 702, NULL),
(171, 324, 1557, 2, 1, 9911, '2012-11-20', 'Asked about reprograming PID controllers. He suggested turning on Fuzzy logic of Auto tune and collect input values per product per extruder.', NULL, 702, NULL),
(174, 306, 1453, 2, 1, 9692, '2012-11-21', 'Called to follow up on the draft I sent. Left a message because he didn\'t answer.', NULL, 689, NULL),
(177, 225, 1550, 2, 1, NULL, '2012-11-20', 'Call on 11/20/12\n\nSee video for process overview:\n\nEquipment\nCNC\n5 CNC punches\n12 CNC brake presses\n(?) CNC riveters\nCompressed Air: 75 HP VSD Sullair (\"runs at low and modulates\"). AIr is used for some pneumatic equipment, lubrication systems, and to clear powder (from 12 filters?) (in powder coat process - if so then a blower recommendation - but... they also have 10 HP blower?)\nPallatized wrapper\nLights: T8s amd T5s (they manufacture 1000 W MH)\nAir conditioning units on roof are old (Climacheck target?)\nBlower motors on powder coating equipment\nPowder Coat Ovens: New burner on one over. Other two are checked once a year (saftey or combustion efficiency ?) . They use a butterfly valve to adjust the combustion. Squirrel cage blower. Oven opening is 4 x 5 foot. Oven temp ~400 deg F.\nManual (electric?) pallet jacks, tote lifts and propane forklift\nNeed to keep a positive pressure in the shop. Vents in building (roof?) to balance the system.  \n\nBottleneck: speed of the powder coat system (feed?), or perhaps riveting to keep up with powder coat. \n\nWaste water off of powder coat - wash water 500 to 600 gallons dumped every other week. kept at 110 deg F. (Total waste water bills only in $6K range (annually?). Tank is way over sized. originally ran to heat water from 40 deg F to 140 deg F. Dropped to 110 deg F. (below 100 deg - tank foams)\n\nNo special safety gear: closed toe shoes and safety glasses.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(178, 225, 1553, 2, 1, NULL, '2012-11-27', 'Followed up again. Caught Shaun on the phone. Agreed to shoot  for early January. Sent preaudit letter and suggested Friday Jan 4. He is Ok with us inviting PPL (Alan Meyer)', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(179, 225, 1551, 2, 1, NULL, '2012-11-29', 'Following up to see if we could move forward on scheduling an assessment. ', 2, NULL, NULL),
(180, 225, 1551, 1, 1, NULL, '2012-11-19', 'Set up an assessment? (Date estimated)', 2, NULL, NULL),
(181, 225, 1551, 1, 1, NULL, '2012-07-09', 'Hi Misty,\n\nI left you voice mail today and I and sending this email in follow-up.\n\nI was calling to talk to you about our OSU Industrial Assessment Center program. We provide no-cost energy efficiency assessments to industrial facilities in the Northwest. Sam Walker at Clark Public Utilities suggested I contact you to see if you might have interest in having us come to your facility. We have been to your site twice in the past but the last time was in 2005 so I imagine that much has changed. \n\nMight there be an ideal time for me to call to discuss our program and a potential visit to Frito Lay?\n\nThanks - Joe Junker\n\nResponse: \n________________________________\nHi Joe,\n \nI would love for you and your team to complete an energy assessment of our facility as it is always beneficial to have that extra set of eyes to evaluate things.  Currently things are very busy and chaotic for us but should (hopefully) slow down over the next few weeks.  How does sometime in mid to late August sound? \n \nRegards,\n \nMisty Steele\nFaciliy/CapEX BUL\nFrito-Lay Vancouver\n360-737-3049\n ', 2, NULL, NULL),
(182, 225, 1551, 1, 1, NULL, '2012-08-01', 'A few emails and calls through rest of summer. First targeting August then moving back to October or later.', 2, NULL, NULL),
(183, 225, 1558, 2, 1, NULL, '2012-11-29', 'Talked to Kurt and send pre-audit doc.\n\nHe saw a copy of our sample report, provided by Doug Swier - Cowlitz. \n\n10 Employees\n\nMain Energy user: Autoclave (8 of them) 3-4 month process cycle (has insulation jacket around 100 tons of steel, electric heaters inside. Max temperature 360 deg F, different zones. The heat creates a convective current. May use seed natural quartz. \n\nProduce synthetic quartz. Used for electronics chips and SLR camera lenses\n\nApprox $30k a month in electricity cost. Some natural gas use.\n\nAny time could work as long as they are not opening one of the autoclaves.\n\nShoot for early January. ', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(184, 225, 1559, 2, 1, NULL, '2012-11-29', 'Talked to Jace and followed up with an email with the preaudit letter. 200 employees off season, 800 on season.\n\nLots of cost streams to look at: elect, nat gas, water, labor, etc.  Food conferences early January. Mid to late January likely good time. ', 27, NULL, NULL),
