(258, 225, 1606, 1, 1, NULL, '0000-00-00', 'Hi Joe, I heard about the program below and am wondering if you know of any service like this for industry in Skagit County Washington.\n .......â€\n \nThank you!\nRenee Westlund, CIH, CSP\nEHS Supervisor\nChemtrade Sulex Inc.\n13221 Farm to Market Road\nMount Vernon, WA 98273\nCell: (360) 610-3861\nPlant: (360) 424-5915\nrwestlund@chemtradelogistics.com\n ', 41, NULL, NULL),
(259, 225, 1606, 1, 1, NULL, '2013-04-01', 'Hi Renee,\n\nThanks for your interest. Our center does get as far North as you. We typically would make the trip over summer break. To leverage the travel cost, we work to identify a couple of facilities to visit on such a trip. If you are interested we could start the process and see if we can get you and some other plant(s) in your area lined up for this summer. \n\nI should note that to help ensure we can make enough impact with U.S.DOE\'s investment in us to serve you, one key criteria for us is that your annual energy costs are over at least $100,000 per year, and preferable over $200,000 per year.\n\nLet me know if you would like to move forward. I would be glad to work with you. \n\n- Joe Junker\n\n(By the way, I would be interested to hear how you learned of us - thanks)\n______________________________\nThatâ€™s great! We have a plant in Kalama WA and the Cowlitz County PUD encourages the use of the program. That is how I heard about you. Our natural gas usage is about 90K per year and our electricity is 50K. What is required of companies to use this service and are there any potential negative outcomes?\nThanks,\nRenee\n\n______________________________\nRenee,\n\nThe only requirement of the plant is to provide us information ahead of time, work with us on the day of the assessment, and provide any follow-up information we need to develop an analysis. No negative outcomes to date (since 1986). I am running out the door and will be back on Wed. If I am not able to before that, I will email you a letter outlining the process and the information we collect to do our work. If you are around on Wed I can give you a call too. \n\n- Joe\n______________________________\n\nOk, I will look forward to the letter outlining the process. Thanks!', 41, NULL, NULL),
(260, 225, 1607, 1, 1, NULL, '2013-03-25', 'Hi Joe\n \nI received information from Doug Swier about the Energy Efficiency testing you perform and believe we would like to sign up for a audit.  Please contact Steve Colwell our maintenance supervisor to make arrangements.  His phone number is 360-673-4503 or email: scolwell@chemtradelogistics.com.  \n \nThanks\nGloria Owen\nPlant Manager\nChemtrade Logistics\n404 Hendrickson Drive\nKalama,  WA  98625\n(360)-673-4503 plant\n(360)-673-4506 Fax\n(360)-431-4796 Cell', 43, NULL, NULL),
(261, 225, 1607, 1, 1, NULL, '2013-04-01', 'Steve, Gloria,\n\nWe would be glad to arrange an assessment with you! Sorry not to get back to you sooner. I have been traveling for the last week and my laptop died. When I get back into the office this Wed, I will give you a call. \n\nThanks - Joe Junker', 43, NULL, NULL),
