(363, 225, 1654, 1, 1, NULL, '2013-06-27', 'Good morning Dr. Wheeler and Dr. Junker,\n \nI am the environmental coordinator for Roseburg Forest Products veneer mill in Weed, CA.  We are subject to the area source boiler MACT rule and will need to perform an energy assessment as part of our compliance.  Iâ€™m wondering if the IAC or the EEC group at Oregon State would be available to perform an assessment of our facility.  Please let me know if either group would be interested in performing the assessment.  If you have any questions please give me a call at 530-938-5735.  Thank you.\n \nScott Dunn\nEnvironmental Coordinator\nPly # 7\nWeed, CA\nPhone: (530) 938-5735\nCell: (541) 430-0202\n ', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(364, 225, 1654, 1, 1, NULL, '2013-06-28', 'Hi Scott, \n\nThanks for your interest. I think that one way or the other we should be able to help you out:\nAs you are in California and equidistant from us and the San Francisco State University I am checking to see if they want to serve you. I should defer to them if so.\nHowever I am currently working on dialing in a trip to serve a facility in White City Oregon this August. That would put us within 1-1/2 hours of you so if SFSU defers, I think it might work for us to visit. \nI am copying the SFSU Director, Dr. Ahmad Ganji on this email. I called yesterday and it sounded like he might not be available to respond until next week. \n\nThanks - Joe\n', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(365, 225, 1654, 1, 1, NULL, '2013-06-28', 'Hi Joe,\n \nThat will work for me.  I worked for OSUâ€™s IAC while I went to school, so I figured I would contact you guys first.  Thanks\n \nScott\n\n\nAhh - yes you did back in 2000. I knew your name was familiar. Well we have been to a number of RFP sites in Oregon, so I would enjoy getting down to work with you. We will have to see what Ahmad says. I owe him the courtesy to decide if he wants to serve you but it would be far for him to go compared to the little extra distance we would travel. \n\nHopefully we will be able to sort it out next week. \n', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(366, 225, 1654, 1, 1, NULL, '2013-07-02', 'Hi Scott,\n\nWe heard from Dr. Ganji at the SF IAC (I think he copied you). Sounds like we can plan to visit you in August. I would like to target Monday, Tuesday, or Wednesday the week of August 12th for our team to spend a day at your site.\n\nI\'ve attached our pre-audit letter. It outlines our assessment process and what we need to collect to best prepare for an assessment. (I expect it will sound familiar to you after your time here at the center). The critical things to return so we can get things started are the:\nIndustrial Pre-Assessment Form (that includes eligibility and logistic information)\nUtility Release (so we can collect a one year month-to-month profile of your energy use and utility expenses)\nThe letter also includes a list of additional helpful preparatory information. While they are not required, they are helpful and can greatly improve the job we are able to do for you. Please call me if you have any questions. Once you return 1 & 2 above, we can get started preparing for the assessment. I look forward to hearing from you. \n\nThanks!\n\n-Joe Junker.\n\n(You might also want to visit our web-site to find out more about our how our program has developed since you were here: http://eec.engr.oregonstate.edu/)\n', NULL, NULL, NULL),
