(446, 310, 1630, 2, 1, 10920, '2013-08-26', 'Called Kendall and left a message in reference to the email I sent last week requesting data.', 46, 755, NULL),
(447, 310, 1630, 1, 1, 10920, '2013-08-20', 'Hi Kendall,\n\nI am following up on Joe Junker\'s previous email concerning the Pre-Assessment Letter that he sent you.  I am coordinating the baseline for your assessment, which includes analyzing your facility\'s utility bills.  In order to do this I need the utility release permission form (included in the Pre-Assessment Letter) to be filled out, signed, and either faxed or scanned and emailed back.\n\nPlease fill out the letter and email the final copy back to me or fax it to us at (541) 737-5035 so that we can begin the analysis of your utilities.  I have attached the letter below for your convenience.\n\nThank you,', 46, 755, NULL),
(448, 310, 436, 1, 1, 10922, '2013-08-21', 'Hi Jack,\n\nI\'m collecting the necessary data for the utility analysis we will be preparing for your report.  I have received all of the Excel spreadsheets and other information you passed on to Joe Junker back in May, but to complete our analysis I will need a bit more information.\n\nI need your 2013 use history for Electric, Natural Gas, and Water utilities as well as a copy of the most recent bills for each of them.  This will help us to understand exactly how your facility is charged so we can accurately estimate future costs and savings.\n\nI realize collecting all that information can take a lot of time, so if you prefer you can just fill out and sign the Utility Release Permission form and I will take care of all the data collection we need.  The Utility Release Permission form is attached below and you can either scan and email the completed form back to me or fax it to us at (541) 737-5035.\n\nThank you!', 50, 754, NULL),
(449, 310, 436, 2, 1, NULL, '2013-08-26', 'Called and left a message in reference to the email I sent last week and requested his reply to it.', 50, NULL, NULL),
(450, 310, 436, 1, 1, NULL, '2013-08-26', 'Jack replied with the 2013 use history but still need more info.\n\nJack,\n\nThanks for sending me the 2013 file!  That will be a great help but I will need just a bit more information from you if possible.  Would you be able to send me copies of your most recent bills for electricity, natural gas, and water?  I need the breakdown of the rate schedules your facility is on and the bills should have everything else that I will need.\n\nThank you,', 50, NULL, NULL),
(451, 310, 1618, 1, 1, 10423, '2013-08-29', 'Hi Aimee and Joe,\n \nI am looking at AR No. 7 from Plant 1 and was wondering who you had quote the control system and if you have a copy of the quote. If you have a copy of the quote or the vendor information could you shoot it to me in an email?\n \nThanks,\nJames Brown\n\nHi James,\n\nUnfortunately I do not have an actual vendor quote to pass on to you, but I am linking the case studies used in the recommendation in hope that they will be useful for you.  The implementation cost in AR No. 7 for Plant 1 is based off of this case study by the U.S. Dairy Sustainability Commitment.  The analyst scaled the investment cost stated in the case study by comparing your refrigeration system\'s total horsepower to that in the case study and used the ratio to downsize the investment for your plant.  Here\'s the equation: 3,450 hp/5,000 hp = 0.69 * $466,000 = $321,540 implementation cost.  A second case study conducted by Emerson Climate Technologies was also used in this recommendation for estimating the possible percent energy savings.\n\nIf you have any more questions please let me know and I will do my best to answer them.  I\'m happy to hear that you\'re finding the report helpful!\n\nThank you,', NULL, 733, NULL),
(452, 315, 1630, 2, 1, 11018, '2013-08-29', 'Called Kendall to check on status of Utility Release form. He said that he has received it via Aimee\'s email, but hasn\'t had a chance to complete it. He said that he will complete it this afternoon.', 46, 755, NULL),
(453, 310, 1558, 1, 1, 10228, '2013-09-03', 'Kurt,\n\nSorry for the long delay in getting this addendum recommendation to you.  Attached is the complete work up for the heat pump opportunity, we hope that it comes in handy for your plants in Japan.  If you have any more questions regarding this opportunity, please feel free to send them my way.\n\nI have sent the PDF of your report off to printing and will have the hard copies sent to you within the next few weeks.\n\nThank you for your patience.', NULL, 715, NULL),
(454, 334, 1654, 1, 1, 10850, '2013-09-04', 'Colleen,\n \nHere is some of your information requested:\n \nVeneer Produced:  134,175 msf Dry\n                                       218504 msf Green\n6,800 hours/year operating in 2012 going to 8,400 hours/year next year\nSteam Capacity: 130,000 lbs/hr\nSteam Pressure: 625 psi (Superheated)\nAir Compressor HP: 300 hp; 150 hp\n \nThe steam production data is attached for Benjamin\n \nFor Brad M:  Clipper hydraulics hours will be the same as production\n \nFor you Iâ€™ve attached power invoices and a map\n \nIâ€™ll pass along more information as it comes available.\n \nScott\n ', NULL, 749, NULL),
(455, 225, 1630, 2, 1, 11018, '2013-09-04', 'Kendall called to say his boss wants to cancel our visit. Evidently ETO (Chritine?) included them in a \"Core Initiative\" and his boss feels that our work would be duplicative and put too much on their staff\'s plate. He was going to a meeting today and will see if her mind can  be changed', 46, 755, NULL),
