(490, 0, 55, 2, 1, 11053, '0000-00-00', 'Called Scott to verify that it\'s ok to talk to Hallie at Pacific Power regarding our recommendations to see about custom incentives that may apply to RFP. Scott said it was fine to talk to Pacific Power about the in process report.', NULL, 749, NULL),
(528, 332, 1666, 1, 0, 10673, '2013-07-17', 'Josh,\n \nFollowing our phone conversation yesterday, here is info for the fan in Sumner WA.  The unit was a Twin City size 490 BC-SW, Class 3 wheel. It is the exact same fan as our CB, and I have attached the curve for the CB-SW. I have also attached a curve for a CBA-SW airfoil.\n \nAs you can see, the CBA needs to run faster. The original unit shipped less motor & drives, so I do not have any info on the drive selection they used, so they will need to change either the fan sheave or the motor sheave to get the increased speed required.\n \nHere is my quote per your request for the new wheel:\nSize 490 CBA-SW Steel Wheel, Class 3 construction, CW Rotation, with a  bore, coated with Air Dry Epoxy:\nPRICE EACH: $ 7,353.00         (approx. 510 lbs)\nStandard lead time is approx. 4 weeks.', NULL, 739, NULL),
(529, 0, 1030, 1, 0, -1, '2013-10-07', 'Jack Higgins, the main contact, will be gone on vacation 10/25/2013 and is not sure when he will return. He confirmed today this Friday, the 11th, will work for the audit. Analysts have confirmed they can audit this Friday, and we will have pre audit call at 2:15 pm today.', NULL, 754, NULL),
(530, 310, 1690, 2, 0, -1, '2013-10-07', 'Called and left a message with Neal asking him to call back so we can go over the implementation calls or to direct me to the correct contact to speak with.', NULL, -1, NULL),
(531, 321, 1703, 2, 0, NULL, '2013-09-30', 'Contacted Paul Cook who is a manager at Ninkasi in Eugene. He informed me that they would be interested in an energy assessment this year or beginning of next. They just expanded  their production facility so it would be a winter or spring term assessment. Pre-assessment package is with them and we are waiting for it back. Will contact again at the end of term.', NULL, -1, NULL),
(532, 0, 783, 2, 0, NULL, '0000-00-00', '(Brad)called and left voicemail about scheduling a fall assessment.', NULL, -1, NULL),
(533, 315, 783, 2, 0, NULL, '2013-09-26', '(Brad) called and left voicemail about scheduling a fall assessment.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(535, 310, 1670, 2, 0, 11001, '2013-10-08', 'Spoke with Dathan and completed implementation report for 571. Possible assessments desired at other plants in Oregon and Idaho.', NULL, 757, NULL),
(537, 310, 1705, 2, 0, 11001, '2013-10-09', 'Called Dennis and left a message for implementation tracking.', NULL, 757, NULL),
(538, 310, 1685, 2, 0, 11001, '2013-10-09', 'Called Cole at facility number and left a message.', NULL, 757, NULL),
(540, 315, 1619, 2, 0, 9190, '2013-10-09', 'Ann called to discuss confidentiality concerns and our process. She has forwarded pre-assessment packages to each of the three facilities that we plan to visit (Wilsonville; Portland; and Bellvue, WA). She told them to send those back to me directly by next Friday (10/18).', NULL, 662, NULL),
(541, 325, 783, 2, 0, NULL, '2013-10-10', 'Yes, interested. They are seasonal but November should work fine. Initial opportunities mentioned include water jacket heat recovery and fully condensing exchanger to heat green houses. Mentioned that anaerobic digester bio-gas production fluctuates regularly enough that each month energy is both purchased and sold back to utility. Bill is ready to schedule whenever we are and is awaiting audit dates from us.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(542, 0, 1701, 1, 1, NULL, '2013-10-10', 'Josh responded to my email to ask about the status of our assessment schedule and what we typically focus on at waste facilities. I responded to his email.\n', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(544, 0, 1698, 2, 0, 9190, '2013-10-10', 'Called Lisa to tell her that we are not able to assess GreenFlex and she asked me to email her and CC the company president, so I did.', NULL, 662, NULL),
(558, 310, 1373, 2, 0, 11001, '2013-10-11', 'Called Tim Frazier about Boise Cascade Plants and got an answering machine for Cole (who I\'m assuming to be Cole Winegar) and left a message for him to call me back about feedback on the report.', NULL, 757, 642),
(559, 310, 1549, 2, 0, 11001, '2013-10-11', 'Called Mark and left a message about getting back to me with feedback for the Neil Jones Company report.', NULL, 757, 646),
(560, 310, 1404, 2, 0, 11001, '2013-10-11', 'Called Jerry and left a message.  Know that he was waiting on energy specialist to finish the information on the recommendations but not sure who that is.', NULL, 757, 650),
(561, 325, 783, 1, 0, 11051, '2013-10-14', 'Just emailed Bill and connected him with Brad.  He is awaiting audit date scheduling and pre-audit paper work.', NULL, 758, NULL),
(562, 315, 783, 1, 0, 11051, '2013-10-14', 'Emailed Bill to attempt to set a date for the visit and sent pre-assessment package.', NULL, 758, NULL),
(563, 315, 783, 2, 0, 11051, '2013-10-15', 'Called Bill. Set visit date for November 7th. Will email him with a proposed time for a pre-assessment phone call. He asked what the scope of our assessment will be since Stahlbush has farms in Corvalls, Eugene, and Medford areas.', NULL, 758, 31),
(564, 333, 1639, 1, 0, 11075, '2013-10-02', 'David,\n My name is Scott Lindbloom and I am the lead analyst for the upcoming energy assessment at API. As part of our pre-assessment process, we typically set up a phone call with the facility, Joe Junker, and the lead. During this call, we discuss the processes our team will encounter when we arrive on the 14th and any specific areas of focus you\'d like us to look in to. This information helps us direct our pre-assessment research and what equipment to bring.\n Could we schedule a phone call for next week? Our schedule is open Monday through Wednesday after 2 pm. \n Thanks for your time,\n Scott Lindbloom ', NULL, 756, 764),
(565, 333, 1639, 1, 0, 11084, '2013-10-15', 'Hi David, \n Thanks for your time yesterday during our site visit, and for allowing us to use Craig\'s time to install data loggers. I\'ve attached one more document, which I forgot to bring along yesterday. This information release outlines who you would prefer to receive copies of the report, as well as whether you would prefer us to use API\'s name if we contact any vendors for quotes. If you could fill this out and return it we\'d appreciate it. \n Just to confirm our plan for the data loggers installed on your equipment, there are eight of them which started recording amperage and run times beginning at five AM today. They will record for one week. They can be removed anytime after five AM 10/22. We left a Pelican case to use for shipping them back to us. There are current transducers plugged into seven of the loggers. Their locations are listed below:\n #8 is installed (magnetic) on motor case of the chip conveyor on MV-4 (no transducer attached)\n#10 is installed inside the cabinet of the NH-6300 - 2 horizontal mill at the cell\n#11 is installed in the service disconnect box for the Quincy air compressor\n#13 is installed inside the control cabinet for the paint sure oven\n#17B is installed in the service disconnect (on roof) for the paint booth recirculation fan\n#18B is installed in the service disconnect for the dust collection fan in the debur area\n#19B is installed in the service disconnect for the dust collection fan in the saw area\n#21 is installed in the control cabinet of the NMH-6300 - 5 horizontal mill at the cell\n\nWithin a week, I\'ll send over a trip report which outlines the potential opportunities we will be pursuing. \n\nThanks,\nScott Lindbloom\nOSU Energy Efficiency Center\n', NULL, 756, 764),
