(629, 333, 1639, 1, 0, 11155, '2013-11-22', 'Hi David,\n While I was analyzing the data logs we collected from the air compressor, I noticed some issues with the operation that I thought I should bring to your attention right away. It appears that during times where the system demand is low (between shifts), that the compressor does not fully unload. It appears to be short cycling, starting to unload and then the system calls for air and it switches back to load again. Given your facility\'s receiver capacity, we would expect to see a gradual turndown to about 25% of full power followed by a 45 second unloading process, and then several minutes of operation unloaded, around 5% of full power. I\'ve talked to several other analysts here and a representative from Rogers in Portland. While we\'re not sure what is causing this, it seems like a good idea to investigate it further.\n Attached is a sample of the short cycling we observed. \n \nThanks, ', NULL, 756, NULL),
