(634, 331, 1665, 2, 0, NULL, '2013-07-10', 'Grid powered mechanical aerators to replace 105 hp of motor aeration. This aeration method will use a much smaller motor ~5 hp. Specific mixer was chosen based on wastewater specifications and flow. ', NULL, -1, NULL),
(635, 331, 1721, 1, 0, 10662, '2013-07-15', 'EMAIL from Chris: \nThanks for reaching out to us regarding a dissolved air flotation system for a fish processing facility. The flow rates youÃ¢â‚¬â„¢ve specified fall right in line with what our V-408 DAF system was designed for. These systems start right around $75,000 and vary with included ancillary support systems, i.e. chemical feeders, flocculation tubes, feed pumps, sludge dewatering equipment, etc.\n \nInfluent parameters will be required to determine final sizing of the system, especially if TSS loadings are higher than 1400 mg/L. ItÃ¢â‚¬â„¢s always an absolute must to get a water analysis performed before going ahead with a capital equipment purchase of this nature. You only buy a system once, gotta make sure to get it right the first time.\nFor wastewater from a fish processing facility, IÃ¢â‚¬â„¢d expect to use some sort of ferric-based coagulant and a liquid polymer. pH adjusting reagents should also be available. Chemicals can be selected through jar testing and costs can be estimated based on % solution and dosing rate.  \n \nOur V-408 DAF system has 8.5HP installed on the unit. 7.5HP for the pump, 0.5HP on the Scraper Drive, and 0.5HP on the Auger Drive. 480V 60Hz 3-Phase electrical required.', NULL, 741, NULL),
