(664, 332, 436, 1, 0, -1, '2014-01-02', 'Jack\'s feedback from client review: <br><br>Josh, I have briefly reviewed the recommendations in the draft report.  The report is thorough and contains a lot of useful information.  All of the recommendations will be reviewed and considered based on their individual costs and merits.  We eagerly look forward to receiving the completed report. AR No. 1, Upgrade Air Compressor Controls, contains one error.  The mills fire sprinkler system consists of 18 risers or separate systems.Of the 18, only 9 are dry systems requiring pressurization at 40 psi with compressed air.  Air is supplied to each riser from the mills compressed air system, i.e. the 100 hp Gardner Denver.  There is no dedicated air compressor for the fire system. AR No. 2, Shut off Exhaust Fans, has been discussed previously and will be easy to implement. AR No. 3, Flash Steam Recovery, has a good return and makes sense.  It may require replacing some or all of the existing condensate receivers. AR No. 4, Upgrade Lighting, is in progress.  We have signed a letter of agreement with Clark PUD to complete the exterior lighting conversion to LED by 4/1/14.  We have also considered motion controls for the Dyehouse basement in the past and will probable go ahead.  It will require reconfiguring the existing lighting circuit layout. The Other Measures Considered, are food for thought and may fit in with long term planning such as replacing the continuous washer in Finish with a more water efficient process.', NULL, 754, 131),
(665, 225, 1404, 1, 0, -1, '2014-01-07', 'Handed it off - what did we do - lighting no diesel - shut off timer - expanded to other bases. Put into capital program for funding. Able to use report for long term  Will work to get that information to us. ', NULL, -1, 650),
