(712, 332, 1722, 1, 0, 11236, '2014-03-12', 'Hi Robert, <br><br>I have a couple of questions regarding the proposed compartment house anox system, and the heat exchanger bypass. The two main bits of information I need are:<br><br>For the proposed compartment house anox system, what would be the expected annual maintenance cost?<br>For the bypass heat exchanger analysis, I have 12 in/h20 across the fan. However, what is the delta P across the heat exchanger? If you have this data for both compartment and flex that would be preferable, if you think they\'re similar one would be ok.<br><br>Updates on analysis for these two subjects:<br><br>Heat exchanger bypass: I expect a savings maximum limit of $4,700/yr with the combined savings of both bypasses. This is based on national weather bin data analysis, showing that 6.8% of the year is above 75 F, the threshold point. The savings will only go down based on the delta P across the heat exchanger, Possible not the most promising analysis here.<br><br>Proposed anox system for compartment house: The trickiest part here is coming up with a number for the boiler line losses. Since they were underground we can only surmise. Due to the age of the system, large physical distances, and voiced doubts of the efficiency, I am using a possible aggressive 10% line loss estimate. This puts fuel savings at 43,200 MMBtu/yr, and combining this with maintenance savings I estimate $710,000 annual savings. This number will also go down once I factor in maintenance costs of the new system.<br>Additionally, I am using an annual current fuel use of 5032 therms/day for the boiler that I was quoted during the assessment. This was based on a 77 day average. I\'m not sure if you have more refined numbers for the boiler annual fuel use?<br><br>Just thought I\'d let you know how these two recommendations were coming. Please let me know your thoughts. I need further data on the two bullet points to proceed.<br><br>Much thanks!<br>-Josh Mutch', NULL, 760, 494),
(713, 332, 1722, 1, 0, -1, '2014-03-12', '\"Please ensure that Ken Weaver and Robert Seggewiss are included on the correspondence.\"', NULL, 760, 494),
