(780, 225, 1765, 1, 0, NULL, '2014-07-01', 'Trident Seafoods : Jeff Thompson (Johnson)Alaska Plant - 15 - 50 Million energy costs a year. Kodiak Plants in August. Would need to determine how to pay. Would check with George Roe (?) in Alaska State gov? and Trident? To see if we could serve them.  I will:Check with Rutgers/U.S.DOETouch base with John GardenerRough out travel costs (hours?)Told him I was buried and it might take a week to close the loop. ', NULL, -1, 822),
(781, 333, 1744, 1, 0, 11474, '2014-07-02', 'Hi Julia,  Thank you for the opportunity to visit your plant last week. Our team was very impressed by CBA\'s energy management. Attached is a trip report which briefly summarizes our assessment and the possible opportunities that we have identified for recommendation. If you have any questions or concerns about the trip report, please feel free to email me.  In order to begin our recommendation process, the team will need the following information if possible:1. Water and waste water bills for the last year.2. Could we see the Cambrian Innovations proposal when you receive it?3. Are there other waste water treatment vendors or technologies that CBA is pursuing? 4. Is the \"Logged Boiler Data\" spreadsheet part of a report? If so, can we see it or contact the report author? 5. Does the facility have the original specifications for the water heater that is a candidate for replacement?6. As part of our analysis of the ammonia refrigeration system, we could send a data logger connected to a humidity sensor to be placed in the vicinity of the condenser. We would be interested in knowing if the hot moist air from the kettle stacks may settle into the roof valley where the condenser is located. Is this of interest to you? Thanks for your help, ', NULL, 770, 813),
(782, 325, 1652, 2, 0, -1, '2014-07-03', 'Just contacted Phil Thompson at PNWB and apparently our original primary contact, Phil Pokorny no longer works at PNWB.  Our report had fallen to the wayside but Phil is going to review it in preparation for a follow-up call 7/16/2014 at 10 a.m.', NULL, -1, 763),
