(815, 225, 1772, 1, 0, NULL, '2014-07-09', 'Sent web form in requesting audit: First Name: PaulLast Name: CourtoisTitle/Relation to Company: Plant LeaderEmail: paul.courtois@owenscorning.comCompany Name: Owens CorningTelephone: 503.273.1401Fax: 419.325.9777Street Address: 3750 NW Yeon AveCity: PortlandState: ORZip Code: 97210-1322PO Box:City :State:Zip Code:Industry: Building MaterialsMajor Products: Asphalt ShinglesProblem you would like investigated: Would like to discuss conducting energyassessment to identify opportunities to reduce energy intensity through bestpractices and capital investment.', NULL, -1, 431),
(816, 225, 1774, 1, 0, NULL, '2014-08-19', 'Sent in Web form: First Name: GregLast Name: SladcikTitle/Relation to Company: Facilities ManagerEmail: gregs@selmetinc.comCompany Name: Selmet, IncTelephone: 541-917-8331Fax: 541-917-7419Street Address: 33992 SE Seven Mile LnCity: AlbanyState: ORZip Code: 97322PO Box: PO Box 689City : AlbanyState: ORZip Code: 97321Industry: Titanium FOundryMajor Products: Jet Aircraft ComponentsProblem you would like investigated: Recently joined the DOE \"Better Plants\"program and committed to reducing energy usage by 25% over the next 10 years.Would like an energy assessment conducted to help identify conservationopportunities.', NULL, -1, 826),
(817, 225, 1774, 1, 0, NULL, '2014-08-20', 'Called Greg and LVM - be glad to work with you to set up an audit.', NULL, -1, 826),
(818, 225, 1772, 1, 0, NULL, '2014-08-21', 'He called and LVM with his Cell phone number. I called back. Agreed to send Pre-Audit Doc. Targeting Fall Audit. Uses french proununciation: Cor - twa', NULL, -1, 431),
(819, 225, 1774, 1, 0, NULL, '2014-08-21', 'Greg Called back and LVM. Called again and got me. Would like to have us audit them. They have 130K sq ft facility, 300 Employees. use 25 to 40 K Therms a month, 366 K therms a year. 14.3 MW (hrs?) a year. Fall a good time. They just upgraded their lights (did not get into detail) and compressed air system (reducing on hours and going to VSD trim controlled compressor with 2nd baseload compressor at full capacity when needed. Purchase their electricity from CPI (consumers power?) and used ESI money for energy projects. Agreed to send Pre- Audit doc.', NULL, -1, 826),
(820, 225, 1772, 1, 0, NULL, '2014-08-29', 'Courtois, PaulAttachments 10:36 AM (2 hours ago)to Mike, Frank, Kenneth, John, Carl, Karl, David, Melissa, Keith, me, OSU Thanks Joe,I have attached a spreadsheet with key contacts, energy usage-billing for past two years and 2013 waste streams. We look forward to working with you on this assessment. Please feel free to reach out to any of the contacts listed.Thanks, Paul  Paul A. CourtoisPortland Site Leader503.273.1401 Office303.489.8647 Cellpaul.courtois@owenscorning.com  ', NULL, -1, 431),
(821, 225, 1772, 1, 0, NULL, '2014-08-29', 'Joseph F. Junker <joseph.f.junker@gmail.com>12:40 PM (2 minutes ago)to Tracie, Paul, OSU, Mike, Frank, Kenneth, John, Carl, Karl, David, Melissa, Keith Thanks Paul,We will get started on our preparatory work. I think we agreed to shoot for a visit after October 1. We are just sorting out fall schedules, once we know our best dates to field an audit team we will get back to you with some proposed dates. Looking forward to working with you.- Joe', NULL, -1, 431),
(822, 225, 473, 1, 0, NULL, '2014-08-29', 'Touching base regarding fall audit.Also wanted to get your insights on Mike Gilbert and Regenergy365Bruce called back. Willing to go with fall audit. Was unsure what he needed to send. Supports the Regenergy folks. OK to have them demonstrate their system while we are there on the audit.  ', NULL, -1, 331),
(823, 334, 1641, 2, 0, 11552, '2014-09-02', 'Called and left a voice mail for Mike Fisher requesting information about Shining Ocean\'s implementation of our recommendations. Followed up with email outlining the information we need for our implementation report, and an email with an attached pdf of the Shining Ocean Assessment Report.', NULL, 757, 751),
(824, 225, 1774, 1, 0, NULL, '2014-09-11', 'Hi Greg,I thought I would touch base again. I am looking to get my fall schedule set. Do you think you will be ready by then.? Let me know if you have questions.Thanks - Joe Junker', NULL, -1, 826),
(827, 332, 1772, 1, 0, -1, '2014-09-22', 'Hi Paul,My name is Josh Mutch and I\'ll be the team lead for the upcoming assessment on October 9th. I\'d like to set up a pre-assessment phone walk-through to discuss logistics and also get a heads up for what kind of processes to be prepared for on assessment day.<br>During this phone call our department head Joe Junker and myself will be attending on our end. We welcome you to invite anyone on your end who may be helpful for the phone call.I\'d like to propose Wednesday, October 1st, at 2pm for the phone call. If this time doesn\'t work for you we can do a later time on that day, otherwise we can set up another day. Thanks,Josh Mutch', NULL, 777, 431),
(828, 332, 1732, 1, 0, -1, '2014-09-22', 'Sent another draft to Lisa for approval.', NULL, 764, 812),
(830, 334, 336, 2, 0, 11552, '2014-09-24', 'Left a voice mail for Benji reminding him of the implementation report information we need.', NULL, 757, 528),
(831, 334, 1622, 1, 0, 11552, '2014-09-25', 'Sent initial email to Bill James to begin implementation report. Will call to follow up in a week.', NULL, 757, 761),
(832, 334, 336, 1, 0, 11552, '2014-09-30', 'Colleen, Here is an update on the recommendations 1-8:1.     Process in place (Assumption provided by OSU is high)2.     Purchase of compressor is in the progress.3.     Controls only to be implemented4.     Same as #1.5.     Done6.     Purchasing capacitors in 6 month intervals for identified applications7.     Not at this time8.     Evaluating and better understanding incentive options The analysis and focus has been good. We are considering projects mostly with a 1 year or less payback. We have shared the learnings across the organization. This facility is currently working with the Energy Trust of Oregon to better understand and implement energy savings to this facility and others. Thank you and your team for your time and efforts. Feel free to contact Rob Patrick rpatrick@woodgrain.com or myself for anything regarding this project. Kind regards, Benjamin S. Barron', NULL, 757, 528),
(833, 225, 1749, 1, 0, -1, '2014-10-01', 'Calling to see:1- What you thought of the report2- If there is any follow on work we could do with you3- If by chance there are any impacts to include in our Semi Annual report to EPA.', NULL, 772, 818),
(834, 225, 1783, 2, 0, NULL, '2014-10-08', 'Calling in followup to web request for assessemnt', NULL, -1, NULL),
(835, 225, 1783, 2, 0, NULL, '2014-10-08', 'Calling in response to web request for an assessment - followed up with an email - (no way to leave message)', NULL, -1, 828),
(836, 332, 1772, 1, 0, -1, '2014-10-15', 'Sent initial email asking our questions after the debrief meeting. cced Carroll and Carl.', NULL, 777, 431),
(837, 341, 1622, 2, 0, 11106, '2014-10-24', 'Called phone but was directed to another person voice mailbox. Left a voicemail. Sent email to Bill James but it was returned (probably not in directory and working for facility). Will send email to Jason Femrite.', NULL, 215, 761),
(838, 341, 1663, 1, 0, 11106, '2014-10-24', 'Sent email. Will follow up in a week.', NULL, 215, 761),
(839, 332, 1772, 1, 0, -1, '2014-10-27', 'Called Paul. Got forklift vendor contact info, gave questions about compressed air and air ducts.', NULL, 777, 431),
(843, 334, 1664, 1, 0, 11552, '2014-08-14', 'Colleen,I am on vacation tomorrow and next week, but will follow up with you when I get back.  Larry Morrison, who was involved also, and myself will give you a call.  Thanks.--Jeff Bollen', NULL, 757, 754),
(844, 334, 1664, 1, 0, -1, '2014-09-02', 'Jeff,I am just checking in to find out if you are back from vacation, and if you would be able to look into getting the information for my implementation report sometime this week. Give me a call if you have any questions, or just email me the implementation information when you have a chance. Thank you,Colleen Johnson', NULL, -1, 754),
(845, 334, 1664, 2, 0, 11552, '2014-10-27', 'Left Jeff Bollen a voice mail requesting Implementation Information and reminding him of the emails I sent. ', NULL, 757, 754),
(846, 334, 1664, 1, 0, 11552, '2014-11-03', 'Re-sent the email template with the AR list and implementation questions.', NULL, 757, 754),
(847, 332, 1772, 1, 0, -1, '2014-11-07', 'Called and left message, then followed up with this email.Hi Paul,Just left a message for you. As it stands right now, I have some updates and a few questions.Updates - Fans and compressed airWe obtained the gear ratio on DCS #3 fan from Phelps Fan LLC, so please don\'t worry about finding that data point. The fan blade in that system appears to have worn down - it is not operating at along its original fan curve. It is 20 years old, perhaps time to replace it.Analyzing the weekend data on the VFD compressor, there appears to be a large leak load of about ~55% of maximum air demand. We think it\'s feasible for a facility such as yours to operate at 20-30% leak loads.Questions - Forklifts, fiberglass, and backup compressorHow much propane do the forklifts use monthly? We were provided data that showed they used ~$10,000 worth of propane, but we don\'t have propane bills to calculate the actual energy use.Where do you purchase raw fiberglass? This will help us track down possible recyclers.Nameplate information on backup 75 hp compressor. Sullair was unable to provide this data.Thanks for the help! Let me know if any of the questions were confusing.', NULL, 777, 431),
(848, 321, 1783, 1, 1, NULL, '2014-12-02', 'Sent information about our assessments and the pre-assessment form to Seth Crass. He responded letting me know his VP of operations approved. He said he would fill out the forms and consider January dates when he was done. Follow up with a call next week.', 103, -1, NULL),
(873, 332, 1797, 1, 0, 11708, '2014-11-06', 'Emailed Mike, got a $25,000 quote for installing battery stations through an email.', NULL, 777, NULL),
(874, 225, 1792, 2, 0, 11740, '2014-11-21', 'Following up on coversation you had with my grad student. Sounds like you had an unsatisfactory experience with the center in the past. Wanted to find out more. Also wanted to see if you have demand data with more resolution than the the bill for Selmet.', NULL, 778, NULL),
(875, 334, 1791, 1, 0, 11552, '2014-11-07', 'Jeff and Colleen, Specific Feedback:                 AR #1  Combine Air SystemsThis has not been implemented.  The cost is considered too much at this time.                AR #2  Notched V-BeltsWe have installed some notched belts.  However, in choosing or replacing belts, energy savings are a secondary consideration.                AR #3  Efficient LightingThis is an ongoing process.  We have made a decision to replace fixtures as they fail.                AR #4  Efficient Fan BladesThis has not been implemented.  We are in discussions about  priority and actual cost benefit.                AR #5  Engineered Air NozzlesThis has been implemented.  We replaced all nozzles with OSHA approved safety nozzles, and I have been told they are also energy-efficient engineered nozzles. This was an ongoing process over the past two years. General Feedback: The report was very helpful.  We are currently involved in a High Performance Energy Management program with ESI and Bonneville.  We used your report among others to establish areas of emphasis for improving energy efficiency.  We are currently concentrating on our compressed air system, specifically leak elimination.  We will certainly consider implementing your suggestions for the air systems if economic conditions allow.   Larry MorrisonElectrical Systems SupervisorSimpson Lumber  Longview', NULL, 757, 754),
(876, 334, 1644, 1, 0, 11552, '2014-12-01', 'sent initial email with implementation report questions and AR summaries to Darren Wilson.', NULL, 757, 769),
(877, 334, 1644, 1, 0, -1, '2014-12-01', 'Sent initial email to Darren Wilson with implementation questions and AR summaries. Will follow up with a phone call in a week. ', NULL, -1, 768),
(878, 334, 1641, 1, 0, 11552, '2014-10-13', 'Hi Colleen,Sorry for not responding sooner. We have had a major change in our management here at Shining Ocean. On top of that we are in the last two weeks pf preparations for a major inspection. If it is ok with you could you give me a note the first of November and I can find all the pertinent info. If you are on a hard deadline let me knowThanksMichael FisherMike,Thank you for getting back to me. We are a little past our deadline, but if you can\'t get the information until November, I can still work with that. I will send you a reminder November first if I don\'t hear back from you before then.Thank you,Colleen', NULL, 757, 751),
(879, 334, 1641, 1, 0, -1, '2014-11-03', 'Mike,I am writing to remind you about the energy recommendation implementation information you agreed to send me now that it is November. I will also re-send the initial email outlining everything we need for the implementation report we have to submit to the DOE. I hope to hear from you soon.Thank you,Colleen JohnsonOregon State UniversityEnergy Efficiency Center/Industrial Assessment CenterEnergy Analyst/Implementation Manager', NULL, -1, 751),
(880, 321, 1703, 1, 1, NULL, '2014-12-02', 'Trying to re-contact Paul again about an assessment. Was very interested but in the middle of expansion last time we talked (few months previous). Will call again next week.', 64, -1, NULL),
(881, 321, 1799, 1, 1, NULL, '2014-12-02', 'Contacted Bill about a winter assessment at International Paper. Contacted back with pre-assessment information filled out. Looking to see if Winter date works. ', 104, -1, NULL),
(882, 225, 1801, 1, 0, NULL, '2014-12-10', 'Sent pre-audit - and NDABBU is a food manufacturing company producing fresh baked products such as bread, rolls, muffins, donuts etc. I am interested in knowing the possibility of conducting no cost energy assessments at our manufacturing plant and depots in Oregon. Deports are basically warehouses for route truck pickups to grocery stores. Do your center also conduct energy assessments in neighboring States? I have attached a list of depot and plant locations in Oregon. I recently worked with one of the IACs at Univ of Miami on an energy assessments at our manufacturing plants in Florida. Please let me know if you need additional information. Thank you', NULL, NULL, 832),
(883, 225, 1801, 1, 0, NULL, '2014-12-11', 'Hello Kumar,I am following up on our conversation today.  I would be glad to field a team to visit your Beaverton Bakery January. At the moment the I know I can field a team on Monday or Friday. If  I can find another day mid week, I will let you know. I will look forward to hearing what specific dates might be best for you.I will also be glad to field a team to visit your Kent Bakery. Given the distance to travel, it will be best to set that for Spring Break or this summer.Thanks- Joe Junker(Apologies if I interrupted you at home when I called. I did not realize you were on the east coast.)', 105, -1, NULL),
(884, 225, 1641, 1, 0, -1, '2014-12-16', 'Trying to follow up to get implementation results.', NULL, -1, 751),
(885, 321, 1799, 1, 1, NULL, '2014-12-16', 'Bill is out of the office until the new year. They are ready for a Winter term audit on a tue/wed/thur. He wants to address confidentiality concerns. ', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(886, 225, 1802, 1, 0, NULL, '2014-12-17', 'Jeff Mason sent our pre-audit letter on to Andy', NULL, -1, 836),
(887, 225, 1802, 1, 0, NULL, '2014-12-17', 'Good Morning Andy, (Thanks Jeff),I understand you have an interest our assessments. I see Jeff has sent you our standard letter assessment offer letter. I will be pleased to field a team to visit your facility and perform an assessment on a date that works for you. I have no doubt your annual energy costs exceed U.S.DOE\'s minimum of $100,000.  Do you have any thoughts on when it might be best for you to have us visit? We have openings next term and beyond. If you would like to learn more about he program, I would be glad to give you a call, but I understand how time be tight in the lead up to winter holiday. Let me know.In the mean time, the letter outlines our assessment process and what we need to collect to best prepare for an assessment. The key things to return so we can get started are the:Industrial Pre-Assessment Form (that includes eligibility and logistic information)Utility Release (so we can collect a one year month-to-month profile of your energy use and utility expenses)The letter also includes a list of additional helpful preparatory information. While they are not required, they are helpful and can greatly improve the job we are able to do for you. Again, let me know if you have any questions.  I look forward to working with you. Thanks!-Joe Junker.(You might also want to visit our web-site to find out more about our program: http://eec.engr.oregonstate.edu/) ', NULL, -1, 836),
(888, 225, 1803, 1, 0, NULL, '2014-12-18', 'Sent pre-audit doc - schedule for Summer 2015?Dear Mike,I hope you can accept my apologies for the late-late follow-up to your expressed interest in an OSU Energy Efficiency Center / Industrial Assessment Center assessment of your facility. (Christina Kruger at Pacific Power had forwarded me your email this summer while I was on the road performing audits. It just slipped down in my email list and I missed follow-up in a more reasonable time. With the term over I have been working through older flagged emails)In any case, I would be pleased to field a team to visit your site. With your distance from OSU we would typically plan to visit when classes are not in session. Would you like to work towards arranging a visit for this coming summer?  Based on Christina\'s referral I have no doubt your annual energy costs exceed the U.S.DOE required minimum of $100,000. To  provide you with more information I am attaching our standard letter outlining our process and the information we work to collect in preparation for a visit. I will endeavor to call you after January 1st. In the mean time, have a pleasant holiday.-Joe Junker.', NULL, -1, 821),
(889, 225, 1801, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-01-07', 'Joe, The Beaverton plant is currently involved in an oven upgrade project and has requested if the audit can be done on a Tue in February or March. Mondays and Fridays are their down days for cleaning. Thanks. Saludos, Kumar NavileProject Engineer - Environmental/ SustainabilityCell Phone: 828-368-2349', NULL, -1, 832),
(890, 225, 1802, 1, 0, NULL, '2014-12-18', 'Hi  Joe, Thanks for your email and making yourself available. Ill get working on the forms. As for timing, I think we can make a day in January work. Tuesdays are usually a good day for me, as I dont usually have any regularly-scheduled meetings, but we can make another day work if needed. Thanks, Andy Tobin | General ManagerThermal Modification Technologies, Inc.503.654.6511 Thanks Andy,I will look forward to working with you then. Currently Mondays and Fridays are our best days to field a team, although I have asked my lead students to find at least one more day - mid week. I will let them know that a Tuesday would be ideal for you. It is getting thin around here with students heading out on holiday, so I may not be able close the loop on a proposed date to visit until all are back after Jan 1st.Much appreciated! - Joe', NULL, -1, 836),
(891, 225, 1802, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-01-07', 'Hi Andy,Just thought I\'d follow up on our conversation from before the holidays. Do you have an idea of potential dates to schedule an assessment visit? Looking forward to working with you.- Joe', NULL, -1, 836),
(892, 315, 1804, 2, 0, 11762, '2015-01-07', 'Called John to discuss titanium weighing method recommendation.', NULL, 778, 837),
(893, 225, 1808, 2, 0, NULL, '2015-01-15', 'Explained our audit process to Adam and followed up with the preaudit letter and email. He will work with the plant folks to confirm their willingness to participate. ', NULL, -1, 835),
(894, 225, 1604, 2, 0, -1, '2015-01-16', 'Imp call attempt', NULL, -1, 751),
(895, 225, 1803, 2, 0, NULL, '2015-01-16', 'LVM - Following up on pre-holiday email. And fall referral from Christina Kruger. ', NULL, -1, 821),
(896, 321, 1801, 1, 1, NULL, '2015-01-20', 'Date is set for February 24th (Tuesday). Kumar is working on pre-assess and utility release', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(897, 321, 1802, 1, 1, NULL, '2015-01-10', 'Date set for February 2nd. Brad to work on pre-asses paperwork ', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(898, 225, 1816, 2, 0, NULL, '2015-01-22', 'Jack Called to say they wanted to have us visit this summer. Krisinda Gibson is his supervisor. They make xray film - coating and drying - but now expand to coating anything. A lot of ovens for drying. Use steam to heat to 200 deg. Had ETO in for...... An AVISTA transport customer. He suggested and I agreed to followup with an email to Krisinda. I sent Krisinda the pre-audit letter again. ', NULL, -1, 821),
(899, 225, 1799, 2, 0, NULL, '2015-01-22', 'Pre-audit walkthrough call - Tyler and Alberto included.', NULL, -1, NULL),
(900, 225, 1808, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-01-22', 'Message from Adam. Met with waste water plant folks. The would like to go forward. Can you call to clarify some details.?For utility information energy profiler PPL ok - yesNG information - yesPlant guys like a couple days better than one. Perhaps a pre-audit visit instead of call would be good too. ', NULL, -1, 835);
INSERT INTO `ContactLog` (`ContactLogId`, `EmployeeId`, `PersonId`, `ContactTypeId`, `GrantId`, `TaskId`, `Date`, `Notes`, `LeadId`, `ProjectId`, `LocationId`) VALUES
(901, 332, 1772, 2, 0, 11800, '2015-01-23', 'Called and spoke with Paul. He has a team meeting set up on 1/27/15 to discuss the report, will hold off on printing and mailing after after I receive feedback on that. Emailed him the latest version after Rutger corrections.', NULL, 777, 431),
(902, 225, 1289, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-01-23', 'Michael Birran - was with Atlas Cylinder - now with Fujimi Corporation - in Tualatin and Wilsonville  Office :503-972-5573   Cell: 503-539-5573 Liked working with us at Atlas - would like to have us visit', NULL, -1, 840),
(903, 225, 1289, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-01-26', 'Make Abrasives for INTEL to polish Wafer. Have an issue now (dropped fire extinguisher discharged and made a mess). Send the info to my email. Will follow up. Pencil us in for Spring. Want to get a place in line. Will send Pre-audit DocEmail- mbirran@fujimico.com Spring Assessment.', NULL, -1, 840),
(904, 344, 1818, 2, 0, 11106, '2015-01-27', 'Called the number and found out that Darren Wilson no longer works there. And was redirected to Environmental Health Manager, Jessica Straight. She answered all the questions.', NULL, 215, 768),
(905, 346, 1818, 1, 0, 11106, '2015-01-29', 'I have called the number and got the email. Also let her know that we will have a follow up around july.', NULL, 215, 768),
(906, 346, 1662, 2, 0, 11106, '2015-01-29', 'I called the Customer Support Department and got the call transfer to Judy Anderson. She got my contact information and sent it to a couple people in hopes that someone will be able to report back to me.', NULL, 215, 761),
(907, 346, 1662, 2, 0, 11106, '2015-01-29', 'Got a call from attune foods, they have no idea who we should talk to, and gave me Jason\'s number. I left a message for him and is hopes for him to contact me soon with a reasonable answer.', NULL, 215, 761),
(911, 225, 1641, 1, 0, -1, '2015-02-03', 'Joseph F. Junker <joseph.f.junker@gmail.com>2:49 PM (19 hours ago)to mikefisher Hi Mike,I thought I would touch base again. I am hoping I did not miss an email from you with feedback on our assessment and report for Shining Ocean. If not, might it be easier for you to have a quick phone conversation than draft an email. If so let me know a good time to call.- Joe Junker', NULL, -1, 751),
(912, 225, 1641, 1, 0, -1, '2015-02-04', 'Mike Fisher <Mike.Fisher@shining-ocean.com>8:41 AM (1 hour ago)to Tony, Rick, me Hi Joe,Sounds good. I am free from 10am. Call my cell at 206-786-2874 Mike Fisher <Mike.Fisher@shining-ocean.com>8:41 AM (1 hour ago)to Tony, Rick, me Hi Joe,Sounds good. I am free from 10am. Call my cell at 206-786-2874 Called @ 10:30 and LVM - will try again later today', NULL, -1, 751),
(914, 332, 1772, 2, 0, 11715, '2015-02-04', 'Paul\'s feedback on the digital copy of the report.AR#1: Was concerned that the AR stated that air would be pulled in from within the facility, but air is actually being drawn in from the outside. The feasibility of this needs to be examined, as there may be a delta T in some months of the year.ARs 2,4,5,7: seemed to be taking action on pursuing these ARs.ARs 3 & 6: hadn\'t had time to fully look into these ARs, but didn\'t shut them down as unfeasible.', NULL, 777, 431),
(915, 225, 1819, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-02-11', 'Pre-audit letter sent......Good day Adelina,Thank you for the email. Yes, our center offers no-cost assessments to eligible industrial sites. I would be pleased to set up a visit to your facility. I have little doubt your energy costs exceed the minimum $100,000 a year that our  U.S.DOE funding requires. I can give you a call to let you know more about the program and answer any questions you might have. Is there an ideal time? In the mean time, I\'ve attached a letter that outlines our assessment process and how we prepare. If you just want to get thing rolling, the key items to return are the:Industrial Pre-Assessment Form (that includes eligibility and logistic information)Utility Release (so we can collect a one year month-to-month profile of your energy use and utility expenses)(The letter also includes a list of additional helpful preparatory information. While they are not required, they are helpful and can greatly improve the job we are able to do for you.) I look forward to working with you. Thanks!-Joe Junker.(You might want to visit our web-site to find out more about our program: http://eec.engr.oregonstate.edu/)', NULL, -1, 839),
(916, 310, 1606, 2, 0, 11106, '2015-02-11', 'Called to follow up with Renee, haven\'t heard back via email or phone since sending the original documentation.  Will follow up with bumps on emails.', NULL, 215, 752),
(917, 346, 1662, 2, 0, 11106, '2015-02-12', 'I have contacted Judy and she will see what she can do about finding a head electrician to talk to', NULL, 215, 761),
(918, 310, 1606, 1, 0, 11106, '2015-02-12', 'Received return email from Renee and Patrick Murphy regarding implementation, have enough information to enter into Rutgers.', NULL, 215, 752),
(919, 225, 1819, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-02-11', 'Good Afternoon Joseph, Jeff asked me to contact you in regards to conducting an energy efficiency assessment of our facility.  Please let me know what I can help you with and how we can move forward. Best Regards,Adela  Adelina Campuzano | CI CoordinatorSheldon Manufacturing, Inc.300 N. 26th Ave | Cornelius, OR 97113503.640.3000 ext. 147www.shellab.com |adelinac@shellab.com', NULL, -1, 839),
(920, 225, 1819, 2, 0, NULL, '2015-02-19', 'Putting that info together. PGE and NWNG ~$120K - spring term would be ideal. Lets shoot for April. Want to make sure Jeff & Fred Stevens can be there. Best Days: Mon, Tue or Wed ', NULL, -1, 839),
(921, 346, 1597, 1, 0, 11106, '2015-02-26', 'I have emailed Dan about the questions and asked what time we could make the call.', NULL, 215, 504),
(922, 321, 1808, 1, 1, NULL, '2014-02-24', 'Contacted Adam again about the feasibility of the first week of April as the date. ', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(923, 225, 1820, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-02-24', 'Hello Bob, I just came across this email exchange from this fall so I thought I would follow up again. I would be pleased to work with you to set up as U.S.DOE no cost assessment of your facility. Might you have any interest? FYI: I am attaching PDF version of information on our program that one of my students just prepared.  Let me know if you would like to learn more. Thanks - Joe Junker', NULL, -1, 842),
