(937, 225, 1825, 2, 0, -1, '2015-04-21', 'Scott - Site Electrician - only person left to talk to - Mobile: 541-228-2780Bill James and engineer and maint manager let go with new owner ship. Gave copy of study to new maintenance supervisor and health and safety  regarding fans. Thats as far as it went. Still in a whirlwind of new policies - not sure what the ultimate goals - could talk to acting supervisor - Maintenance Supervisor. - Michale Castorena 0 mcastorena@attunefoods.com  and have him give a call. Air to deal with, allergen issues, fan issues. Adding exhaust fans vfds and energy efficient.  Wanting to work on correcting controls and settings on compressed air. The VFD and standard air compressor are not staged well for lead and lag operation. The pressures are also not well set. 100 PSI on standard and 125 PSI on VFD - (issue with air starvation at far end)a lot of variation in what lines run air demand fluctuates wildly.', NULL, -1, 761),
(938, 225, 1829, 1, 0, -1, '2015-04-22', 'Hello Michael,I was just speaking to Scott OConnor regarding the assessment report OSU prepared for Attune Foods in 2013. It sounds like there have been a lot of change in facility operation. He thought you might be able to speak to the suggestions we made. U.S.DOE asks us to follow up on the work they fund to see what has resulted. I would also be glad to explain anything we suggested as time and staff have moved on since we prepared that report. For the report: ...(standard imp email)', NULL, -1, 761),
