(1000, 321, 1722, 1, 0, 11106, '2015-06-01', 'Contacted Robert about implementation. Summarized recommendations and asked if he could help with our imp. report. Going to set up a time to talk on the phone. ', NULL, 215, 494),
(1001, 225, 1916, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-06-01', 'Scott,Thanks, I am glad you are interested in having an OSU team visit.  Regarding a conference callThis Thursday afternoon should work for me.Friday is trickier but I have time before 11 AM, and could fit in a call around 1:45 PM or after 4 PMIn the mean time I\'ve attached a letter that outlines our assessment process and what we like to collect to best prepare for an assessment. The key items that allow us to prepare are the:Industrial Pre-Assessment Form (that includes eligibility and logistic information)Utility Release (so we can collect a one year month-to-month profile of your energy use and utility expenses)The letter also includes a list of additional helpful preparatory information. While they are not required, they are helpful and can greatly improve the job we are able to do for you. Once we settle on a time for a call,  I will look forward to speaking with you. Thanks!-Joe Junker.John Thornton: Hi Scott  Im connecting you to Joe Junker of the OSU Energy Efficiency Center so he can get in contact with you for planning and logistics.  His contact information is enclosed below. ', NULL, -1, 856),
(1002, 225, 1917, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-06-01', 'Bill Chambers Stahlbush: Steve, In 2014 the OSU Energy Efficiency Center did an energy audit of my plant.  It was the fourth energy audit that we have done over the years.  Each time it have been very valuable and I would encourage you to look into an audit for your plant.  Joe Junker is the head of the center, his email is attached.   Hope the information on the air compressors was of value.  I did some more reading on blow molding and appreciate more the specific need of oil free and 600 psi air.Thanks Buddy,We are mid way in a large project with Energy Trust but Mike will follow up...yes I love to delegate.Keep it Real, Steve Emerywww.earth2o.comSteve,Let me know when you would like to follow-up. I would be pleased to send a team to work with your facility. Given your distance from OSU, a summer or winter/spring break trip would be ideal. (We still have some openings this summer).FYI: I am attaching some eBrochures about the OSU Energy Efficiency Center and our Industrial Assessment Center project. Thanks - Joe Junker', NULL, -1, 857),
(1003, 225, 1918, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-05-29', 'Hi Joe, We would like to lock-in your group for coming to Dillard the week of July 27.  If that still works for your group, lets plan on it. I found the below e-mail and thought it would be good for jogging both our memories.  It is a good summary of the time requirements needed for Dillard.One slight correction needed pertains to the total hours needed for Dillard.  If you combine the 3 Boilers with the two natural gas heaters at Dillard particleboard (the Dillard Complex is considered one source), you have a total annual thermal energy used of 8.3 TBTU.  Therefore: Dillard (including 3 boilers and 2 natural gas heaters) - Annual thermal energy use: 8.3 TBTU, 82.4 Minimum site hours  (~2-3 minimum site days for us) (still accurate?) The Dillard Complex includes the sawmill, 2 plywood plants, particleboard plant, and powerhouse. I still need to ask Ellen about the assessment your group performed of the Sawmill in 2011.  At first, she did not think we could count that towards the energy assessment.  But in reading the rule, I still want to run some things by her. Lets still plan on the week of July 27.  But  I will hopefully have an answer for you by next week, regarding the Sawmill portion. Thanks,Kristana', NULL, -1, 545),
(1004, 225, 1918, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-06-01', 'Thanks Kristana,I will put it on our calendar. I think the 2-3 days will still hit the 82.4 Minimum site hour as long as we bring a larger team. Let me know about the Sawmill.Do you still have the letter outlining the assessment process and the information we will want to collect ahead of time, or should I send one again?- Joe', NULL, -1, 545),
(1005, 225, 1918, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-06-01', 'Hi, If you would, please resend the letter. You likely sent it to Ellen last time, and I cant find a copy in my files. Thanks! Your main contact at the Dillard site is Nate Webb.  I will send him your contact info.  Nate will be the one gathering all the requested info and coordinating the specific details as the date approaches.  Nates contact info is:Nate WebbFacility Environmental Manager  Dillard Complex541-679-2695nathanw@rfpco.com Also, regarding the Sawmills assessment in 2011, it would need to meet the requirements below, in order to count as a Boiler MACT energy assessment.  Do you think what you did in 2011 would count? If so, I will still need to run it by Ellen, and we would probably need to have the 2011 assessment amended to meet the requirements. An energy assessment completed on or after January 1, 2008, that meets or is amended to meet the energy assessment requirements in this table, satisfies the energy assessment requirement.a.       A visual inspection of the boiler or process heater system.b.      An evaluation of operating characteristics of the boiler or process heater systems, specifications of energy using systems, operating and maintenance procedures, and unusual operating constraints.c.       An inventory of major energy use systems consuming energy from affected boilers and process heaters and which are under the control of the boiler/process heater owner/operator.d.      A review of available architectural and engineering plans, facility operation and maintenance procedures and logs, and fuel usage.e.      A review of the facilitys energy management practices and provide recommendations for improvements consistent with the definition of energy management practices, in identified.f.        A list of cost-effective energy conservation measures that are within the facilitys control.g.       A list of the energy savings potential of the energy conservation measures identified.h.      A comprehensive report detailing the ways to improve efficiency, the cost of specific improvements, benefits, and the time frame for recouping those investments. Thanks,Kristana ', NULL, -1, 545),
(1006, 225, 1918, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-06-02', 'Kristana, I would think our sawmill report would have met the energy assessment requirements. Do you have a copy of the report? (Let me know, if not, I can likely find the PDF to send.)In the mean time I am attaching the letter I mentioned. It outlines our assessment process and what we need to collect to best prepare for an assessment. The critical things to return so we can get going on our pre-visit analysis are the:Industrial Pre-Assessment Form (that includes eligibility and logistic information)Utility Release (so we can collect a one year month-to-month profile of your energy use and utility expenses) (In the case of your facility, we will also likely need a one year month-to-month profile of internally measured energy use - at the power house and any other plant specific data.)The letter also includes a list of additional helpful preparatory information. While they are not required, they are helpful and can greatly improve the job we are able to do for you. I am copying Nate as I imagine he will help us with a lot of the above.Please call me if you have any questions. Our next step will be to schedule a pre-assessment phone conversation to review plant processes before the audit - once we have completed our pre-analysis.  I look forward to working with you and visiting in the week of July 27th. Thanks!-Joe Junker.(You might also want to visit our web-site to find out more about our program: http://eec.engr.oregonstate.edu/)', NULL, -1, 545),
(1007, 346, 1751, 2, 0, 11106, '2015-06-02', 'I have try calling Ronald at 3 and left him a message', NULL, 215, 760),
(1008, 225, 1090, 2, 0, NULL, '2015-05-28', 'Talked to Tom. He said they needed to check with their Owner.', NULL, -1, 850),
(1009, 225, 1090, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-06-02', 'Hello Tom,I thought I would follow-up to our conversation last week. I know you need to check with the owner before you can invite us. I thought it might help to see the letter we send in preparation for a visit. It outlines our assessment process and what we need to collect to best prepare for an assessment. The key items we ask you to return so we can get going on our pre-visit analysis are the:Industrial Pre-Assessment Form (that includes eligibility and logistic information)Utility Release (so we can collect a one year month-to-month profile of your energy use and utility expenses) (In the case of your facility, we will also likely need a one year month-to-month profile of internally measured energy use - at the power house and any other plant specific data.)The letter also includes a list of additional helpful preparatory information. While they are not required, they are helpful and can greatly improve the job we are able to do for you. I hope I can I look forward to working with you - Thanks!-Joe Junker.(You might also want to visit our web-site to find out more about our program: http://eec.engr.oregonstate.edu/)', NULL, -1, 850),
(1010, 321, 1606, 2, 1, NULL, '2015-06-01', 'Talked to Renee on the phone. She expressed that the facility has already undergone energy management practices and is not seeking our services at this time.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(1011, 225, 1450, 2, 0, NULL, '2015-06-04', 'LVM: 541 613 3022.Getting close to end of June looking to land 2 more. Rogue River is a possibility. How about Sabroso, Amy\'s Kitchen, Harry and David? Would you like me to contact them directly?- Joe', NULL, -1, 845),
(1012, 225, 1467, 2, 0, NULL, '2015-06-04', 'Woodland Washington - connected to Columbia Cold Storage. Might want to do both. Yes - go ahead - help us with if you want.Something like last time - bring in Sarah York.Send Brochure. One of the leads maybe instead of the manager(Did all the lighting)', NULL, -1, NULL),
(1013, 225, 1612, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-06-04', 'LVM - Any potential with Entek or Weyerhaeuser? (Should I be calling a diff number for your office and not this cell phone all of the time?)', NULL, -1, NULL),
(1014, 225, 1742, 2, 0, NULL, '2015-06-04', 'Hi Uli,Any potential to visit your Issqua plant on a trip to Seattle this summer.?', NULL, -1, NULL),
(1015, 225, 338, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-06-04', 'Called Tom\'s number, got someone else. Called central number - Tom\'s name no longer familiar. Got put through to current facility manager Dave ???. Left voicemail', NULL, -1, NULL),
(1016, 225, 1920, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-06-04', 'Hi Bryan,I just left you voice mail as well. I was calling at the suggestion of Christina Kruger, Pacific Power. I wanted to see if you would be interested in a no cost Energy Efficiency Assessment. We are planning a trip to Southern Oregon this summer to visit a few facilities and would be pleased to include yours. There is no cost to eligible facilities as the audit is paid for by the U.S.DOE. All it takes on your part is the time to host us.I am attaching two e-brochures to fill you in more:.The IAC brochure speaks to the industrial assessmentThe EEC brochure speaks to our program in general.Let me know if you have an interest.Thanks - Joe Junker', NULL, -1, 859),
(1017, 225, 1920, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-06-04', 'Joe, Were interested.  What dates / times do you have? Bryan', NULL, -1, 859),
(1018, 225, 1920, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-06-04', 'Glad to hear it. We  have not locked in dates but we have been looking at the end of this Month (June). Would one day the earlier part of the week of June 29th work for you? - Joe', NULL, -1, 859),
(1019, 225, 1801, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-06-04', 'Hello Kumar,I am scheduling my summer audit trips and would like to include your Kent facility. We are looking at the Week of June 29th for a trip a few plants in the Kent - Seattle - Tacoma  area. Is there someone I should work with at the Kent facility - or can you see if that time frame works?Thanks - Joe Junker', NULL, -1, 833),
(1020, 225, 350, 2, 0, NULL, '2015-06-04', 'Wondered if you would like us to visit again to refresh the 2008 audit.?', NULL, -1, NULL),
(1021, 225, 350, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-06-04', 'Subject: No cost Energy Efficiency Assessment: Oregon State University Energy Efficiency CenterHi Robert,I just left you voice mail as well. It has been awhile since our 2008 energy efficiency assessment of your facility.  I wanted to see if you would be interested in an updated assessment. We are planning a trip to Southern Oregon this summer to visit a few facilities and would be pleased to include yours. There is still no cost to eligible facilities as the audit is paid for by the U.S.DOE. All it takes on your part is the time to host us.I am attaching two e-brochures to fill you in more:.The IAC brochure speaks to the industrial assessmentThe EEC brochure speaks to our program in general.Let me know if you have an interest.Thanks - Joe Junker', NULL, -1, NULL),
(1022, 225, 1801, 2, 0, -1, '2015-06-05', 'Calling to follow up on email (late I know) - Would it work to visit your Kent facility in the week of June 29th?', NULL, 787, 833),
(1023, 225, 1801, 1, 0, -1, '2015-06-04', 'Hello Kumar,I am scheduling my summer audit trips and would like to include your Kent facility. We are looking at the Week of June 29th for a trip a few plants in the Kent - Seattle - Tacoma  area. Is there someone I should work with at the Kent facility - or can you see if that time frame works?Thanks - Joe Junker', NULL, 787, 833),
(1024, 225, 1801, 2, 0, NULL, '2015-06-05', 'Called me back - concerned about plant closures - not sure of future of Kent plant. Will get back to me in the middle of next week. ', NULL, -1, 833),
(1025, 225, 1913, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-06-08', 'Doug, I spoke with Darren earlier today about the OSU Industrial program, and it sounds like Darrens boss is not onboard with Longview participating. Not sure for the reason, but unfortunately I dont think it will work out. Just wanted to update you. Also, thanks again for all your great info on soft starts, reactive power, etc.. It has been very helpful in putting together our Energy Team training. Skyler', NULL, -1, 103),
(1026, 225, 1467, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-06-04', 'Hi Jackson,Good talking. I would be pleased to set up a trip to your Woodland facility. (Columbia Coldstore, and collaboration with Sara York would be icing on the cake)I have attached our two new brochures.The IAC brochure speaks to our industrial assessmentsThe EEC brochure speaks to our program in general. Take care - Joe', NULL, -1, 860),
(1027, 225, 1467, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-06-04', 'Thanks, Joe. I emailed John King at Woodland, but he is out of the office until Monday.', NULL, -1, 860),
(1028, 225, 1467, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-06-08', 'Hi Joe, We are flexible on what day you want to visit. What works best for you? Thank you,Jackson', NULL, -1, 860),
(1029, 225, 1921, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-06-05', 'Christina, Good morning.  We are currently preparing for our annual outage and will be pretty busy until after the second week of July.  If you would like to schedule an assessment sometime after July 11th we can accommodate your study.  My contact info is below if you have any questions.  Thanks. Sean Lenninger', NULL, -1, 550),
(1030, 225, 1921, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-06-05', 'Sean,I am glad to learn you are interested having us visit for an assessment. I would be pleased to add you to our list of facilities we plan to serve. As Christina noted, we are currently working on dialing in a trip to your area in the end of this month (June). I understand that this is not a good time-frame for you.  We could try to mount another trip in your direction later this summer (to leverage our travel costs, we try to arrange for 3-4 sites to visit on a trip to your area.) If we can not pull that off this summer, we could shoot for a spring break or summer trip next year. In the mean time I am attaching a letter that describes our assessment process. It outlines what we work to collect ahead of time to best prepare for an assessment. The key items we ask you to return so we can get going on our pre-visit analysis are the:Industrial Pre-Assessment Form (that includes eligibility and logistic information)Utility Release (so we can collect a one year month-to-month profile of your energy use and utility expenses) (In the case of your facility, we will also likely need a one year month-to-month profile of internally measured energy use - at the power house and any other plant specific data.)The letter also includes a list of additional helpful preparatory information. While they are not required, they are helpful and can greatly improve the job we are able to do for you. Of course, please call me if you have any questions. Our next step would be to schedule an assessment for a time that works for both you and the students. I look forward to working with you. Thanks!-Joe Junker.I am also attaching two e-brochures on our program: The IAC brochure speaks to the industrial assessmentThe EEC brochure speaks to our program in general.(You might also want to visit our web-site to find out more: http://eec.engr.oregonstate.edu/)', NULL, -1, 550),
(1031, 225, 1467, 2, 0, NULL, '2015-06-05', 'Pref not in June - Will check with plant. July, Week of 29th Mon or Thur (29th or 2nd.) See what works best. (Mid July or any week in August workable too)', NULL, -1, 860),
(1032, 225, 1920, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-06-08', 'The 30th works best for us.  Please get back to me with the amount of time I should set aside on the 30th.', NULL, -1, 859),
(1033, 225, 1920, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-06-08', 'Glad to hear it Bryan, I will look forward to fielding a team to visit your facility on June 30th to perform an assessment then.Typically we spend a day on site with a team of 4-5 analysts and a faculty lead. The morning starts with introductions and an orientation tour of the facility followed by a brainstorm on potential opportunities. With feedback from you on what to prioritize we spend the remainder of the day collecting a data set to model the systems we want to develop recommendations around. After an end of day de-brief we will head off to prepare a report for you with in ~60 days. I\'ve attached a letter that outlines our assessment process and what we work to collect to best prepare for an assessment. The key items we ask you to return so we can get going on our pre-visit analysis are the:Industrial Pre-Assessment Form (that includes eligibility and logistic information)Utility Release (so we can collect a one year month-to-month profile of your energy use and utility expenses) (In the case of your facility, we will also likely need a one year month-to-month profile of internally measured energy use - at the power house and any other plant specific data.)The letter also includes a list of additional helpful preparatory information. While they are not required, they are helpful and can greatly improve the job we are able to do for you. Please call me if you have any questions. Thanks!-Joe Junker.', NULL, -1, 859),
(1034, 225, 1921, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-06-08', 'Sean,In reviewing our database and the last time we were able to assess your plant, I realized it might take two days to assess your site, as I believe you have a plywood plant and a particleboard plant on site. Am I correct? We would typically spend a day at each plant. That would mean we would only need to find one other facility to visit to stretch the value of our travel costs. (And I am talking to one other facility that might fill that slot.) If we could make it work, I would think we could get down to visit you this summer, perhaps in August. Would that work for you?Thanks - Joe Junker', NULL, -1, 550),
(1035, 225, 1090, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-06-08', 'Hi Tom,I wanted to follow up with you regarding scheduling a visit to your site this summer. It currently looks like our June trip might be fully scheduled. However, we have two other plants we are talking to that are not included in the June trip as it was too soon for them. As a result we are working to schedule as second trip south later this summer, perhaps in August. I got the sense that having us visit you this June might be to quick for you as well. Might it work better for you to have us visit in August?Let me know. I\'d be pleased to put you on our calendar.Thanks - Joe Junker', NULL, -1, 850),
(1036, 225, 1801, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-06-08', 'Hi Kumar,I know you thought it would take until mid-week to sort out whether to go forward with having us assess your Kent facility. However - I now have another facility that would like to take that slot for our North trip in the week of June 29th. I am holding that for your Kent facility, but wanted to get a sense from you if you could estimate how likely it is that it will be a \"go\".Thanks - Joe', NULL, -1, 833),
(1037, 225, 1742, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-06-05', 'Joe, John Got your messages yesterday. I did ask the Chehalis plant to see if they were interested. Unfortunately they have not made a decision. I did send a reminder this morning. Thanks,', NULL, -1, 858),
(1038, 225, 1742, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-06-05', 'Thanks Uli,I appreciate your checking. I am not sure of John\'s thinking, but one of your Seattle area facilities could also be good candidates for us as we expect to be traveling to Kent and Everette too. - Joe JunkerUnderstood. However, the Issaquah plant is currently without a maintenance manager and the Rainier facility just had a Track & Tune with Cascade Energy. So Chehalis would be a better choice. Thanks, (Uli)Makes sense, Thanks Uli. - Joe', NULL, -1, 858),
(1039, 225, 1742, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-06-08', 'Hi Uli,I am now talking to another facility that might fit into the slot for our North trip in the week of June 29th if it will not work for your Issaquah plant. This other facility is close enough that we could also visit them on a long single day round trip, so I am holding the trip spot open for you but wanted to note that it would be helpful to know as soon as possible.Thanks - Joe', NULL, -1, 858),
(1040, 225, 1922, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-06-05', 'Chris Magee - Harry and David - message sent over by Dave Bowden .. Give me a call at (541) 864-2741 .... be glad to work with youLVM - Week of 29th, glad you are interested. Will call after 2.He called back , gave me his email address. Said the time frame works. Sent Pre-Audit Doc. ', NULL, 796, 520),
(1041, 225, 1742, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-06-09', 'Joe, It looks like we will need to pass this time around. Please let us know when you will be back in this area. Thanks,               Uli', NULL, -1, 858);
INSERT INTO `ContactLog` (`ContactLogId`, `EmployeeId`, `PersonId`, `ContactTypeId`, `GrantId`, `TaskId`, `Date`, `Notes`, `LeadId`, `ProjectId`, `LocationId`) VALUES
(1042, 225, 1801, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-06-09', 'Sorry KumarI was putting out fires yesterday and got really busy.  Joe, Please read Kellys response below. Thanks for keeping us in mind. I will be in contact about Beaverton and other possible opportunities for an energy audit. Saludos, Kumar NavileProject Engineer - Environmental/ SustainabilityCell Phone: 828-368-2349I really dont see the value of doing this for Kent, since it is a leased facility, very small, and difficult to determine any real savings because they pay a percentage of the utility bills, based on square footage.  ThanksKelly ', NULL, -1, 833),
(1043, 225, 1820, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-06-09', 'Out of office - LVM - Want to get on the summer schedule?', NULL, -1, 842),
(1044, 225, 1783, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-06-09', 'may be interested - changed departments - do have new maint manager that would handle facilities type things - could get better information.  EMail best: lovellcurrence@tbfood.com - or call this number to be connected. ', NULL, -1, 828),
(1045, 225, 1923, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-06-09', 'Good Morning Lovell,Seth Crass suggested I contact you. Seth and I have been talking about setting up a no-cost full scope energy and efficiency assessment of Trail Blazer Foods. There is no cost to eligible facilities as the audit is paid for by the U.S.DOE. All it takes on your part is the time to host us.I am attaching two e-brochures to fill you in more:The IAC brochure speaks to the industrial assessmentThe EEC brochure speaks to our program in general.Let me know if you have an interest. I would be pleased to put you on our assessment calendar this summer.Thanks - Joe Junker(FYI: We have a full compliment of state of the art equipment to bring to bear on these assessments including combustion analyzers, thermal imaging cameras, a non-contact ultrasonic flow meter, specialized refrigeration system analysis tools, power quality analyzers, and a broad selection of data loggers. If you have any systems that might benefit from the evaluation these allow, I believe the center can help.)', NULL, -1, 828),
(1046, 225, 1691, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-06-09', 'Joe, Sorry for the delay,  Im attaching the Letter, filled out as much as I can for the Tillamook facility.  Please let me know what your schedule looks like in July for an assessment.  Im able to provide you with spreadsheets of the utility data you may need, without going to the Tillamook PUD, unless you think there may be an advantage in getting their data. Sam ', NULL, -1, 501),
(1047, 225, 1691, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-06-09', 'Thank Sam,If you are tracking all the electrical data such as KVAR and KW (Power Factor and Demand charges) all we would need in addition is the rate schedule you are on and perhaps one bill to confirm we understand the billing. Currently it looks like we could get a team over to you one day in the week of July 13th.  Would that work? - Joe', NULL, -1, 501),
(1048, 321, 1783, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-02-21', 'Seth had indicated that he was switching roles and would no longer be the appropriate contact. He informed me he would find someone new to work with us. I followed up to see who the new contact would be. Seth had not responded.', NULL, -1, 828),
(1049, 321, 1820, 2, 0, NULL, '2015-04-22', 'Email correspondence with Bob. He accepted the pre-assessment information and wanted to move forward with dates. I sent him multiple dates. When I didn\'t receive correspondence I called, no answer.   Hey Bob,My name is Miles Naughton, Operations Manager at the EEC. I wanted to follow up with you about scheduling an assessment at the Swan Island Dairy. My director Joe sent you forms outlining what we typically collect before the assessment. I have attached them again for your convenience. If you would like to start projecting a date for the assessment sometime in May that would be great. We look forward to working with you. Regards,MilesDalton, Bob <bob.dalton@kroger.com>Apr 6to Emily, me, EEC Shoot me some dates Miles. From: Miles Naughton [mailto:milesnaughton@gmail.com] Sent: Monday, April 06, 2015 3:48 PMTo: Dalton, Bob; EEC ManageSubject: Energy Efficiency Assessment: The Kroger Co. Swan Island DairyMiles Naughton <milesnaughton@gmail.com>Apr 6to Bob, EEC, Emily Any of the days May: 6th, 7th, 8th, 13th, 14th, 15th.Miles Naughton <milesnaughton@gmail.com>Apr 22to Bob Hey Bob,If it\'s amiable for the facility we would like to set a date for the energy efficiency assessment. May 19th-21st would be a good date range for us, or the 26th-28th. Regards,Miles Naughton ', NULL, -1, 842),
(1050, 225, 1923, 2, 0, NULL, '2015-06-10', 'LVM - following up on email per Seth Crass', NULL, -1, 828),
(1051, 225, 1923, 2, 0, NULL, '2015-06-10', 'He called back, send pre-audit doc. He was ready to have us come tomorrow, but can not say about the week of the 29th until the 26th. ', NULL, -1, NULL),
(1052, 225, 1921, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-06-10', ' Joe, You are correct, we have a Hardboard and a Particleboard plant onsite.  Each plant is operated independently requiring each managers approval and coordination with their respective maintenance departments.  The Particleboard Maintenance Superintendent is Jon Dressell and his contact information is (541) 885-4815. I spoke with my maintenance superintendent about the timing of your survey and I think it would be best to postpone until next spring.  I want to ensure that we are able to provide you with the necessary support to complete your survey and with the number of projects currently scheduled, I am not sure we will have the resources.  Let me know a couple of months ahead of time and I will be able to better coordinate your visit.  Feel free to call if you have any questions.  Thanks.Thanks Sean, Yes I will put it on my calendar to contact you around the turn of the year regarding a spring trip to your site. I will follow up with Jon regarding including him in a spring trip too.- Joe ', NULL, -1, 550),
(1053, 342, 1927, 2, 0, 11978, '2015-05-11', 'Contacted Ken GRimm on the phone. The STAR program that trains painters in the correct use of tools and appropriate techniques advertise that the minimum improvement by a highly skilled painter is a 20% reduction of raw materials.Training cost USD$1,295 for a max of 45 ppl, it takes 3-4 hours, in-facility. The training considers filming workers while they do their activities and analyse their performance ', NULL, 791, 839),
(1062, 321, 1639, 2, 0, 11106, '2015-06-15', 'Called David again about the implementation report. Was out of the office, left him my name and number and a brief description. Also followed up with another email. ', NULL, 215, 764),
(1163, 346, 1936, 1, 0, 11973, '2015-05-22', 'This is a drum type evaporator there is either the batch operation or there is an auto fill option.DE-2B:  $8,595 (200 GPW, batch operation)DE-4A:  $10,990 (400 GPW, auto-fill)', NULL, 791, 839),
(1165, 348, 1643, 2, 0, 11106, '2015-06-18', 'I left and voicemail detailing that the U.S DOE requires information about the assessment. I explained that we needed specific feedback on each of recommendations we made and general feedback on the assessment we performed.', NULL, 215, 687),
(1169, 347, 1616, 1, 0, 11106, '2015-06-23', 'I sent her the base email.', NULL, 215, 759),
(1170, 347, 473, 1, 0, 11106, '2015-06-23', 'I emailed him the base email.', NULL, 215, 331),
(1171, 347, 1616, 1, 0, 11952, '2015-06-23', 'We set up a time to make the implementation call.I am calling her at 9 am on Friday the 26th.', NULL, 215, 759),
(1172, 353, 1937, 1, 0, -1, '2015-06-23', 'introductory email to introduce EEC and give an idea of what information we will be requesting.Contact received by phone receptionist Raymond is the new contact since Brian Switzer is no longer working with the Kroger Bakery', NULL, -1, 823),
(1173, 332, 1772, 1, 0, -1, '2015-06-24', 'Left voicemail & sent email for implementation follow up. Will try again in a couple days if no response.', NULL, 777, 431),
(1174, 332, 1727, 1, 0, -1, '2015-06-24', 'Called (wrong phone number) and sent implementation email on 6/24/2015. Received automatic email that Jodie is out of town until 6/29/2015. Will try again after that.', NULL, 761, 807),
(1175, 332, 1922, 2, 0, -1, '2015-06-24', 'Had pre-audit phone call. Arrival at 8:00 am locked in. Safety vests required but not steel toe. Major energy users include refrigeration, with possibility opportunities regarding boilers, air compressors, and lighting. Chris also expressed interest in water conservation measures due to the drought. Lead electrician will not be present on audit day, although there will be others to open panels.', NULL, 796, 520),
(1176, 225, 1919, 1, 0, -1, '2015-06-24', 'Nate will be our primary site contact for the July assessments', NULL, 793, 545),
(1177, 347, 1816, 2, 0, 12051, '2015-06-24', 'We talked about the plan for the assessment.', NULL, 788, NULL),
(1178, 353, 1937, 1, 0, -1, '2015-06-25', 'Sent the final assessment and sample questions to Raymond and asked to schedule a time to make a formal call', NULL, -1, 823),
(1179, 332, 1940, 1, 0, 12049, '2015-06-26', 'Steven was a part of the pre-audit call with Chris. He followed through with several motor/equipment inventory sheets, which are now stored on dropbox in Report Generation > Site Data > Motor Inventory.', NULL, 796, 520),
(1180, 225, 1765, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-06-26', 'LVM: Washinton site audtis this summmer? Aug (or late July early Sept)?Followed up with email:Hi Jeff,I just left you voice mail as well. It has been awhile since we talked about setting up energy efficiency assessment of your Alaskan plants.  Looks like we missed making that happen this year.  I was just talking to John Thornton at NWFPA and he thought you might like to set up assessments of your NW plants. I see you have plants in Anacortes, Bellingham, Seattle and Tacoma. We have some opening in the end of the summer (August primarily) and we could schedule in a trip to say, three of them if you like. Unlike the Alaskan audits - we would have the travel cost in our budget. There is still no cost to eligible facilities as the audit is paid for by the U.S.DOE. All it takes on your part is the time to host us.I am attaching two e-brochures we recently developed - although I know you are familiar with our programThe IAC brochure speaks to the industrial assessmentThe EEC brochure speaks to our program in general.Let me know if you have an interest. I\'d be pleased to get something set up. (I also would be glad to set up a visit to your Newport site, but that would be a good trip for us to do during the school year when we can not travel as far)Thanks - Joe Junker', NULL, -1, NULL),
(1181, 346, 1751, 2, 0, 11106, '2015-06-29', 'I left Ronald a message and left him my number and asked him to contact me the best time for a scheduled phone meeting ', NULL, 215, 760),
(1182, 321, 1670, 2, 0, NULL, '2015-06-29', 'Called Dathan at Tillamook and followed up with an email. Going to forward the information I give him to other production people to see if they are interested. Sent pre-assessment information. ', NULL, -1, 811),
(1183, 225, 1941, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-06-24', 'Submitted on Wednesday, June 24, 2015 - 11:51Submitted by anonymous user: 66.236.16.210Submitted values are:First Name: MikeLast Name: HolmTitle/Relation to Company: President/OwnerEmail: mike@ocfp.comCompany Name: Oregon-Canadian Forest Products Inc.Telephone: 503-647-5011Fax: 503-647-0910Street Address: 31950 NW Commercial StCity: North PlainsState: OregonZip Code: 97133PO Box: 279City : North PlainsState: OregonZip Code: 97231Industry: Lumber remanufacturerMajor Products: Douglas Fir high gradeSystems of interest or problems to be investigated:The results of this submission may be viewed at:http://mime.oregonstate.edu/node/550/submission/373', NULL, -1, 861),
(1184, 225, 1941, 2, 0, NULL, '2015-06-29', 'LVM: Call to see if we can get you set up for an assessment. I now my student, Ben, spoke to you and that he knows you because he worked for you. Will follow with an email. ', NULL, -1, 861),
(1185, 225, 1941, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-06-29', 'Hi Mike,I just left you voice mail as well. I was following up on your submittal to our online \"Arrange for an Assessment\" form. I would be pleased to work with you to set up an energy efficiency assessment  of your facility. There is no cost to eligible facilities as the audit is paid for by the U.S.DOE. All it takes on your part is the time to host us.I am attaching two e-brochures to fill you in more:.The IAC brochure speaks to the industrial assessmentThe EEC brochure speaks to our program in general.As I noted on the phone, I will be leading assessments in the Seattle area this week, but I will follow-up late this week or next. Let me know if there is a best time to call.Thanks - Joe Junker', NULL, -1, 861),
(1186, 225, 1941, 2, 0, NULL, '2015-06-29', 'He called back. Would like to set up audit. (He is not avail: Jul 10-18, Wk of Aug 17. Said we could shoot for wk of Aug 3 or 10. Sending Pre- audit letter. They have 125 employees, $350K energy cost. They work sawn lumber from other sites. (Hull Oaks +?) - Processes include, 4 Planers, Dry kiln, 6\" edger, resaw. mizer. Cut...', NULL, -1, 861),
(1187, 353, 1937, 1, 0, -1, '2015-07-04', 'Raymond - \"I would like to setup a phone call with to discuss this report. Thinking July 13th around 1 pm?\"Me - \"July 13th at 1 pm works. You should expect a call from me then.Please let me know if anything changes on your end.\"Raymond - \"Ok. Its on our calendars.\" ', NULL, -1, 823),
(1188, 225, 1946, 2, 0, NULL, '2015-07-06', 'Paul called to see if we could serve the Forest Grove plant. They are eligible so I sent the pre-audit doc. I brought up the Tillamook plant. He was willing to try to make that happen. ', NULL, -1, 485),
(1189, 321, 1670, 2, 0, NULL, '2015-07-06', 'Called Dathan again about an energy assessment. No answer, left voicemail. Will try again later this week.', NULL, -1, 811),
