(1223, 339, 1920, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-07-13', 'Hello Bryan,I have attached a trip report which briefly summarizes our assessment and the opportunities that we have identified for recommendation.We would like to receive the following information to help us with the recommendation process.-Boiler feedwater treatment chemical usage and cost per unit-Motor List/Inventory (John said he could get this in an excel file)-Live amperage readings for the blower on line 5-Size of the condenser fan on the smaller evaporative condenser attached to Engine Room #1 (in hp)-Map of the plumbing in the facility-Inventory of pneumatic equipment (required pressures included)-Metering logs for the boiler gas use, water use and steam production-Operating hours for the following equipment          - T-30         - APV West         - Buffalo Vac         - Forecirc         - APV Eact         - Steralizer 1 (same side of the street as large boiler room)         - Steralizer 2 I would also like to send a reminder that our dataloggers are done logging and if they have not been sent back yet please pull them and send them back to the OSU Energy Efficiency Center.Please feel free to email me with any questions or comments you may have regarding the report.Thank you,Vincent AlbrightEnergy Efficiency CenterOregon State UniversityEmail: albrighv@onid.oregonstate.edu', NULL, NULL, 859),
(1224, 339, 1920, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-07-15', 'Hello Bryan,I wanted to follow up and ask about the status of our questions. If our dataloggers have not been sent back yet please make sure they are sent back.', NULL, NULL, 859),
(1225, 339, 1920, 2, 0, NULL, '2015-07-15', 'Left Bryan Voicemail about receiving follow up questions.', NULL, NULL, 859),
(1226, 339, 1958, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-07-16', 'Yes, the dataloggers were sent back. They should have went out earlier this week so you should see them anytime now. Thanks,John', NULL, NULL, 859),
(1227, 339, 1958, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-07-16', 'Hello John,We recieved the dataloggers this morning. I have looked at the compressor data and saw that the compressor was down for a period on Sunday 7/5 through Monday 7/6. Was there a period of time where the compressor was running, but no pneumatic equipment was operating? If so could you provide me the time so I can asses the leak load of the facility.I also would like to ask again about the questions I sent on Monday. It seems Bryan is pretty busy, would you be able to provide any of the information we requested? Or direct us to the appropriate people to ask for this information?Thanks,Vincent', NULL, NULL, 859),
(1228, 339, 1958, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-07-20', 'Hello John,I still haven\'t received any of the following information.-Boiler feedwater treatment chemical usage and cost per unit-Motor List/Inventory (John said he could get this in an excel file)-Live amperage readings for the blower on line 5-Size of the condenser fan on the smaller evaporative condenser attached to Engine Room #1 (in hp)-Map of the plumbing in the facility-Inventory of pneumatic equipment (required pressures included)-Metering logs for the boiler gas use, water use and steam production-Operating hours for the following equipment          - T-30         - APV West         - Buffalo Vac         - Forecirc         - APV Eact         - Steralizer 1 (same side of the street as large boiler room)         - Steralizer 2 I also would like to know if there was there a period of time where the compressor was running while being datalogged, but no pneumatic equipment was operating? If so could you provide me the time so I can asses the leak load of the facility. If provided, I could also instead use the measured airflow reading off the air flow meter while no pneumatic equipment is running.If you could provide any of this information (even estimates) at your next convenience it would be greatly appreciated.Thank you,Vincent', NULL, NULL, 859),
(1229, 339, 1958, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-07-20', 'Vincent,I received your email. I will try to get back to you today with the requested information when I get back to the office.Thanks, JohnSent from my iPhone', NULL, NULL, 859),
(1230, 339, 1958, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-07-22', 'Hey John,Sorry to keep bugging you, but if it makes it easier to contact individuals at the facility regarding some of this information we could try contacting them instead. We would just need their contact information.Thanks,Vincent', NULL, NULL, 859),
(1231, 339, 1958, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-07-28', 'Hey John,Our team has been dillegently working on the report for your facility, but there is still some information that would help us in the . I have narrowed down the list of questions. -Boiler feedwater treatment chemical usage and cost per unit-Amperage readings for the blower on line 5-Metering logs for the boiler gas use, water use and steam production-Measured airflow reading off the air flow meter while no pneumatic equipment is running.I am also using 6336 annual operating hours for general equipment, provided that the facility runs close to 24/7 for four months, and 24 hours per day four five days per week for seven months. Let me know if this is a bad assumption.Any of this information (estimates included) are greatly appreciated.Thank you,Vincent', NULL, NULL, 859),
(1232, 332, 1976, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-07-28', 'A couple emails back and forth with Les. Les provided fan nameplate information, but I\'m still trying to ascertain where these fans operate on the fan curve in terms of percent flow. I asked him if there is any CFM metering.', NULL, NULL, 821),
