(1261, 347, 1990, 2, 0, NULL, '2015-08-07', 'Pre-assessment phone call.', NULL, NULL, 865),
(1262, 341, 1764, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-08-12', 'Brent,Sorry for the lack of communication. You said you would ask the maintenance crew about the development of three of our recommendations, did these ever get implemented? if so, when? or why not?Upgrade Compressed Air Controls :Convert the VFD controlled compressor to analog signal control and implement a VFD trim sequencing strategy to control the load on each compressor. These actions will reduce associated annual energy use by 87%.Insulate Condensate Return Pipe: Insulate 50 feet of condensate return piping, a pipe fitting located behind the glue manufacturing site, and the deaerator tank found next to the boiler with a fiberglass all service jacket. This will reduce heat loss from hot surfaces, lowering annual energy consumption by 3% per year.Install Dedicated Air Compressor: Install a dedicated air compressor for the dry fire sprinkler system to eliminate the operating hours of the 300 hp compressor on Sundays. This will reduce associated annual energy consumption by 1%.Lastly, if you could share the quotes for the Control Humidity in Facility recommendation that would be much appreciated.Thank you,Tyler GiddingsOperations ManagerEnergy Efficiency CenterOregon State University', NULL, NULL, 183),
(1264, 315, 1714, 1, 0, 11992, '2015-07-27', 'Brian\'s implementation report feedback:\"Hi Brad, Sorry for the delayed response. We have not implemented any of the recommendations at this time.We are in the process of looking at upgrading air compressor controls at both sites.The primary reason is that we have been busy upgrading the plant sites and upgrading controls packages and machinery. Thanks,Brian\"', NULL, 767, 827),
