(1276, 339, 1958, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-07-28', 'lease see attachments I have included the following items; Utility LogsMotor ListBoiler LogsChemical Pricing (the main usage is the 2103 which we go through a drum about every two weeks)Potable Water Line Maps Amperage Readings for Line 5 Blower and Air Knife (2 different pieces of equipment)                 Air Knife               BlowerT3           8.75                        4.30T2           9.35                        4.37T1           8.75                        3.75  The only information that I dont have is the Airflow, Size of the condenser fan on the smaller evap condenser attached to Engine Room #1, and the operating hours for the equipment listed out. If you resend the data logger we can make another attempt at capturing the air flow with no equipment operating.  Thanks, John BradleyTree Top, Inc.638 S. Grape St. Medford, OR 97501Phone: 541-842-8725  Cell: 541-292-1453John.Bradley@Treetop.com', NULL, NULL, 859),
(1277, 339, 1958, 1, 1, NULL, '2015-08-03', 'Hey John, I will send an extra data logger to try and capture your leak load. I will send a magnet to be placed on the compressor that is running with a reminder for the operators to keep the compressors on while pneumatic equipment is running. Could you also make sure to remind operators to leave the compressors running? I also have two questions about the high speed doors. First, what approximate time are they left open? we took a conservative guess of 5 hours per week, is this a fair estimated? Second, I wanted to verify that there are 5 high speed doors in the cold rooms, is this correct?Thanks,Vincent Albright', NULL, NULL, 859),
(1278, 339, 1958, 1, 1, NULL, '2015-08-03', 'Hey John,The Datalogger is being sent today in order to gather the compressed air leaks in the facility. Could you please make sure that there is a time period when the compressor is running while the pneumatic systems are turnded off. This will allow the compressor to only serve the compressed air leaks.Thank you,Vincent Albright', NULL, NULL, 859),
(1279, 353, 1997, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-08-12', 'Mr. Junker,Please see the attached completed forms for our business energy assessment.If you have any questions or comments please feel free to contact me.Regards,Dustin Houeland', NULL, NULL, 861),
