(1286, 353, 1941, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-08-31', 'Confirmed the 9th of October. New primary contact for pre-audit call is Dave Huntley. Setting teams tomorrow w/ Miles and plannign out next contact', NULL, NULL, 861),
(1287, 315, 1968, 2, 0, 11951, '2015-08-28', 'Cassandra returned my phone call, telling me that she passed the report and information to facility maintenance personnel. I returned her call and left a voicemail requesting that we complete this implementation report by the end of the fiscal year.', NULL, 749, 773),
(1288, 332, 1977, 2, 0, NULL, '2015-09-01', 'Called and left message to Mike. Emailed him, but email bounced back (was working fine before). Next step should probably be to call receptionist at facility and ask for him... perhaps he\'s moved on.', NULL, NULL, 807),
(1289, 353, 1937, 2, 0, NULL, '2015-09-01', 'Got ahold of Raymond and submitted the dates that he reported.', NULL, NULL, 823),
(1290, 346, 1751, 1, 0, 11954, '2015-09-02', 'I have emailed and left him a message Jacob that about the ARS and he replies within 6 hours.', NULL, 762, 760),
(1291, 353, 2019, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-09-04', 'Called Joel about our services and he informed me that ETO had been there within the past few months and expressed no interest in us coming.', NULL, NULL, 25),
(1292, 348, 1643, 2, 0, NULL, '2015-09-09', 'I called and scheduled a phone call with steve, I will be calling him on Tuesday September 15th to get feedback on the report ', NULL, -1, 687),
(1293, 321, 1977, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-09-15', 'Emailed Mike. Noted that Josh moved on, and I am handling the implementation. Sent him the implementation email. Awaiting response', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(1294, 321, 1727, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-09-15', 'Mike Griggs email was not available anymore, so I contacted Jodie Garlington. Hopefully she will give a response. ', NULL, NULL, 807),
(1295, 348, 1643, 2, 0, 11953, '2015-09-15', 'I contacted steve and got feedback of the report. He said that in the next few weeks (approximaltey 3) that the facility will be meeting with investors and potentially get more capital to increase the plants production hours and increase staff. He said if they receive more capitol they will look into the recommendations. I finished off the phone call by explaining that I will be calling in the months to come(in 6 months) to see if other recommendations were implemented. ', NULL, 752, 687),
(1296, 353, 1982, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-09-08', 'Hey Dale,One of our analysts is missing a few pieces of information on the Quincy air compressor. He has all of the compressor nameplate data but is looking for the motor nameplate data.If someone at your facility could provide us with the following it would be much appreciated:Motor RPMHorsepower ratingRated Voltage/AmperageEfficiencyOnce again, we are only looking for nameplate data for the motor. Our analyst has all of the compressor nameplate data but we don\'t know what motor is operating the compressor.Thanks,Ben', NULL, NULL, 864),
(1297, 353, 1982, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-09-01', 'Hey Dale,I have a few questions that would really help the recommendation writing process. If you could answer these or pass them on to someone else who can answer them as soon as possible it would be much appreciated.What are the current maintenance costs for all of the refrigeration rooftop units?Can you confirm that there is about 500 tons of refrigeration for the whole facility?Is there anyway to quantify the make-up water used in the boiler? Are steam production logs available? Anything about the boiler\'s feed water would be helpful.I hope to hear back from you soon,Ben', NULL, NULL, 864),
(1298, 321, 1977, 2, 0, NULL, '2015-09-16', 'Mike called me back, and we completed the implementation call. 2/5 AR\'s implemented. Spin off of 2. ', NULL, NULL, 807),
(1299, 354, 1989, 2, 0, NULL, '2015-09-18', 'Pre-audit call with PA and client.', NULL, NULL, 237),
(1300, 348, 1148, 2, 0, NULL, '2015-09-25', 'Talked to Mike Higgins, he said that corporate had sent an energy audit team 6-7 months ago to assess their plant. He said that they are not looking for an audit right now but might look into in a year or two. I sent in the information about the audit through email.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(1301, 348, 2041, 2, 0, NULL, '2015-09-25', 'Contacted the facility and asked for Tom DeCarlo. It turns out that he does not work there. However, I had a chance to talk to the Stephanie and wrote down her information. I also sent her information about the IAC assessment. She said that everything audit has to go through corporate first and that she will find out the right person to discuss this with. ', NULL, NULL, 66),
(1302, 348, 1148, 2, 0, NULL, '2015-09-25', 'Talked to Mike Higgins, he said that corporate had sent an energy audit team 6-7 months ago to assess their plant. He said that they are not looking for an audit right now but might look into in a year or two. I sent in the information about the audit through email.', NULL, NULL, 69),
(1303, 348, 1615, 2, 0, NULL, '2015-09-25', 'Contacted Scott Spencer and Sent in information about the assessment ', NULL, NULL, 758),
(1304, 353, 2050, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-09-29', 'Sent pre-audit letter and utility release request. ', NULL, NULL, 874),
(1305, 348, 2041, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-10-06', 'Stephanie Cross returned an email saying that they do not have the manpower resources to support this activity, that they would need to have one of their guys escort the group throughout the facility and they are unable to do so at the time. She also mentioned that the Plant Manager said it might be something that they would consider in the future and to keep them in our list of potential future opportunities. ', NULL, NULL, 66),
(1306, 353, 2050, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-10-06', 'Received utility release, utility bills, and all other pre-assessment data', NULL, NULL, 874);
INSERT INTO `ContactLog` (`ContactLogId`, `EmployeeId`, `PersonId`, `ContactTypeId`, `GrantId`, `TaskId`, `Date`, `Notes`, `LeadId`, `ProjectId`, `LocationId`) VALUES
(1307, 354, 2023, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-10-08', 'Hello!I have attached some questions from our analysts about the facility. Adam:Flash Steam RecoveryWhat is your estimated amount of hog fuel used annually?What is the price of dry hog fuel?Anthony:Notched V-BeltAttached is a spreadsheet given to me during our audit. Do you see any large hp motors that are not belt driven?Will an assumption of 70% of the total hp on that list (both the barker and the planar) be sufficient?Electric Forklift (5 propane forklifts used inside hardwood)Cost of propane?Average fuel use (gal/month, gal/year, ect.) for a forklift. A spreadsheet recording fueling would be beneficial if one is kept. Wet Hog FuelAn estimated required storage area of 300x400 ft was given to me by personnel. Is this a good assumption?We talked about a way to calculate savings from keeping the hog fuel dry. I have information regarding the dryer\'s annual usage. Would the amount of profit lost from waiting for fuel to dry be a good estimate? Or perhaps the cost to run the dryer on an annual basis? If we move forward using production loss I would also need an estimate regarding $$/hour of production.We may have more questions in the future but please respond to these at your earliest convenience.', NULL, NULL, 237),
(1308, 354, 2023, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-10-09', 'Russ,Have you guys had a chance to pull the Dataloggers from the hydraulics and the forced draft boiler fan?  I have attached an image of the list of Dataloggers we placed throughout the lumber facility during the assessment on 9/23.  Please mail those back to us whenever you get a chance.Regards,', NULL, NULL, 237),
(1309, 225, 1968, 2, 0, NULL, '2015-10-14', 'LVM re: Imp Report - Called back - Scott left May 20, 2014 - working at Timber Products now - up in Medford - might be able to get his contact info. ', NULL, NULL, 773),
(1310, 353, 1982, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-10-20', 'Called Dale and confirmed operation hours for the freezers. 35% of the time off.', NULL, NULL, 864),
(1311, 321, 473, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-10-26', 'Emailed Bruce and David with implementation data. Will follow up with call this week. ', NULL, NULL, 331),
(1312, 342, 2064, 2, 0, NULL, '2015-11-30', 'I called Ross to remind him about pulling out the data loggers. He said that the datloggers would be shipped tomorrow.', NULL, NULL, 861),
(1313, 353, 1670, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-12-15', 'Called and left voicemail and follow up email. need to get preassessment info still', NULL, NULL, 811),
(1314, 353, 2062, 2, 0, NULL, '2015-12-15', 'Called Arden and set audit date for January 7th 2016. He said he would follow up on the pre-assessment work. sending follow up email and setting team', NULL, NULL, 868),
(1315, 353, 2062, 1, 0, NULL, '2015-12-16', 'Left a voicemail and follow up email.Requested date change to Jan 14th or 15th.Reminded of preassessment info', NULL, NULL, 868),
(1316, 353, 2062, 2, 0, NULL, '2016-01-05', 'Reminded Arden of preassessment information. Should receive by tomorrow', NULL, NULL, 868),
(1317, 333, 2062, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-01-05', 'Emailed Arden to propose Friday Jan 8 at 10AM for the pre-assessment walk through phone call. ', NULL, NULL, 868),
(1318, 333, 2062, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-01-06', 'Received confirmation of walk-through call with Arden for Friday Jan 8th at 10 AM ', NULL, NULL, 868),
(1319, 353, 2062, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-01-07', 'Called Arden requesting pre-assessment paperwork. Left a voicemail and email.', NULL, NULL, 868),
(1320, 353, 1670, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-01-19', 'following production issues, there might be a possible reschedule. Waiting on response from Dathan to figure out when this might be.', NULL, NULL, 811),
(1321, 333, 2062, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-01-23', 'Arden,      I have attached a trip report which briefly summarizes our assessment and the opportunities that we have identified for further analysis. Our next step will be to further analyze these systems and determine the feasibility of improvement recommendations. Our final analysis should be complete in mid-March, after which we will deliver the report. Please feel free to email me with any questions or comments you may have regarding the report.           I will compile a list of followup questions that the team has in an email following this one.      If the data loggers have not yet been removed from the air compressors and the reheat furnace combustion air fan, they can be removed and shipped back to EEC.     Again, thank you for your time.', NULL, NULL, 868),
(1322, 333, 2062, 2, 0, NULL, '2016-02-01', 'Called Arden to ask about dataloggers and the follow up questions I emailed him on 1/23. He said the electricians will remove the loggers today and they will send them after. Arden also said he has some of the info we requested and may be able to email it today. ', NULL, NULL, 868),
(1323, 341, 1703, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-02-04', 'Paul,My name is Tyler Giddings and we just spoke on the phone about an energy assessment. We offer FREE energy and productivity assessments. A team of engineering students from OSU would visit your facility for one day, take copious notes and develop 5-10 recommendations that typically total hundreds of thousands of dollars in annual savings and pay back in about a year or two.I have attached relevant files that you will find helpful and go into further detail about the process.Also, we are available to schedule an assessment as early as the end of February based on your availability.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(1325, 341, 1703, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-02-04', 'Paul,My name is Tyler Giddings and we just spoke on the phone about an energy assessment. We offer FREE energy and productivity assessments. A team of engineering students from OSU would visit your facility for one day, take copious notes and develop 5-10 recommendations that typically total hundreds of thousands of dollars in annual savings and pay back in about a year or two.I have attached relevant files that you will find helpful and go into further detail about the process.Also, we are available to schedule an assessment as early as the end of February based on your availability.', NULL, NULL, 791),
(1326, 341, 1612, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-02-04', 'Initially contacted Alan Meyer the Pacific Power utility rep for contact information.', NULL, NULL, 876),
(1327, 353, 2068, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-02-04', 'Sent preassessment info today. Seemed very enthusiastic about proceeding with the audit', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(1328, 348, 2041, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-02-05', 'Stephanie Cross emailed back to express interest in an audit. I sent her a Industrial Pre-Assessment Form to fill out to determine the facilities eligibility. ', NULL, NULL, 66),
(1329, 333, 2062, 2, 0, NULL, '2016-02-05', 'Called Arden and checked the status of the data loggers again. Left message on voice mail requesting a tracking number', NULL, NULL, 868),
(1330, 333, 2062, 2, 0, NULL, '2016-02-08', 'Called Arden again to ask about the data loggers. Left voicemail and told him I\'d follow up with email. ', NULL, NULL, 868),
(1331, 333, 2062, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-02-09', 'Hi Arden, I\'m writing this afternoon just as a quick follow-up to my voicemail, in case you are away from the plant and not able to receive voice messages.  Our team has still not received the data loggers that we left on the air compressors and the combustion air fan for the reheat furnace. The data in those loggers is necessary to generate our report. We plan to deliver the report on time, but without that data doing so may be difficult.  If the loggers have shipped and there is a tracking number for the shipment, I\'d be glad to call UPS or Fedex to determine their whereabouts.  Thanks for your help,Scott Lindbloom ', NULL, NULL, 868),
(1332, 341, 1703, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-02-11', '\"Hi Paul,I hope you found the documents helpful. I was curious if you looked through the eligibility and have thought about a date that works for you? Thanks,\"Spoke to on phone as well. He will call back tomorrow with information.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(1333, 341, 2069, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-02-11', 'Contacted Bob over the phone. Says they are working with ETO and would not be interested in an energy assessment for a year or two.', NULL, NULL, 876),
(1334, 353, 2070, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-02-17', 'Left voicemail introducing us and explaining the service. Asked for him to call back.', NULL, NULL, 842),
(1335, 353, 1923, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-02-17', 'Left voicemail and sent follow up email with EEC brochure', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(1336, 341, 1649, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-02-17', 'Scott,My name is Tyler Giddings and I left you a voice-mail today about an OSU Energy Efficiency Center assessment. As I mentioned on the phone, the center has been in contact previously in August 2013. I see there were concerns about confidentiality and  if you have any questions I would like to address those concerns.We offer FREE energy and productivity assessments. A team of engineering students from OSU would visit your facility for one day, take copious notes and develop 5-10 recommendations that typically total hundreds of thousands of dollars in annual savings and pay back in about a year.We\'ve got some availability starting this April and going forward. I have also attached our Pre-Assessment document that has more information regarding the process.Best regards,', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(1337, 341, 2071, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-02-17', 'Contacted listed number and left a voicemail. First initial contact.', NULL, NULL, 721),
(1338, 341, 1703, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-02-24', '2/11: Hi Paul,I hope you found the documents helpful. I was curious if you looked through the eligibility and have thought about a date that works for you? --2/16: Hi Tyler, Sorry for not getting back to you last week.We had a significant power outage last week here at the Brewery and are still digging out. You are on my list and I will get back to you this week. Best regards,Paul--2/24: Hey Paul,Hope everything is back on track. I was wondering if you would like to set a time we can talk? I am free Thursday (Tomorrow) before 5. Next week I am available Wednesday, Thursday, and Friday any time.Let me know,', NULL, NULL, 791),
(1339, 225, 2068, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-02-26', 'Spring break assessment ? LVM - EM', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(1340, 341, 1921, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-03-02', 'Left a phone message. Email: Jon, Sean,My name is Tyler Giddings and I just spoke on the phone with Jon and left Sean a message about an OSU Energy Efficiency Center assessment. As I mentioned on the phone, you have previously been in contact with our center director Joe Junker and suggested waiting for the Summer of 2016 for an opening.As a reminder, we offer FREE energy and productivity assessments. A team of engineering students from OSU would visit your facility for one day, take copious notes and develop 5-10 recommendations that typically total hundreds of thousands of dollars in annual savings and pay back in about a year.We have lots of availability this summer in the month of July if that month works for you, let us know and we\'ll get you started with our process. Thanks for you interest and I hope it works out.Lastly, I have attached pre-assessment documents for each of your facilities. They contain further information on the process and if you have any questions please ask.Best Regards,Tyler Giddings', NULL, NULL, 550),
(1341, 341, 1926, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-03-02', 'Spoke to on phone. Email: Jon, Sean,My name is Tyler Giddings and I just spoke on the phone with Jon and left Sean a message about an OSU Energy Efficiency Center assessment. As I mentioned on the phone, you have previously been in contact with our center director Joe Junker and suggested waiting for the Summer of 2016 for an opening.As a reminder, we offer FREE energy and productivity assessments. A team of engineering students from OSU would visit your facility for one day, take copious notes and develop 5-10 recommendations that typically total hundreds of thousands of dollars in annual savings and pay back in about a year.We have lots of availability this summer in the month of July if that month works for you, let us know and we\'ll get you started with our process. Thanks for you interest and I hope it works out.Lastly, I have attached pre-assessment documents for each of your facilities. They contain further information on the process and if you have any questions please ask.Best Regards,Tyler Giddings', NULL, NULL, 549),
(1342, 341, 1926, 2, 0, NULL, '2016-03-10', 'Left a voicemail following up on previous email.', NULL, NULL, 549),
(1343, 341, 1921, 2, 0, NULL, '2016-03-10', 'Left a voicemail following up on previous email.', NULL, NULL, 550),
(1344, 341, 1703, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-03-10', 'HI Tyler, I talked this over with our Management team and have sent your info to Jennifer Olsen, our VP of Operations to coordinate your audit.Jen works directly with our Facilities team and we believe this will be the most direct pathway for your audit.Paul,Thank you very much. I will be expecting her email and I look forward to meeting all of you.', NULL, NULL, 791),
(1345, 341, 1799, 2, 0, NULL, '2016-03-10', 'Initial contact over phone. He will confirm a date we can speak next week.', NULL, NULL, 831),
(1346, 341, 1799, 2, 0, NULL, '2016-03-10', 'Initial contact over phone. He will confirm a date we can speak next week.', NULL, NULL, 831),
(1347, 333, 2066, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-03-11', 'Hi Robert,  We have finished our report of the assessment at your facility and I have attached it for your review.  In two weeks time we will be sending it to printing, so if there are any details you would like changed please let us know within that time.  Regards,Scott LindbloomOSU Energy Efficiency Center', NULL, NULL, 868),
(1348, 341, 1921, 2, 0, NULL, '2016-03-21', 'Spoke to Sean on the phone. Claims to be busy with operations and does not have time to commit to an energy assessment. I said we will contact them within a year or two to see if they are interested then. Sent an email as well to confirm with both Sean and Jon.', NULL, NULL, 550),
(1349, 341, 1926, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-03-21', 'Spoke to Sean on the phone. Claims to be busy with operations and does not have time to commit to an energy assessment. I said we will contact them within a year or two to see if they are interested then. Sent an email as well to confirm with both Sean and Jon.', NULL, NULL, 549),
(1350, 341, 1703, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-03-21', 'Contacted Paul Cook to get contact information for Jennifer Olsen. Email and phone voicemail. Apparently out of office till tomorrow.', NULL, NULL, 791),
(1351, 341, 2074, 2, 0, NULL, '2016-03-29', 'contacted by phone through the main line to initiate contact. Paul Cook does not work at Ninkasi anymore.', NULL, NULL, 791),
(1352, 225, 473, 2, 0, NULL, '2016-03-30', 'Imp call - got email with questions. Working way through. Been working on it. Apologies. Will call tomorrow early afternoon.', NULL, NULL, 331),
(1353, 225, 473, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-03-31', 'Bruce: Tied up today after all. What is a good time tomorrow. (I told him any time after 10:30)', NULL, NULL, 331),
(1354, 341, 1824, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-03-31', 'Called and left a voicemail but also sent an email of available times to meet next week.', NULL, NULL, 831),
(1355, 341, 2077, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-04-01', 'Miles, Our previous Plant Engineer, Bob Dalton, was trying to schedule an energy efficiency assessment for our plant last April.  Id like to coordinate this assessment for a date in the coming months.  Could you please send me more information about this assessment and list of dates? Thanks in advance. Regards,Emily BaumgartnerPlant EngineerKroger Swan Island Dairy4950 N. Basin Ave.Portland, OR 97217(503) 240-5167-----------Hello Emily,I can help you get started. I will provide some documentation tomorrow that will explain the process in detail. When I am back in the office Monday we will discuss available dates and go from there. Thank you for following up.-Tyler Giddings', NULL, NULL, 842),
(1356, 341, 2077, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-04-02', 'Sent Pre-assessment paperwork', NULL, NULL, 842),
(1357, 347, 473, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-02-15', 'I emailed him asking when would be a good time to have the implementation call. I did not get a response.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(1358, 347, 473, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-02-17', 'I called him to ask about the implementation call information. He told me he was working on it.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(1359, 347, 473, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-03-10', 'I emailed him again to talk about requesting a time to make the call. He did not respond.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(1360, 341, 2077, 2, 0, NULL, '2016-04-08', 'Emily,To highlight our conversation. We will shoot for the week of May 9th. Wednesday the 11th is not available. I will let you know what days my analysts are available to go and you will check in with your lead mechanic.Have a great weekend,', NULL, NULL, 842),
(1361, 353, 2080, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-04-13', 'Contacted about Pneumatic mixer info. Gave overall CFM but it doesn\'t match up with total use. Contacted back asking about percent total use he would estimate.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(1362, 225, 2081, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-04-14', '(His other phone number is : 206-464-3196) Located in North Creek Bothell. 350K sq ft facility. Working on \"258 Energy Program\" (a PSE program I think), spend upwards of $100k a month on energy. Wondering about alternate lower energy humidification instead of using a boiler: ultrasonic? Localized room by room?. Big energy users: presses, HVAC, compressed air, lighting. (Have T8s, considering LEDs. Have $179k to invest in energy projects.Sending PreAudit Doc. Told him we were looking at one of the last weeks of June, and would settle it once we find a third facility. ', NULL, NULL, 879),
(1363, 353, 2082, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-04-14', 'contacted about potential assessment ', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(1364, 341, 2077, 2, 0, NULL, '2016-04-19', 'Spoke to on phone and Monday is the best day to schedule the audit. Sent out an email trying to confirm a team and will follow up with collecting baseline.', NULL, NULL, 842),
(1365, 341, 2077, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-04-20', 'Emily,I called and left a voicemail but I wanted to confirm that Monday May 9th works for us. From this point going forward we are going to need to collect utility information so we can have a utility analysis prepared.Pavel Grechanuk, our Baseline Manager, will connect with you to get the last details he will need to collect your utility bills.Thank you,', NULL, NULL, 842),
(1366, 341, 2074, 2, 0, NULL, '2016-04-20', 'Called one last time to try and connect with Jennifer and see if they were interested. I got a main line voicemail so now waiting to see if there is a returned call. Cold for now.', NULL, NULL, 791),
(1367, 341, 2076, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-04-21', 'Nick,My name is Tyler Giddings and I left you a voice-mail today about an OSU Energy Efficiency Center assessment. As I mentioned on the phone, we\'ve learned about you through David Kunz. He recommended you to us as a good fit for the type of assessments we do.We offer FREE energy and productivity assessments. A team of engineering students from OSU would visit your facility for one day, take copious notes and develop 5-10 recommendations that typically total hundreds of thousands of dollars in annual savings and pay back in about a year.We\'ve got some availability in late June and July if those general times work for you, let us know and we\'ll get you started with our process. Thanks for your interest and I hope it works out.Best Regards,', NULL, NULL, 878),
(1368, 346, 1808, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-04-21', 'I have left them a message and an email to let them know why we are contacting them', NULL, NULL, 835),
(1369, 346, 1289, 2, 0, 11955, '2016-04-21', 'I have contacted mike and he is willing to set up a phone call. However since he has to get the information it would be better to answer through email. I have sent him an email with the questions. Now he will try to get us the response as soon as possible. Then, if I have anymore questions, we could set up a call to talk about it.', NULL, 790, 840),
(1370, 341, 2074, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-04-21', 'Hi Tyler,Yes, Ninkasi would be interested in the energy assessment.  Im currently hiring a Sustainability Coordinator and hope to have that person in place by 5/16.  I would like to schedule a date after that so that person can participate.  Whats your time frame like?Jen------------Jennifer,That is great to hear and we are very excited to help out.Our time-frame is highly flexible planning later out. For our earlier openings we have a trip the week of June 27th.  We would be visiting two other facilities so the day of the week may not be as flexible. We also have plenty of openings in July for day trips and the day of the week is very flexible.When I am back in the office I will send you more information on the program.Thank you,', NULL, NULL, 791),
(1371, 341, 2074, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-04-21', 'Jennifer,Here is the pre-assessment form that contains information on the process and has some fields for you to fill out. If you have any questions feel free to ask.Regards,', NULL, NULL, 791),
(1372, 348, 1819, 2, 0, -1, '2016-04-06', 'Called the facility and left a voicemail because no one picked up. ', NULL, 791, 839),
(1373, 348, 1819, 1, 0, -1, '2016-04-06', 'Sent out an email with the list of recommendations to get feedback', NULL, 791, 839),
(1374, 348, 1819, 2, 0, -1, '2016-04-22', 'Called the facility to ask about the feeback progress of the recommendations. I ended up leaving a voicemail because no one would answer. ', NULL, 791, 839),
(1375, 353, 2050, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-04-25', 'Set up longer call for Wednesday the 27th. Will discuss the process of working with a lead and sending early dataloggers.', NULL, NULL, 874),
(1376, 347, 1816, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-04-26', 'Jack,I would like to get feedback from you on the Energy Assessment Report prepared for Carestream Health by the Oregon State University Energy Efficiency Center. The site assessment was conducted on June 29th 2015 and the report should have been mailed to you approximately two months after the site assessment. Please send me your best contact number and let me know when would be a good time for me to call you in the next several days to discuss your overall experience with our report as well as the recommendation specific questions listed below. Feel free to respond to these specific questions via email if that will work best for you.Specific Feedback for each Recommendation:Did you implement it? When did you implement it? Did you save more or less than we estimated? How much more/less? Did is cost more or less than we estimated? How much more/less? Did you receive any incentives to help pay for the project? What was your overall experience? Did you choose not to implement it? Why not? Did it cost too much? Did you disagree with our analysis? Have you not had staff available? When we speak on the phone I will be looking for more general feedback on the assessment we performed for you. I will be asking questions similar to the ones listed below. General Feedback: Was the report helpful? Was it easy or hard to read? Did our visit or report influence you to take any actions other than those we recommended? Did any actions you took extend to other sister plants? Can you offer any constructive criticism about our process? If you have any questions about this email, please dont hesitate to contact me. I look forward to discussing this matter with you in the near future. Thanks in advance for your feedback! If I do not hear from you before tomorrow afternoon, I will give you a call Thursday afternoon around 1:30.Megan O\'LearyOregon State UniversityEnergy Efficiency Center971.241.5577', NULL, NULL, 821),
(1377, 225, 2081, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-04-14', 'Sent pre-audit doc to client', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(1378, 347, 1816, 2, 0, NULL, '2016-04-28', 'I called him and he was in a meeting so he needed to get back to me about a day for implementation.', NULL, NULL, 821),
(1379, 346, 1916, 1, 0, 12108, '2016-04-28', 'I called and left a message with an email reminder', NULL, 794, 856),
(1380, 341, 2088, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-04-28', 'Jeanne,I just left a voicemail but we are looking to set a date for an energy assessment. We are available as early as the week of July 11th. We will be scheduling out as far as August 1st for this Summer. Since it is Summer we are normally highly flexible for the day of the week as well. If you could let me know what week you are interested in and the best days of that week we can get you on the calendar.Thank you,', NULL, NULL, 884),
(1381, 341, 2074, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-05-01', 'Jennifer,After talking with my management team it is looking like the week of July 25th would be the best week for us to schedule an assessment. Let me know if this works for your facility, otherwise we can find another solution.', NULL, NULL, 791),
(1382, 341, 2074, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-05-02', 'Hello,That week should work.  How long will the assessment take?Jen-------------Jennifer,That is great to hear, I have you scheduled in. If you know a day of the week that works best for you and your facility let me know.The assessment takes 1 day and I have detailed below what the day looks like and who we will need to have an effective assessment:8am: We arrive.8-8:30: We do introductions, safety, and a quick kickoff meeting8:30-10: Tour of facility. We need someone who is knowledgeable of the process and key energy users.10-11: Brainstorm. Helpful to have someone from the facility to bounce questions off of.11-11:30: Lunch11:30-12: Set up data collection plans12-3/3:30: Data collection. We will need someone who can open electrical boxes for live readings and such. Also we like to have more than one team so hopefully we can have a couple of maintenance people to help (based on the nature and size of your operation it may not be as applicable to have two). We also go to talk to key personnel who have information we need.3:30-4 Closeout meeting and discuss findings. Important to have someone who is knowledgeable of the process here.Lastly, I have attached the pre-assessment information. Once you fill that out we can begin our baseline analysis.', NULL, NULL, 791),
(1383, 341, 1799, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-05-02', 'Called and Emailed-----Bill,I just left you a message, I would like to find a time that works for both of us to complete the implementation call. I need to have it completed and submitted in the next three weeks. My availability the next three weeks is as follows:Monday: 8:00 am-2:00 pmWednesday: 3:00 pm-6:00 pmThursday: 8:00 am-12:00 pmFriday: All DayHere is a quick summary of the recommendations:1. Insulate Lime Kiln  Savings: $219,206 - Implementation: $131,5382. Install Dissolved Oxygen Monitors - Savings: $53,670 - Implementation: $26,7763. Replace Centrifugal Compressor - Savings: $93,377 - Implementation: $176,4964. Improve Lighting Efficiency - Savings: $17,419 - Implementation - $69,3065. Implement Air Blower Agitation - Savings: $10,636 - Implementation: $8,8126.Install VFD on Boiler Fan - Savings: $28,356 - Implementation: $245,000Thank you,', NULL, NULL, 831),
(1384, 347, 2077, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-05-03', 'Emily, My name is Megan O\'Leary and I am contacting you on behalf of the Oregon State Energy Efficiency Center.  I will be the lead for the assessment taking place at your facility on May 9th. The principal auditor will be Joe Junker, and we will be accompanied by a group of energy analysts whom you will be introduced to on the day of the visit.I am contacting you to see about setting up a pre-assessment phone call with you or another employee that you believe would be able to provide us with information about the facility.  I would like to ask some questions about the process that goes on in your facility so I can get an idea of what our team will be assessing.The topics I will be asking about include:-The process that your facility uses-Which machines are the biggest consumers of energy-What opportunities you would like us to focus on during the visit-The logistics of the visit (such as when we shall arrive and who our main contact will be during the tour.)I will have a few other questions, but the phone call should take only 30 minutes to an hour to complete.I would be free to have this phone call anytime after 12 pm on Wednesday the 4th and after 12 pm on Friday the 6th.  If possible, I would like to have the phone call done as soon as possible so I can meet with my team before the assessment.Please respond and give me a time and a way to contact you or another employee so I will be able to call with Joe and go over the information stated above.Thank you in advance,Megan O\'LearyEnergy Efficiency CenterOregon State University971.241.5577', NULL, NULL, 842),
(1385, 347, 2077, 2, 0, NULL, '2016-05-04', 'I called and left a voicemail regarding the pre-assessment phonecall.', NULL, NULL, 842),
(1386, 343, 1821, 1, 0, 11994, '2016-05-03', 'Directed me to a new contact who I emailed acook@bbumail.com. ', NULL, 783, 832),
(1387, 347, 2077, 2, 0, NULL, '2016-05-05', 'Called and left a voicemail.', NULL, NULL, 842),
(1388, 347, 1990, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-05-11', 'Mike,I would like to get feedback from you on the Energy Assessment Report prepared for Trident Bellingham by the Oregon State University Energy Efficiency Center. The site assessment was conducted on August 8th 2015 and the report should have been mailed to you approximately two months after the site assessment. Please send me your best contact number and let me know when would be a good time for me to call you in the next several days to discuss your overall experience with our report as well as the recommendation specific questions listed below. Feel free to respond to these specific questions via email if that will work best for you.Specific Feedback for each Recommendation:Did you implement it? When did you implement it? Did you save more or less than we estimated? How much more/less? Did is cost more or less than we estimated? How much more/less? Did you receive any incentives to help pay for the project? What was your overall experience? Did you choose not to implement it? Why not? Did it cost too much? Did you disagree with our analysis? Have you not had staff available? When we speak on the phone I will be looking for more general feedback on the assessment we performed for you. I will be asking questions similar to the ones listed below. General Feedback: Was the report helpful? Was it easy or hard to read? Did our visit or report influence you to take any actions other than those we recommended? Did any actions you took extend to other sister plants? Can you offer any constructive criticism about our process? If you have any questions about this email, please dont hesitate to contact me. I look forward to discussing this matter with you in the near future. Thanks in advance for your feedback! If I do not hear from you before tomorrow afternoon, I will give you a call Friday afternoon around 1.Megan O\'LearyOregon State UniversityEnergy Efficiency Center971.241.5577', NULL, NULL, 865),
(1389, 347, 1816, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-05-18', 'Jack, I am contacting you again to see about setting up a time to talk about the assessment recommendations. Could you please check your schedule and find an open time to talk for 30-45 minutes depending on your feedback?Thanks, ', NULL, NULL, 821),
(1390, 347, 1990, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-05-18', 'Mike, I am emailing you again to see about getting the last information needed to complete my report. It can be found in the last email, a lot of it is just confirming dates (even if they are your best estimate!) and confirming savings/implementation costs.Thank you, Megan O\'LearyEnergy AnalystOSU Energy Efficiency Center971.241.5577', NULL, NULL, 865),
(1391, 341, 2076, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-05-25', 'Hello Nick,I am looking to touch base again. I see that we missed setting up a phone call. If you would still like to do that let me know your available times. Also, I would like to retrieve the Pre-Assessment work and set a date for the week of July 18th so we can take care of logistics on our end.', NULL, NULL, 878),
(1392, 341, 2074, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-05-25', 'Hello Jennifer,I would like to touch base again. I hope you have been able to hire your Sustainability Coordinator so we can connect with them. Also, I would like to retrieve the Pre-Assessment work and set a date the week of July 25th. Looking forward to hearing back from you.', NULL, NULL, 791),
(1393, 341, 2088, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-05-25', 'Hello Jeanne,I wanted to follow up with you to let you know we are still working on assigning our leads. Also, we would like to set a date during the week of 7/11 that works best for you. This way we can reserve our van and take care of any necessary logistics beforehand.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(1395, 349, 1938, 2, 0, NULL, '2016-05-06', 'I called John to ask for his feedback on our recommendations but he was out of town. I left him a voicemail.', NULL, NULL, 860),
(1396, 341, 2116, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-06-27', 'Hello Steve,My name is Tyler Giddings and I left you a voicemail today about an OSU Energy Efficiency Center assessment. As I mentioned on the phone, weve learned about you through your utility representative at the Clark Public Utilities, Zeecha Van Hoose. She recommended you to us as a good fit for the type of assessments we do.We offer FREE energy and productivity assessments. A team of engineering students from OSU would visit your facility for one day, take copious notes and develop several recommendations that typically total hundreds of thousands of dollars in annual savings and pay back in about a year.We were told SAPA has two facilities between Portland and Vancouver. The forms I have sent you have been started for SAPA Portland and Vancouver and include additional information about what we offer. Weve got some availability in the Fall beginning the week of September 26th, let us know and well get you started with our process. Thanks for your interest and I hope it works out.Best Regards,', NULL, NULL, 890),
(1397, 341, 2088, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-06-27', 'Jeanne,I wanted to confirm from our conversation the date for our assessment will be Thursday July 14th. Megan, the report lead, will be in contact with you shortly.Have a great day,', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(1398, 341, 2076, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-06-27', 'Nick,I would like to confirm that the date of Tuesday July 19th is available for the assessment. Also, if you could please return the Pre-Assessment Form that would be much appreciated. We will begin on the utility analysis right after. We have set Hari Nagarajan as the Report Lead. He will be getting in contact with you shortly.', NULL, NULL, 878),
(1399, 349, 1938, 2, 0, NULL, '2016-06-27', 'I called John and he said that he has no information on the implementation numbers as he was in Westport for the last one year. But I have set up another phone appointment with him on 5th of July at around 3:30 pm so that he\'ll have some more information on it.', NULL, NULL, 860),
(1400, 348, 1966, 2, 0, 12495, '2016-06-22', 'Called facility and scheduled an phone call appointment with Nathan for June 28th @ 9am. ', NULL, 781, 545),
(1401, 348, 1966, 2, 0, 12495, '2016-06-28', 'Contacted Nathan but he was unable to follow through with the phone call appointment because of he had to tend to some facility issues. He rescheduled the phone call for July 6th, 2016 @ 8am. ', NULL, 781, 545),
(1402, 341, 2118, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-06-28', 'Hi Tyler, Wednesday the 27th works for me.  Who all should be involved in this assessment? Ive attached a few maps, as well as an asset list.  Im not sure what all information you would like for equipment, I just sorted out some of obvious things I thought would be out of scope (like computers, small equipment and piping).  Ill send you a second email with a previous assessment done by the U of O.  There are a bunch of files with that one. Let me know if theres anything else I can help gather before the assessment. Cheers!', NULL, NULL, 791),
(1403, 341, 2118, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-06-28', 'Kristi,Great! I look forward to July 27th. Also, thank you for providing this additional information. We will assign a Report Lead shortly and they will get in contact with you and schedule a pre-assessment phone call to learn about your operation and discuss the logistics of the assessment. The team will include a faculty adviser and a group of 4-7 student analysts. We will need an electrician or two who can open boxes and take live readings for us. Below is a typical breakdown of our agenda and who is needed throughout the day.8am: We arrive.8-8:30: We do introductions, safety, and a quick kickoff meeting8:30-10: Tour of facility. We need someone who is knowledgeable of the process and key energy users.10-11: Brainstorm. Helpful to have someone from the facility to bounce questions off of.11-11:30: Lunch11:30-12: Set up data collection plans12-3/3:30: Data collection. We will need someone who can open electrical boxes for live readings and such. Also we like to have more than one team so hopefully we can have a couple of maintenance people to help (based on the nature and size of your operation it may not be as applicable to have two). We also go to talk to key personnel who have information we need.3:30-4 Closeout meeting and discuss findings. Important to have someone who is knowledgeable of the process here.Thank you,Tyler GiddingsOperations ManagerEnergy Efficiency CenterOregon State University', NULL, NULL, 791),
(1404, 341, 2076, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-06-28', 'Tyler,We are still good for the 19th.  Actually, I have my administrative assistant working on the assessment info for you as we speak, so you should have it this week.  Let me know if you need anything else.          Nick,Great! That is all we need for now.', NULL, NULL, 878),
(1405, 346, 2119, 1, 0, 11994, '2016-06-28', 'Adam has repoonded with: (he seems a little annoyed)I have responded back with . The compressed air leaks have been fixed and is something we try to stay on top off.The exhauster VFD has not been installed due to possible change in air flow and low priority right now.The other one I believe was the glycol system vfd which was installed. Thank you Adam CookMaintenance Manager10750 SW 5th StBeaverton, OregonCell 785-409-3608ACook@bbumail.com', NULL, 783, 832),
(1406, 225, 2120, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-06-29', 'I emailed and he called back. Wants to sell assessment to facility folks. ', NULL, NULL, 883),
(1407, 346, 1982, 1, 0, 12487, '2016-06-29', 'I have called dale, and he said he needs some time to contact his team to see if there are anything are is implemented. I sent him an email with the template.', NULL, 803, 864),
(1408, 349, 1938, 2, 0, NULL, '2016-07-05', 'I called Pacific Seafood and was told that John doesn\'t work there anymore. I was then directed to Mike Fissette and he said that none of the recommendations were implemented but couldn\'t say for sure. ', NULL, NULL, 860),
(1409, 348, 1966, 2, 0, 12495, '2016-07-06', 'Got in touch with Nathan and received recommendation feedback for both the particle board and plywood facility. :)', NULL, 781, 545),
(1410, 341, 2116, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-07-07', 'Called and left a voicemail about calling tomorrow.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(1411, 341, 1747, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-07-07', 'Left a voicemail about calling again tomorrow morning.', NULL, NULL, 890),
(1412, 341, 2124, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-07-07', 'Bonnie,Hello, my name is Tyler Giddings and I received your request for an OSU Energy Efficiency Center assessment.We offer FREE energy and productivity assessments. A team of engineering students from OSU would visit your facility for one day, take copious notes and develop several recommendations that typically total hundreds of thousands of dollars in annual savings and pay back in about a year.We have availability come September. Also, we have offered a spot to another facility for the week of August 1st this Summer that has not been confirmed. I will let you know if this spot opens up if you would like to go sooner.I have attached our pre-assessment form to this email. Please fill it out and return it so we can begin on our baseline analysis to prepare us for the assessment. It also provides you information about the center and our process. Thanks for your interest and I hope it works out.Best Regards,', NULL, NULL, 83),
(1413, 341, 2116, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-07-08', 'Hello again Steve,I called and left a voicemail yesterday and was wondering if you were interested in an EEC energy assessment. Please let me know if this is something you would like to consider soon or in the future.Thanks,', NULL, NULL, 882),
(1414, 341, 2116, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-07-08', 'Tyler, Yes, we are interested.  I am in the process of gathering information for Pre-Assessment Form.  How detailed do you want this project to be?  We have the one plant in Vancouver and four plants in Portland.  We also have some significant waste streams in Portland. STEVE NELSON', NULL, NULL, 882),
(1415, 341, 2116, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-07-08', 'Steve,That is great to hear! That is also a good question. I know we have some limitations on how many facilities from the same company we can assess. The biggest restriction is that the facility needs to have above $100,000 in combined electricity and natural gas consumption. However, we obviously would like to start with the facilities you believe have the biggest opportunity. I will discuss this with our Center Director when he comes back from a trip Wednesday and follow up with you.', NULL, NULL, 882),
(1416, 341, 2116, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-07-08', 'We have about $3,680,000 in combined gas/electric for all five buildings.   $1,500,000        Main Plant$   940,000        Riverside$   560,000        Coatings$   530,000        Vancouver$   150,000        Fabrication STEVE NELSON', NULL, NULL, 882),
(1417, 341, 2116, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-07-08', 'Steve,They definitely would all be eligible. We should probably start at the top of the pecking order (the more energy consumption the more available savings) or based on what facility would be available for this Fall. If you would please fill out the Pre-Assessment form for that facility and I will get back to you Wednesday after I talk to our Director.I look forward to getting these set up,', NULL, NULL, 882),
(1418, 341, 1993, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-07-08', 'Hi Jon,I am following up on a voice mail I just left you. I would like to get feedback from you on the Assessment Report prepared for Weyerhaeuser - Santiam by the Oregon State University Energy Efficiency Center (a U.S.DOE Industrial Assessment Center). This is the final requirement in our contract with U.S. Department of Energy who funds these assessments.Feel free to respond to these questions via email or phone or, if you prefer, suggest a good time for me to give you call. Although, we would really appreciate if you could provide your feedback before 07/29/2016.Basically we\'re asking for: 1) Specific feedback on each of the recommendations we madeDid you implement it?                 If so: What should I list as the implementation date? (an estimate of the date is fine)What was your experience?  Did you save more or less than we estimated? Did it cost more or less?                If not:  Why not? (Did it cost too much?  Did you disagree with our analysis?  Have you not had staff available?  Etc.)2) General feedback on the assessment we performed for youWas it helpful?  Was the report easy or hard to read?  Did our visit or report influence you to take any other actions than those we recommended?  Did any actions you took extend to other sister plants?  I will be interested in any constructive criticism you can offer.Here is a summary of the recommendations. I will be following up in a separate email with a copy of the report.Assessment RecommendationsAR #TitleEnergy Savings (MMBtu)Annual Cost SavingsTotal CostPayback (Years)IncentiveNet CostNet Payback (Years)1Convert Stacker Hydraulics379.37$41,305.0$130,0003.1$27,796$102,2042.52Control Hydraulic Tank Heaters0.00$15,820.0$2,5000.2$0$2,5000.23Install Notched V-Belts262.24$7,567.0$00.0$0$00.04Increase Baghouse Efficiency119.21$2,998.0$8640.3$0$8640.35Reduce Compressed Air Leaks389.71$5,683.0$6,6831.2$0$6,6831.26Reduce Saw Test Operation Time76.90$1,080.0$3020.3$0$3020.37Install LED Lighting867.22$15,058.0$70,5684.7$3,416$67,1524.5AR No. 1, Convert Stacker Hydraulics .Convert the hydraulic system controlling the stacker mechanism to an electric linear actuator. This will prevent the safety hazard created by hydraulic fluid leaking, and reduce the annual associated maintenance cost, and annual energy consumption of the stacker mechanism by 60%.AR No. 2, Control Hydraulic Tank Heaters.Install automatic controls on all hydraulic tank heaters in the facility to reduce unnecessary wear to system components, minimize improper operation, and prevent additional stoppages due to insufficient warm-up, increasing associated annual production by 0.1%.AR No. 3, Install Notched V-Belts.Upgrade all belt driven motors to notched V-belts as standard V-belts need replacement. The use of notched V-belts will reduce motor energy use by approximately 2% through improved transmission efficiency. AR No. 4, Increase Baghouse Efficiency.Increase the dust collection system\'s (DCS) baghouse efficiency to reduce associated annual energy consumption by 5.0% and maintenance costs by 47.5%.AR No. 5, Reduce Compressed Air Leaks.Reduce the compressed air system leak load, or minimum sustained air flow, from 373 acfm (51% of peak, non-leak plant demand) to 221 acfm (30% of peak, non-leak plant demand). Maintaining this leak load will decrease associated annual energy use by 19%.AR No. 6, Reduce Saw Test Operation Time.Manually test saw blade alignment after blade changes on the band mill to reduce associated annual energy consumption by 100%.AR No. 7, Install LED Lighting.Install LED lighting throughout the facility. This will increase lighting efficiency, reducing associated annual energy consumption by 1%. Thanks in advance for your feedback!Best regards,', NULL, NULL, 819),
(1419, 341, 1993, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-07-08', 'Attached is a copy of the report.', NULL, NULL, 819),
(1420, 341, 1992, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-07-08', 'Hi Rick,I am following up on a voice mail I just left you. I would like to get feedback from you on the Assessment Report prepared for Pennington Crossarm by the Oregon State University Energy Efficiency Center (a U.S.DOE Industrial Assessment Center). This is the final requirement in our contract with U.S. Department of Energy who funds these assessments.Feel free to respond to these questions via email or phone or, if you prefer, suggest a good time for me to give you call. Although, we would really appreciate if you could provide your feedback before 07/29/2016.Basically we\'re asking for: 1) Specific feedback on each of the recommendations we madeDid you implement it?                 If so: What should I list as the implementation date? (an estimate of the date is fine)What was your experience?  Did you save more or less than we estimated? Did it cost more or less?                If not:  Why not? (Did it cost too much?  Did you disagree with our analysis?  Have you not had staff available?  Etc.)2) General feedback on the assessment we performed for youWas it helpful?  Was the report easy or hard to read?  Did our visit or report influence you to take any other actions than those we recommended?  Did any actions you took extend to other sister plants?  I will be interested in any constructive criticism you can offer.Here is a summary of the recommendations. I will be following up in a separate email with a copy of the report.Assessment RecommendationsAR #TitleEnergy Savings (MMBtu)Annual Cost SavingsTotal CostPayback (Years)IncentiveNet CostNet Payback (Years)1Insulate Boiler138.00$1,318.0$1,0100.8$0$1,0100.82Insulate Kiln Doors116.50$11,122.0$13,0821.2$6,541$6,5410.63Install Water Atomization196.00$1,876.0$3,5351.9$1,767$1,7680.94Install LED Lighting588.09$15,563.0$87,3195.6$24,130$63,1894.15Convert Hydraulics to Electric Motors117.54$4,497.0$38,3938.5$13,438$24,9555.5AR No. 1, Insulate Boiler.Insulate the boiler with ridgid board insulation to reduce heat loss from hot surfaces, lowering annual energy consumption by 4% per year. AR No. 2, Insulate Kiln Doors.Insulate kiln doors with fiber board insulation to reduce heat loss from door and door seals, lowering annual energy consumption by 34% per year. AR No. 3, Install Water Atomization.Install an atomization system in the kilns. This will eliminate direct steam injection, reducing boiler energy consumption by 7.3%.AR No. 4, Install LED Lighting.Install LED lighting and occupancy sensors. This will increase lighting efficiency and reduce operating hours, reducing associated annual energy consumption by 71%. AR No. 5, Convert Hydraulics to Electric Motors.Replace the hydraulic pumps and motors used on the conveyor systems in the facility with electric premium efficiency motors. This will increase conveyor system efficiencies by 53% and reduce associated annual energy consumption by 58%. Thanks in advance for your feedback!Best regards,Tyler Giddings', NULL, NULL, 867),
(1421, 341, 1992, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-07-08', 'Attached is a copy of the report.', NULL, NULL, 867),
(1422, 341, 2116, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-07-14', 'Steve,****Also left voicemail****I spoke with our center director and he said we could set energy assessments up for two facilities in the near future. We would like to start with the Vancouver facility so we can include Clark PUD as part of the process. If you then want to decide on which facility you want to include as well. We can work on getting to the rest of the facilities as time goes on but for the mean time lets focus on two.', NULL, NULL, 882);
INSERT INTO `ContactLog` (`ContactLogId`, `EmployeeId`, `PersonId`, `ContactTypeId`, `GrantId`, `TaskId`, `Date`, `Notes`, `LeadId`, `ProjectId`, `LocationId`) VALUES
(1423, 341, 2124, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-07-20', 'Bonnie,I left you a voicemail and it turns out the slot for the week of August 1st-August 5th is now available for an assessment. We would like to offer that slot to Duraflake. Going forward we will need to set a date that week for our team to come and perform our energy assessment. It looks like you marked every day of the week as a good day. I would like to propose Wednesday August 3rd. We prefer to do our assessments on days that are likely the most representative of production.We will also need your utility account info and utility release information so we can prepare our utility analysis before the day of the assessment.Thank you,', NULL, NULL, 83),
(1424, 341, 2124, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-07-20', 'Bonnie,I wanted to summarize our phone conversation and provide you some additional information before the assessment day. Tuesday August 9th is the proposed date for the assessment. I have also assigned Megan O\'Leary as the Lead Analyst for your facility. She will be contacting you to set up a Pre-Assessment phone call.We will need the utility info to begin our utility analysis shortly.Here is quick breakdown of our process:8:00 am we typically arrive.8:15-30 we do introductions, safety, and a quick kickoff meeting8:30-10: Tour of facility. We need someone who is knowledgeable of the process and key energy users.10-11: Brainstorm. Helpful to have someone from the facility to bounce questions off of.11-11:30: Lunch11:30-12: Set up data collection plans12-3/3:30: Data collection. We will need someone who can open electrical boxes for live readings and such. Also we like to have more than one team so hopefully we can have a couple of maintenance people to help. We also go to talk to key personnel who have information we need.3:30-4 Closeout meeting and discuss findings. Important to have someone who is knowledgeable of the process here.Let me know if this date works and if you need any additional information.', NULL, NULL, 83),
(1425, 356, 2118, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-07-20', 'Hi Kristi,My name is Hari Nagarajan, Operations mangers at the Energy Efficiency Center at OSU, and I will be leading the assessment on 27th July, 2016.We would like to set up a 30 min. conference call with you to familiarize ourselves with Ninkasi. During this phone call, Joseph Junker, Principal Auditor of the assessment, and myself will introduce the program to you and respond to any questions you may have. On our end, some of the information that we would like to obtain from the conversation is the following:Ninkasi process flow and operations.Significant energy uses.Issues or concerns that are most important to Ninkasi.Rough estimates of annual sales, employees, facility surface area, main product/products and quarterly produced, and operation hours per year.Equipment specifications such as but not limited to total motor HP, max motor HP, steam capacity/pressure, air compressor HP/ pressure, etc.The main contact for the day of the assessment.Feel free to invite anyone you believe may be helpful to participate in the call as well.Our preference for the phone call is anytime between 11 am to 12 pm Thursday(07/21) , and 2.30 pm - 5 pm Thursday(07/21), 11 am - 5 pm Friday (07/22). Although, if this time frame does not fit your schedule, we could work around a different time, maybe Monday (07/25) (10 am - 5pm).We look forward to working with Ninkasi.', NULL, NULL, 791),
(1426, 356, 2118, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-07-20', 'Hi Kristi,As a follow up to my previous email, I wanted to introduce the team that will perform the energy assessment as well as the utility and energy representatives who might be joining us for the day. The student team for the day would consist of:1. Joseph Junker (Principal Auditor)2. Hari Nagarajan (Assessment Lead)3. Tyler Giddings (Energy Analyst)4. Megan O\' Leary (Energy Analyst)5. Keith Striby (Energy Analyst)6. Landon Fox (Energy Analyst)7. Alberto Pezzani ( Energy Analyst)8. Even Talan (Energy Analyst)9. Additionally, we have a representative from the U.S Department of Energy(they pay for these assessments), Mr. Eli Levine who will join us to oversee the work performed by the OSU IAC team.Also, as per your permission, we have invited utility representatives Mr. Josh Ruddick from EWEB and Mr. Tom Simpson from NW Natural to join us during our assessment. We do not know if they will join us or not.Another opportunity that has surfaced recently through the center\'s collaboration with the Bonneville Power Administration\'s Energy Smart Industrial program is to have one of their Engineers join us during energy audits. ESI offers incentives for energy projects which might be helpful for your facility when implementing any recommendations we make during the assessment. Let me know if you would be interested in us inviting an ESI Engineer for the assessment.  Thank You', NULL, NULL, 791),
(1427, 356, 1701, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-07-20', 'Hi Josh,My name is Hari Nagarajan, Operations Manager at the OSU Industrial Assessment Center. We have set up an energy assessment with Ninkasi Brewing on Wednesday (07/27) and it would be nice to have you join us during the assessment. Just to run you through the agenda for the day:1) Arrive at facility at 8 AM.2) Kickoff and Safety orientation till 8.30 AM.3) Facility Walk-through (roughly 1 hr -1.5hrs)4) Brainstorm opportunities + Lunch ( Multi-task) (1 hr)5) Rank opportunities 6) Collect data 7) Debrief The process usually ends around 4-5 PM. Let me know if you or anyone else from EWEB would be able to make it. Thank you', NULL, NULL, 791),
(1428, 356, 2137, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-07-20', 'Hi Tom, My name is Hari Nagarajan, Operations Manager at the OSU Industrial Assessment Center. We have set up an energy assessment with Ninkasi Brewing on Wednesday (07/27) and it would be nice to have you join us during the assessment. Just to run you through the agenda for the day:1) Arrive at facility at 8 AM.2) Kickoff and Safety orientation till 8.30 AM.3) Facility Walk-through (roughly 1 hr -1.5hrs)4) Brainstorm opportunities + Lunch ( Multi-task) (1 hr)5) Rank opportunities 6) Collect data 7) Debrief The process usually ends around 4-5 PM. Let me know if you or anyone else from NW Natural would be able to make it. Thank you', NULL, NULL, 791),
(1429, 341, 1992, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-07-21', 'Greetings Tyler: We appreciate the work your team performed here at Pennington. As you were aware when the study was conducted, we were at the preliminary stages of buildinga laminated beam manufacturing plant inside the main crossarm plant. We broke ground (concrete)in December 2015 and had the facility up and running and certified by May 1, 2016. It has been atremendous effort by our maintenance staff, employees, and contractors. Needless to say, we have not had the time and resources to implement any of the energyassessment recommendations.  We plan on addressing them in the near future. To comment specifically on the study and underlying assumptions: 1.        The dry kilns are dehumidification kilns, therefore the boiler does not run continuously.2.        The economics of the cost of natural gas has changed, we switched to an interruptiblerate schedule which lowered the price from approximately $1.00/therm to $.60/therm. Thank you for all your time and efforts on behalf of Pennington Crossarm Co. Regards, Rick StringfieldPennington Crossarm Co.Eugene, OR Cell 503 467 1887', NULL, NULL, 867),
(1430, 341, 1992, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-07-21', 'Hello Rick,I understand how that major project can take priority. It is good to hear that you have completed it and are up and running. I would like to suggest setting up a follow up call within a year or two. Can you give me a date range that we can plan to call you back and find information on what you have decided to implement.Thank you,', NULL, NULL, 867),
(1431, 347, 1816, 2, 0, NULL, '2016-07-22', 'We had the implementation call. All info updated on database and Rutgers.', NULL, NULL, 821),
(1432, 341, 2116, 2, 0, NULL, '2016-07-28', 'Spoke with on the phone. He is working on getting the forms filled out. Thinking about setting up a Portland and Vancouver facility.', NULL, NULL, 890),
(1433, 347, 2088, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-07-22', 'Hi Jeanne, Attached is the trip report, containing a description of the assessment day as well as a brief narrative of opportunities being pursued.Below as a table of some rough estimates of cost savings and implementation for the opportunities we are pursuing. These will be refined as we get more information.Opportunity NameEstimated SavingsImplementationPaybackLight Switch near Wastewater $1,100 $4000.36Stormwater for Dust Management $32,000 $2,0000.06Rueping Tank $24,500 $50,0002.04Cover Tank Farms  $40,000 $80,0002.00Oil Giveaway                                                                                                             $20,000                    $20,000                               2.00  Some other recommendations we are still looking into are:-Kiln fan speed-Kiln seal insulation-Evaporator Efficiency-Preheat Makeup water-Compressed Air LeaksThese are the implementation and payback information based on rough estimates and without incentives. There will be another email coming your way with further questions from the team regarding different systems and your facility.If you have any questions, do not hesitate to send me an email or give me a call.Thank you for your time, ', NULL, NULL, 884),
(1434, 347, 2088, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-07-22', 'Jeanne, Below are the questions that analysts still have after the assessment.Kilns:Any data on a live power reading on Pull Kiln for fans?How many hours per year would is each kiln being run?Storm/Ground Water for Dust ManagementWhat sort of infrastructure will be needed to take the water from the tanks to the water truck?What sort of cost will be associated with changing regulations to allow this to happen?Type of cost and amount?Lighting Controls in Wastewater AreaWill a manual switch be all that\'s necessary due to employee energy awareness? Or should we automate it?I counted 4 250W metal halide and 14 95W fluorescent bulbs, is that correct?Are the 95W fluorescent T6\'s?Rueping TankCost of a rueping tank you are interested in? Difficult to find vendors online.', NULL, NULL, 884),
(1435, 347, 2088, 1, 0, NULL, '2016-07-29', 'Hey everyone, Below are the questions that analysts still have after the assessment.Kilns:Any data on a live power reading on Pull Kiln for fans?How many hours per year would is each kiln being run?Storm/Ground Water for Dust ManagementWhat sort of infrastructure will be needed to take the water from the tanks to the water truck?What sort of cost will be associated with changing regulations to allow this to happen?Type of cost and amount?What is the water capacity of the trucks being used to wet the dirt?How often do you fill the truck?How long does it take to fill truck? (Trying to see how big of a pump and how frequently it would be used)Lighting Controls in Wastewater AreaWill a manual switch be all that\'s necessary due to employee energy awareness? Or should we automate it?I counted 4 250W metal halide and 14 95W fluorescent bulbs, is that correct?Are the 95W fluorescent T6\'s?Rueping TankCost of a rueping tank you are interested in? Difficult to find vendors online.', NULL, NULL, 884),
