(1654, 346, 2018, 1, 0, 12770, '2017-09-19', 'I have talked to Dave and let him know that we would like some feed back, I asked him to respond to us in 2 week time. I have also sent the email with the summary in it.', NULL, 820, 861),
(1655, 367, 2244, 2, 0, NULL, '2017-10-06', 'Scheduled for Jan 8th. PAP sent and will contact on the 16th if it has not been received', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(1656, 367, 2243, 2, 0, NULL, '2017-10-06', 'called and left voicemail and followup email', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(1657, 367, 2243, 1, 0, NULL, '2017-10-06', 'Dennis,My name is Joe Lewis and I am an Energy Analyst at Oregon States Energy Efficiency Center.Jim Hughes reached out to me and explained that your company may be interested in the energy assessments we offer. They are no cost to you, as they are funded through the DOE, and only require analysts on site for one day.I left you a voicemail today about possibly coming out for an energy assessment of your facility sometime early next year. When you get the chance, feel free to call me at (503) 547-5234 to discuss a potential assessment.Thank you for your time and I look forward to the opportunity of working with you.Joe Lewis', 23, 861, NULL),
(1658, 367, 2204, 2, 0, NULL, '2017-10-06', 'Called and got back on top of his to do list. will call back 10/20 to check in', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(1659, 367, 2216, 2, 0, NULL, '2017-10-06', 'left voicemail', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(1660, 367, 2216, 1, 0, NULL, '2017-10-06', 'Julie,My name is Joe Lewis and I am an Energy Analyst with Oregon States Energy Efficiency Center.John Wilhelms let me know that you will be coordinating the potential setup of this assessment.When you get the chance, please call me back at (503) 547-5234, or just reply to this email, and we can further discuss the service we offer.Thank you and I look forward to the opportunity to work with you.Joe', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(1661, 367, 2233, 1, 0, NULL, '2017-10-06', 'Kelly,My name is Joseph Lewis and I am an Energy Analyst at Oregon States Energy Efficiency Center.You have been in contact with my boss, Joe Junker, about an energy assessment that is tentatively scheduled for October 13th. I would like to confirm that date with you right now and apologize for the delay in this confirmation.As I mentioned in the voicemail I left you, I would be more than happy to help with any questions you may have on the Pre-Assessment Package.As for utility information we need, the last 12 months of bills from your electricity, natural gas, and water provider should suffice.Thank you very much and we look forward to working with you!Joe', NULL, NULL, 921),
(1662, 367, 2244, 2, 0, NULL, '2017-10-20', 'Called and left voicemail, set for Jan 8th but still need PAP. Havent heard in a week or two', NULL, NULL, 926),
(1663, 367, 2216, 2, 0, NULL, '2017-10-20', 'Called, no answer. Left a voicemail apologizing for not being available for phone conversation this week', NULL, NULL, 911),
(1664, 367, 2216, 1, 0, NULL, '2017-10-20', 'Julie,I would like to apologize for my lack of availability this week. A string of meetings, exams, and interviews kept me out of the office all week.Please let me know the soonest date and time that works for you to discuss the energy assessments that we provide.Thank you and have a great day.', NULL, NULL, 911),
(1665, 367, 2244, 1, 0, NULL, '2017-10-23', 'Ted,Thank you for sending back the complete Pre-Assessment Package.It looks to be good to go! In the event something is missing, I will get back in contact with you.The next steps on our side is to reserve lodging and transportation, as well as assign a team and a lead to this assessment. Once those steps are taken, the lead will get in touch with you to set up a Pre-Assessment Phone Call.You can expect the lead to get in contact with you around the beginning of December.Thank you for your help and cooperation and I we are looking forward to working with you.Joe Lewis', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(1666, 367, 2243, 1, 0, NULL, '2017-10-27', 'Dennis,My name is Joe Lewis with Oregon State Universitys Energy Efficiency Center.This is a quick followup to the voicemail I just left you.We offer no cost energy assessments through a grant from the Department of Energy. Jim Hughes refereed me to you and said that you would likely be interested in our service.Please feel free to call me at (503) 547-5234 or respond to this email address if you have any questions or would like to further discuss what we offer.Thank you for your time and I look forward to the opportunity of working with you.Joe', NULL, NULL, 927),
(1667, 367, 2243, 2, 0, NULL, '2017-10-27', 'Left voicemail', NULL, NULL, 927),
(1668, 367, 2204, 2, 0, NULL, '2017-10-27', 'Called and left voicemail', NULL, NULL, 909),
(1669, 367, 2204, 1, 0, NULL, '2017-10-27', 'Wally,This is a quick followup email to the voicemail I just left you.I know things are busy on your side and that you have been trying to find a range of dates that may work to have us come out early next year. Im always available (besides when Im in class) to talk about any questions you may have.If you have time today or next week, feel free to call me at (503) 547-5234 or just respond to this email. If I dont hear back from you in that time, I will give you a call the Monday before Thanksgiving, 11/20.Thanks and have a good day,Joe', NULL, NULL, 909),
(1670, 367, 2216, 1, 0, NULL, '2017-10-27', 'Julie,This is a quick followup email for the voicemail I just left you.As I said in my last email, these are the times I am unavailable throughout the week:MW 10-12 and 2-3TR 2-4F 12-2Please let me know if there is any time that works for you to have a conversation over the phone about our services. Or, in the event that no time works out, I can pass this conversation off to my boss, Joe Junker, who is attached to this email.If you have the time today or next week, please give me a call back at (503) 547-5234 or a quick response to this email works just as good.Thank you for your time and patience and we look forward to working with you!Joe', NULL, NULL, 911),
(1671, 367, 2216, 2, 0, NULL, '2017-10-27', 'Called and left voicemail', NULL, NULL, 911),
(1672, 367, 355, 2, 0, NULL, '2017-11-29', 'Called and left voicemail introducing myself and the center', 196, 861, 546),
(1673, 367, 2204, 2, 0, NULL, '2017-11-29', 'Called and left voicemaail, havent heard from him in a few weeks. If no return call I will just table this lead for now', 186, 861, 909),
(1674, 367, 2204, 1, 0, NULL, '2017-11-29', 'Wally,Im just following up to the voicemail I left you earlier.I know we have spoken a handful of times over the last month or so and that things are busy on your end so I do not want to pester you. However, if you would like us to come out to your facility early next year we have a few spots open for the beginning of January, otherwise we could schedule you for late March or sometime this summer.In any case, please let me know which way you are leaning, and also let me know if you have any questions or concerns that you would like to go over.Thanks,Joe', 186, 861, 909),
(1675, 225, 2259, 1, 0, NULL, '2017-12-11', 'Submitted on Monday, December 11, 2017 - 08:56Submitted by anonymous user: 192.109.145.41Submitted values are:First Name: DavidLast Name: AnkcornTitle/Relation to Company: Plant ManagerEmail: david.ankcorn@saint-gobain.comCompany Name: Saint-Gobain Performance PlasticsTelephone: 2534665435Fax: 2538643497Street Address: 507 N Levee RoadCity: PuyallupState: WashingtonZip Code: 98371PO Box:City :State:Zip Code:Industry: Composite ManufacturingMajor Products: Composite Radomes, ducts and thermoformed plastic partsSystems of interest or problems to be investigated: HVAC Efficiency, PlantAir and Vacuum Efficiency, Composite Oven SchedulingThe results of this submission may be viewed at:http://eec.oregonstate.edu/node/20/submission/9', NULL, NULL, 930),
(1676, 225, 2259, 2, 0, NULL, '2017-12-20', 'Heard about us on Corporate Conference Call.  $280K utilities - mostly electric. Make composite plastics, thermoforming, electric ovens, isocyanurate foam production.  MAJOR PRODUCTS: Composite Radomes, ducts and thermoformed plastic parts.    SYSTEMS OF INTEREST: HVAC Efficiency, PlantAir and Vacuum Efficiency, Composite Oven Scheduling', NULL, NULL, 930),
(1677, 367, 355, 1, 0, NULL, '2017-12-08', 'Joe,   We are in the middle of building another production line  new line should be running by end of 2018. We might delay doing this assessment until after our new line is up and running. Thanks', NULL, NULL, 546),
(1678, 367, 2204, 2, 0, NULL, '2018-01-09', 'Called and left voicemail', NULL, NULL, 909),
(1679, 367, 2204, 1, 0, NULL, '2018-01-09', 'Wally,This is just a quick followup to the voicemail I left you today.It has been some time since we last spoke about setting up an assessment with your company. If I recall correctly we had discussed setting the date between mid January and mid February.If that window still works for you, or if you are interested but would like to do it later in the year, please feel free to contact me at (503) 547-5234 or at this email address.Thank you,Joe', NULL, NULL, 909),
(1680, 367, 2210, 1, 0, NULL, '2018-01-09', 'Hello,My name is Joe Lewis and I am an Energy Analyst with Oregon States Energy Efficiency Center.You spoke with my boss, Joe Junker, in July about setting up an energy assessment with your company. During that time you let us know that, due to ownership changes, you needed time to sort things out before scheduling an assessment.I am contacting you today to check if enough time has passed that we could again start discussing setting up an energy assessment with your company.If you would like to go over the details of our assessment process and reports, please call me at (503) 547-5234 or respond to this email.Thank you and I look forward to working with you,Joe Lewis', NULL, NULL, 106),
(1681, 367, 2210, 2, 0, NULL, '2018-01-09', 'Left a voicemail', NULL, NULL, 106),
(1682, 367, 2210, 1, 0, NULL, '2018-01-09', 'Hey Joe-Thanks for following up with us. I appreciate you keeping us in mind. Pacific Foods completed its sale to Campbells right at the end of the year so were still in the throes of changes and updates. Theres a lot coming at our teams over the next three months and I want to make sure we have the capacity to get involved. My gut is telling me that March is a better target to start but Id like to get a sense from you over what your time constraints/preferences look like. If you dont mind sending me a(nother) short high level summary of what the program is and what you need from us, I can pass that on to our leadership team for a response. I am looking forward to working with your organization, and hopefully well be able to do so, sooner rather than later. Thanks', NULL, NULL, 106),
(1683, 367, 2210, 1, 0, NULL, '2018-01-10', 'James,I understand the situation at hand and appreciate your timely response.March would be a perfect time to begin talking about a date for an assessment of your facility. We typically try to schedule clients for late March and early April. If those times dont pan out, we have space to conduct an audit throughout the summer.To briefly describe our program, we provide no cost energy assessments that assess your facility and production line for savings in energy, productivity, and cost. Our process begins with collecting utility information from you to model your current energy consumption. After that, a team of analysts spends one day on site. This visit includes a tour, brainstorming savings opportunities and data collection. Following the assessment, the team spends 60 days writing, editing, and compiling a comprehensive analysis for all systems that data was collected for. Attached to this email is our Pre-Assessment Letter. A more detailed agenda for the assessment is located on pages 5 and 6.As of right now, we do not need anything from you. Please take your time in going over our program and Pre-Assessment Letter. In the event that you do want us to perform an analysis of your facility, we would ask that you complete this form (with utility accounts and contacts) so we can begin the baseline analysis prior to the assessment date.Please let me know if there is any other information you would like, or if you have any questions regarding our program or the Pre-Assessment Letter.Thank you for your time and I look forward to working with you soon,Joe Lewis', NULL, NULL, 106),
(1684, 367, 2204, 2, 0, NULL, '2018-01-10', 'Hi Joe, Thank you for following up.  We have discussed this idea here but we are working on a different aspect of electrical usage, namely power quality and reliability.  This is something that we might entertain doing in 2019. Wally', 186, 861, 909),
(1685, 367, 2204, 1, 0, NULL, '2018-01-10', 'Wally,Thank you for your response.We will keep your company in mind and check back early next year.Thank you,Joe Lewis', NULL, NULL, 909),
(1686, 367, 2260, 2, 0, NULL, '2018-01-10', 'The client is interested in an assessment at the end of Jan. PAP sent', NULL, NULL, 932),
(1687, 367, 2260, 1, 0, NULL, '2018-01-10', 'Shannon,Attached is the Pre-Assessment Letter we discussed on the phone.Please review it as you can and I will be more than happy to talk with you about it and answer any questions you may have tomorrow on our call.You can expect a call from me at about 2:45 tomorrow afternoon.Thank you and I look forward to working with you,Joe Lewis', NULL, NULL, 932),
(1688, 367, 2260, 2, 0, NULL, '2018-01-16', 'Spoke about the PAP and confirmed date of 3/28', NULL, NULL, 932),
(1689, 367, 2235, 1, 0, NULL, '2018-01-09', 'Tammy,Attached is the Pre-Assessment Package we discussed on the phone.It outlines our report process, including an agenda for the one day audit we will perform.It also includes the Pre-Assessment Form and the Utility Release. These two documents are not crucial right now, as we are only introducing you to our service.Please let me know if you have any questions regarding our assessment process or our service as a whole.Thank you and I look forward to working with you,Joe Lewis', NULL, NULL, 922),
(1690, 341, 2091, 1, 0, -1, '2018-01-24', 'Called, left a voicemail and sent an email. Will call tomorrow for IMP.', NULL, 825, 874),
(1691, 341, 2129, 1, 0, 13756, '2018-01-24', 'Nick and Dave are no longer at Pioneer. Andy was in meeting. Called and left voicemail along with email.', NULL, 842, 878),
(1692, 225, 1914, 1, 0, NULL, '2018-02-13', 'Hi David,Let us know if we can add any insight if LTD works with you on implementing anything.In the mean time would you like to have us visit any of your other client sites? In the past we have talked about Swanson Brothers, Ply Veneer and (Roseboro Lumber?).- Joe', NULL, NULL, 853);
INSERT INTO `ContactLog` (`ContactLogId`, `EmployeeId`, `PersonId`, `ContactTypeId`, `GrantId`, `TaskId`, `Date`, `Notes`, `LeadId`, `ProjectId`, `LocationId`) VALUES
(1693, 367, 2242, 1, 0, NULL, '2018-02-13', 'Jim,My name is Joe Lewis with Oregon States Energy Efficiency Center. We spoke in September of last year about the two companies you own and your interest in having us perform an energy assessment at each of them.We assessed your Bend facility early last month and are in the process of writing the report.Unfortunately we never had any communication with your Portland facility. Are you still interested in us auditing this company?If you are, please forward me the contact information of the person I would coordinate with so we can get an assessment scheduled. If not, we can always check back later this year or whenever is convenient for you.Thank you for your time,Joe Lewis', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(1694, 367, 2116, 1, 0, NULL, '2018-02-13', 'Steve,My name is Joe Lewis and I am a student energy analyst at Oregon States Energy Efficiency Center. I am calling to follow up on the voicemail I left you today.The EEC assessed your Vancouver facility in October 2016 and your Portland facility in January 2017, attached are the reports we developed. My records show that you have three other sites in Oregon and may be interested in having them assessed as well.If you would like to discuss a potential audit for any of the additional locations, please feel free to call me at (503) 547-5234 or respond to this email whenever is most convenient for you.Thank you and I look forward to working with you,Joe Lewis', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(1695, 367, 2260, 1, 0, NULL, '2018-02-13', 'Shannon,I am following up on the conversation we had last month about the Pre Assessment Package I sent you for your energy assessment scheduled for the last week of March.You said to check in after one month if I had not heard back from you. Is the PAP done or do you need more time?As I mentioned before, the most crucial part of the package is your facilitys annual energy consumption (it must be over $100k to qualify for an assessment) and the contact information of your utility providers. With just this information we can begin the pre-audit analysis of your facility.Please let me know if you have any questions or need any help with the PAP.Thank you,Joe Lewis', NULL, NULL, 932),
(1696, 225, 2264, 1, 0, NULL, '2018-02-27', 'Following up on email I sent regarding Tacoma Power Suggested no-cost energy assessment. ', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(1697, 225, 2264, 1, 0, NULL, '2018-02-22', 'Hello Mike,I am Director of the Oregon State University Energy Efficiency Center (a U.S.DOE Industrial Assessment Center).I am following up on a suggestion by Keil Drescher and Natasha Houldson at Tacoma Power that I contact you to offer a no-cost full scope industrial energy and efficiency assessment.   We are planning a spring break (March 26-30) trip to visit a few sites in your area and I would be pleased to include your facility.   I wanted to provide you with a little bit of information before giving you a call.  The OSU EEC/IAC has conducted over 600 assessments of Northwest industries since 1986 and identified over $129 Million in cost savings and productivity opportunities. Based on follow up with assessed facilities, an average implemented savings of approximately $40,000 has typically been achieved per site based on our recommendations.The assessment process entails a one day visit to your facility after collecting preliminary information. A team of faculty lead engineering student analysts tour your site, brainstorm on potential opportunities and devote the remainder of the day to collecting data that supports an analysis. Within a typical 60 days, a report is delivered with specific recommendations to reduce energy and waste streams costs and increase productivity and profitability. We have a full compliment of state of the art equipment to bring to bear on these assessments including combustion analyzers, thermal imaging cameras, a non-contact ultrasonic flow meter, specialized refrigeration system analysis tools, power quality analyzers, and a broad selection of data loggers. If you have any systems that might benefit from the evaluation these allow, the center can help. I hope this sounds interesting to you.  If you wish, you can find out more about us at: http://eec.oregonstate.edu/. I look forward to speaking with you and hope to get a chance to work with you.- Joe Junker', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(1698, 225, 2265, 1, 0, NULL, '2018-02-22', 'Hello Kyle,I am Director of the Oregon State University Energy Efficiency Center (a U.S.DOE Industrial Assessment Center).I am following up on a suggestion by Keil Drescher and Natasha Houldson at Tacoma Power that I contact you to offer a no-cost full scope industrial energy and efficiency assessment.   We are planning a spring break (March 26-30) trip to visit a few sites in your area and I would be pleased to include your facility.   I wanted to provide you with a little bit of information before giving you a call.  The OSU EEC/IAC has conducted over 600 assessments of Northwest industries since 1986 and identified over $129 Million in cost savings and productivity opportunities. Based on follow up with assessed facilities, an average implemented savings of approximately $40,000 has typically been achieved per site based on our recommendations.The assessment process entails a one day visit to your facility after collecting preliminary information. A team of faculty lead engineering student analysts tour your site, brainstorm on potential opportunities and devote the remainder of the day to collecting data that supports an analysis. Within a typical 60 days, a report is delivered with specific recommendations to reduce energy and waste streams costs and increase productivity and profitability. We have a full compliment of state of the art equipment to bring to bear on these assessments including combustion analyzers, thermal imaging cameras, a non-contact ultrasonic flow meter, specialized refrigeration system analysis tools, power quality analyzers, and a broad selection of data loggers. If you have any systems that might benefit from the evaluation these allow, the center can help. I hope this sounds interesting to you.  If you wish, you can find out more about us at: http://eec.oregonstate.edu/. I look forward to speaking with you and hope to get a chance to work with you.- Joe Junker', NULL, NULL, 935),
(1699, 225, 2265, 1, 0, NULL, '2018-02-23', 'Kyle,We met a couple of years ago when Mohsen Zaky and I toured your plant.  Natasha Houldson asked me to weigh in on your question.  While the OSU Energy Efficiency Center is not contractually or officially associated with the BPA Energy Smart Industrial Program, it is very much supported by ESI, and informally associated with ESI.  They invite ESI representatives to all their engagements with ESI utilities such as Tacoma Power, and I have personally attended and participated in several of the assessments they have done in the Puget Sound area.  A few of the ESI folks in the same or similar jobs to me are either OSU or UW Industrial Assessment Center alums. I believe they provide valuable and meaningful assessments and reports, and work in concert with both ESI and Tacoma Power on paths forward to improving your plants energy efficiency and overall operation.  Feel free to contact me if you have any questions.Regards,Bob BrennandEnergy Smart Industrial Partner (ESIP)Energy Smart Industrial4113 Banbridge Loop SE Olympia, WA 98501360-310-0747  mobilewww.energysmartindustrial.com', NULL, NULL, 935),
(1700, 225, 2265, 1, 0, NULL, '2018-02-22', 'Joe,Are you guys associated with BPAs Energy Smart Industrial program?Kyle Kendig, M.Eng.Plant EngineerCONCRETE TECHNOLOGY CORPORATION253-404-2223 (direct)253-383-2912 (fax)', NULL, NULL, 935),
(1701, 225, 2265, 1, 0, NULL, '2018-02-23', 'Calling to follow up on our recent email exchange.', NULL, NULL, 935),
(1702, 225, 2265, 1, 0, NULL, '2018-02-23', 'Thanks Bob,Kyle - looks like your question got answered very well. We work hard to collaborate with ESI. I like to think we can be a great first step, casting a wide net over your facility and process to find cost effective opportunities to save on electrical, gas and other energy bills; reduce waste stream costs; and improve productivity. I can give you a call today to fill you in more if you like, at a time that works best for you.- Joe Junker', NULL, NULL, 935),
(1703, 225, 2265, 1, 0, NULL, '2018-02-27', 'Got a hold of Kyle, He said \"no thanks\"', NULL, NULL, 935),
