(1708, 225, 2267, 1, 0, NULL, '2018-02-27', 'Called - receptionist said Brad was no longer there. Replaced as GM by John Smith. He is out for week for training. Sent me to his voice mail. LVM. Said I would email and follow up next week.', NULL, NULL, 937),
(1711, 225, 2268, 1, 0, NULL, '2018-02-27', 'Hi  John,I am following up on voicemail I just left. I was calling on the recommendation of Tacoma Power to offer a no-cost full scope industrial energy and efficiency assessment.  As background: I am Director of the Oregon State University Energy Efficiency Center (a U.S.DOE Industrial Assessment Center).  We are planning a spring break (March 26-30) trip to visit a few sites in your area and I would be pleased to include your facility.   The OSU EEC/IAC has conducted over 600 assessments of Northwest industries since 1986 and identified over $129 Million in cost savings and productivity opportunities. Based on follow up with assessed facilities, an average implemented savings of approximately $40,000 has typically been achieved per site based on our recommendations.The assessment process entails a one day visit to your facility after collecting preliminary information. A team of faculty lead engineering student analysts tour your site, brainstorm on potential opportunities and devote the remainder of the day to collecting data that supports an analysis. Within a typical 60 days, a report is delivered with specific recommendations to reduce energy and waste streams costs and increase productivity and profitability. We have a full compliment of state of the art equipment to bring to bear on these assessments including combustion analyzers, thermal imaging cameras, a non-contact ultrasonic flow meter, specialized refrigeration system analysis tools, power quality analyzers, and a broad selection of data loggers. If you have any systems that might benefit from the evaluation these allow, the center can help. I hope this sounds interesting to you.  If you wish, you can find out more about us at: http://eec.oregonstate.edu/. I look forward to speaking with you and hope to get a chance to work with you.- Joe Junker', NULL, NULL, 937),
(1713, 367, 362, 1, 0, NULL, '2018-02-28', 'Called and spoke about reassessment, not interested now they just worked with ETO \"Low hanging fruit was dealt with\"', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(1714, 341, 2106, 1, 0, NULL, '2018-01-24', 'My Response but no email feedback: Ken,Any information will be helpful. I am free for a phone call today and in the afternoons in general. Else, you can provide a response via email. Phone may be quicker though.Much appreciated!', NULL, NULL, 874),
(1715, 341, 2106, 1, 0, NULL, '2018-03-07', 'Called today but no answer. Left a VM. Sent email.', NULL, NULL, 874),
(1716, 358, 2170, 1, 0, 13859, '2018-04-09', 'Called and left a message and emailed. No answer', NULL, 855, NULL),
(1717, 358, 2199, 1, 0, -1, '2018-04-09', 'Called and left a message and emailed. No answer', NULL, 863, NULL),
(1718, 367, 2210, 1, 0, NULL, '2018-04-03', 'Joseph-Good morning. Do we have a date yet for our assessment? Thanks!', NULL, NULL, 106),
(1719, 367, 2210, 1, 0, NULL, '2018-04-06', 'James,Following up on my voicemail I just left.We are flexible the last two weeks of June and any day after the 20th works for us!Feel free to give me a call back if you want to discuss this. My number is (503) 547-5234. Or just email with a date between June 21st and the 29th that works for you.Sorry for the delay in this chain of communication.Joe Lewis', NULL, NULL, 106),
(1720, 367, 2210, 1, 0, NULL, '2018-04-10', 'Joe-How about the 21st?', NULL, NULL, 106),
(1721, 367, 2210, 1, 0, NULL, '2018-04-12', 'James,The 21st works for us!Now that we have a date scheduled, our next steps are to assign a team and a lead analyst for this project. Once a lead is assigned (typically 2-4 weeks prior to assessment) they will contact you and schedule a pre-audit phone call where they will discuss assessment day logistics and ask questions about your facility and its process.Thank you for your patience and enthusiasm in this process and we all look forward to working with you!Joe Lewis', NULL, NULL, 106),
