(1733, 225, 2284, 1, 0, NULL, '2018-05-14', 'Hello Steve,It has been quite awhile since our 1994 energy and efficiency assessment of the City of Eugene - Waste Water Division facility.  (A that time we worked with Bob Sprick.) I wanted to see if you would be interested in an updated assessment. Our reports have grown significantly and I imagine your facility has changed a lot too.We have a few openings this summer and this fall and I would be pleased to visit you. There is still no cost to eligible facilities as the effort is paid for by the U.S.DOE. All it takes on your part is the time to host us.As a reminder: Oregon State University offers no-cost full scope energy and efficiency assessments to industry and otheres. The center has provided over 600 of these to Northwest industries and municipal facilities since 1986 and identified over $129 Million in cost savings and productivity opportunities. Based on follow up with assessed facilities, an average implemented savings of approximately $40,000 has been achieved.The assessment process entails a one day visit to your facility after collecting preliminary information. The team of analysts tours your site, brainstorms on potential opportunities and devotes the remainder of the day to collecting data to support an analysis. Within a typical 60 days, a report is delivered with specific recommendations to reduce energy and waste streams costs and increase productivity and profitability. The OSU EEC has a full compliment of state of the art equipment to bring to bear on these assessments including combustion analyzers, thermal imaging cameras, a non-contact ultrasonic flow meter, specialized refrigeration system analysis tools, power quality analyzers, and a broad selection of data loggers. If you have any systems that might benefit from the evaluation these allow, the center can help. Let me know if you have an interest. I hope to get a chance to work with you.  I have pasted a summary of what we recommended in that report below. I will follow up with a call later this week.   Thanks - Joe Junker(You can find out more about our program at  http://eec.oregonstate.edu/) ', NULL, NULL, 938),
(1734, 225, 2284, 1, 0, NULL, '2018-05-17', 'LVM - No cost assessment?', NULL, NULL, 938),
(1735, 225, 2284, 1, 0, NULL, '2018-05-17', 'Hi Steve,I just left you voice mail. I wanted to see if you would like to set up a U.S.DOE funded no cost energy and efficiency assessment. - Joe Junker(and apologies for the notable typo in the letter I attached then)', NULL, NULL, 938),
