(1768, 367, 2282, 1, 0, NULL, '2018-04-26', 'Cory,Attached you will find the Pre-Assessment forms that we spoke about on the phone. I know you graduated from the IAC program not too long ago, however I kept all of the logistical information in the documents for your reference.Can you please let me know, either in an email or on the forms, what the names of the two facilities are. I know you said that they are both owned by Tillamook, but I dont recall the name of either one.Thank you for reaching out to us and we are excited to work with you this summer!Joe Lewis', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(1769, 367, 2282, 1, 0, NULL, '2018-04-27', 'Good morning Joe, Columbia River Processing and Columbia River Technology are the names of the two facilities in Boardman. Ill fill out a second PDF of the Columbia River Technology site and make some adjustments to the name.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(1770, 367, 2282, 1, 0, NULL, '2018-05-03', 'Good afternoon Joe, Please find attached .ZIP files of Columbia River Processing & Columbia River Technologys Electricity, Natural Gas, Steam and Water utility invoices from April 2017 through March 2018, along with the associated Pre-Assessment Forms. As questions arise, please feel free to either email or call me for clarification.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(1771, 367, 2282, 1, 0, NULL, '2018-05-16', 'Cory,We would like to schedule the audit of both facilities for the first or second week of August if that works out for you! I dont have any more specific date ranges because we are trying to schedule a third audit for this Boardman trip and I am working with them to find a time that will work out.Do you have any preference as to the first or second week of August?Thanks,Joe', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(1772, 367, 2282, 1, 0, NULL, '2018-05-16', 'Joe,The 14th and the 16th of August are fine with me. I figure the order we the facilities in doesnt matter, but maybe Nick, Bruce, & Jerod have a preference for which facility gets which day.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(1773, 367, 2311, 1, 0, NULL, '2018-05-16', 'Andrew,Hello. My name is Joe Lewis and your contact information was given to me by Jake Flyg.I am reaching out today to discuss the potential of setting up an energy assessment at your facility this summer.Our program is sponsored by the US DOE and is a free service to you and your facility.Our assessment is a one day even where we arrive at your facility at 8 am, tour the facility and take notes on energy saving opportunities. We then work through lunch to brainstorm recommendations. Following the brainstorm, the team works for several hour collecting data around your facility. Once data has been collected, we report back to you with rough estimates on energy and cost savings, as well as the implementation cost of the project. We then spend the next 60 days back in Corvallis generating a comprehensive report of our observations and energy saving recommendations.If this sounds like something you are interested in, please call me at (503) 547-5234 or respond to this email at your earliest convenience.Thank you,Joe', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(1774, 367, 2311, 2, 0, NULL, '2018-05-16', 'LVM, info provided by friend who works at the plant', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(1775, 367, 2311, 2, 0, NULL, '2018-05-21', 'Called again and got a hold of Andrew. Willing to have us out early August.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(1776, 367, 2311, 1, 0, NULL, '2018-05-21', 'Andrew,Attached is the Pre-Assessment Package I spoke to you about over the phone.It includes a form with some general questions about your facility, as well as the utility release document I spoke to you about.Please do not feel rushed to get this back to us, and feel free to ask any questions you may have during this setup process.Thank you again and we all look forward to working with you this summer.Joe Lewis', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(1777, 367, 2282, 1, 0, NULL, '2018-07-06', 'Cory,It has been some time since we last spoke and I wanted to see if you have any preference to which facility is assessed on the 14th of August and which on the 16th.It appears that the men you attached were flexible so if you have no preference, I say we do Productions on the 14th and Technology on the 16th?Let me know what you think and Ill get it set in stone!Cheers,Joe Lewis', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(1778, 367, 2311, 1, 0, NULL, '2018-07-06', 'Andrew,It has been sometime since we last talked, and we are now 5 weeks away from your facilitys audit on August 15th.I am checking in to see if you have made any headway on the Pre-Assessment Package I sent to you on May 21st. I completely understand if you have not, all that I ask is you provide me with names and phone numbers of your utility representatives on the Utility History page so that we may contact and collect utility data and begin our pre-audit analysis.Please let me know if you have any questions bout the PAP and I would be glad to help1Thank you,Joe Lewis', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(1779, 360, 2283, 1, 0, NULL, '2018-07-06', 'Hi Aaron, I have attached a trip report which briefly summarizes our assessment and the opportunities that we have identified for recommendations. We have performed initial estimates and we have some additional questions for you and your team. Please reply to these questions at your earliest convinience. General Background InformationMotor Inventory (if possible)Compressed Air Leaks 75 HP compressor nameplate data What are the current controls of the air compressors? Are the 100 HP and 75 HP compressors both VFD controlled? Could we assume that the air compressor is operating at 70% load capacity? If not, would the capacity be higher or lower? Install VFD on Cooling Tower FanFan motor name plate from SF2 cooling towerDoes the cooling tower fan operate at full capacity during the summer? For our initial estimate, we assumed that the average load on the fan could drop to approximately 80% year round. Does this sound like a reasonable assumption? Could we assume thate the average fan load could drop down to as low as 60% during winter months?Reduce Urea WastePrice per lb of urea and yearly consumption of ureaMaximum weight capacity of the conveyor that feeds urea into kettles 3 and 7Reduce RTO Gas ConsumptionCan you provide any more information on the composition of the total VOC emissions from sf3?  Install VFD on BlowersWhat is the most efficient pressure in the methanol tanks?What is the current pressure of the methanol tanks?What is the behavior of the pressure release valve? (Setpoint, how often it opens, for how long is it open)Preheat Boiler Makeup WaterHow often are the boilers running?What is the usage divide between the natural gas boiler and the boiler running off SF3 exhaust?Boiler nameplate data?Natural gas usage for boilers?Stack temperature for boilers?Condensate not collected? Location of this condensate in facility?Currently analysts are thinking of either installing an economizer on your boiler stack, or collecting condensate for return. Is there any other option for waste heat in your facility that you can think of?Utility AnalysisCommodity charges for natural gas?Thanks,', NULL, NULL, 532),
(1780, 367, 2241, 1, 0, NULL, '2018-06-28', 'Lawrence,My name is Joseph Lewis and I am an energy analyst with Oregon State Universitys Energy Efficiency Center. I am emailing you as a followup to the voicemail I just left.You spoke with my boss, Joe Junker, late last year about a potential audit, but you and your facility were in the midst of energy saving projects and did not have the resources to have us out.We are currently scheduling audits for the fall and winter of this year and also have space available in July as well.If a no cost energy assessment is something you would be interested in hearing more about, please reach out to me at (503) 547-5234 or at this email address.Thank you and I look forward to hearing from you,Joe Lewis', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(1781, 367, 2241, 1, 0, NULL, '2018-07-06', 'Joseph Thank you guys again for your interest. But at this time we are still prioritizing our focus in other areas at the facility as we did last year. Thanks for your interest, I have your contact information and hopefully we see some success we have been implementing over the last 2-3 years and can re-focus towards some energy saving projects in the future and I can look you up. Go Beavs Lawrence Silbernagel', NULL, NULL, NULL),
