(2, 1, 208, 'Northwest Natural', '', 9, 'North - LOCAL - Portland', 225, '0000-00-00', '0000-00-00'),
(3, 1, 494, 'Clark County Food Project', 'Ready to have us come January 2014. Would like to coincide with their Wed energy meetings but other days can be made to work.\n', 9, 'LOCAL - Portland area', 225, '2014-01-08', '2014-01-25'),
(9, 1, 687, 'OMEP/ Stew Overton at Pioneer Cutstock', 'No direct contact yet. Working with Mark it is set for start of Winter Term, could go sooner if we have the ability. Mark brought them up on 6/25/13 again. (Stew suggested them 10/24/12)', 9, 'LOCAL - Bend area', 225, NULL, NULL),
(12, 2, 690, 'Oregon Vineyard Association', 'answered several questions about USDA loan process, waiting on pre-assessment form return. 7/26/12', 3, '', 0, NULL, NULL),
(13, 2, 691, 'Oregon Vineyard Association', 'contact traveling for work, no contact for 3 months. 4/15/12', 3, '', 0, NULL, NULL),
(14, 2, 692, 'Oregon Vineyard Association', 'Did phone walkthrough with Jim, seemed EXTREMELY interested. No contact after two calls. Should try one more time... 4/16/12', 3, '', 0, NULL, NULL),
(15, 2, 693, 'Website and Rebecca Thistlethwaite', 'Will see if plant is ok with Ag$, and 50% AG', 3, '', 0, NULL, NULL),
(22, 1, 720, 'Stew Overton - Pioneer Cutstock', '', 2, 'TRIP EAST - Bend area', 0, '0000-00-00', '0000-00-00'),
(23, 1, 721, 'Stew Overton - Pioneer Cutstock', 'Stew suggest them after imp call Oct 2012\n', 2, 'TRIP EAST - Bend ', 0, '0000-00-00', '0000-00-00'),
(24, 1, 722, 'OMEP - Mark Biederbeck', 'Sent note re:  RB Rubber  10/23. Mark Mentioned them 4/22/2013', 2, 'LOCAL - McMinneville', 0, '0000-00-00', '0000-00-00'),
(27, 1, 31, 'Davis', '', 4, 'LOCAL - Corvallis area', 365, '0000-00-00', '0000-00-00'),
(29, 1, 66, 'Cal Grimmer - NWNG, Alan Meyer', 'Cal emailed to see if we would be interested. Might be on hold - they solved their immediate problem. Alan mentioned them.\n', 2, 'LOCAL - Albany', 348, '0000-00-00', '0000-00-00'),
(31, 1, 731, 'Doug Swier - Cowlitz', 'Doug copied me on email 11/7/2012 after calling to check that Feb 2013 might work. ', 2, 'LOCAL - Longview ', 0, '0000-00-00', '0000-00-00'),
(37, 1, 504, 'Christina Kruger - PPL', 'For July Audit trip - Need to find 1-2 more. Sent pre-audit info already\n', 9, 'Medford', 0, NULL, NULL),
(38, 1, 750, 'Andreas Winardi - PSE', 'Sent Pre-audit letter - targeting last week in June', 4, 'Tacoma area', 0, NULL, NULL),
(39, 1, 751, 'Andreas Winardi - PSE', 'Returned Pre-audit - shooting for last week in June', 9, 'Tacoma Area', 0, NULL, NULL),
(41, 1, 752, 'Heard about us from Doug Swier via Kalama plant', 'FIND ANOTHER FACILITY TO ASSESS WITH THEM AND SCHEDULE FOR LATE JULY. Returned the pre-audit letter - summer trip (mid summer? stack with PSE audits?)', 9, 'Seattle North', 225, NULL, NULL),
(42, 1, 528, 'Kevin Wooster for ETO', 'Returned offer letter + Shooting for June 24th week', 9, 'LOCAL -Bend area', 0, NULL, NULL),
(43, 1, 753, 'Doug Swier - Cowlitz PUD', 'All information back to us. Sent potential date(s) ', 9, 'LOCAL - Longview Area', 0, NULL, NULL),
(46, 1, 755, 'Sean McCaffery ', 'DEFER UNTIL OCTOBER - he preferred July but overridden by his boss. They will send an energy accounting developed by John Thornton.', 9, 'LOCAL - Portland area', 225, NULL, NULL),
(47, 1, 758, 'Doug Swier', 'Try to set them up for a fall audit', 2, 'LOCAL - Longview area', 225, '0000-00-00', '0000-00-00'),
(48, 1, 759, 'Andreas Winardi', 'Told her we had to defer to next fiscal year, that I would see if we could visit early before this term started (maybe we could get permission for one more waste water at the Director\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'s meeting and go on way to Mt Vernon)Otherwise likely over Christmas Vacation\n\nMondays are our busiest day, and Fridays are not always fully staffed so the best days of the week would be Tuesday through Thursday if you need equipment swapped or special scenarios staged for your evaluation.', 9, 'Olympia area', 225, '0000-00-00', '0000-00-00'),
(49, 1, 760, 'Contacted by Coca-Cola', 'Sent Pre-audit doc. 3 Plants: Portland, Wilsonville, Bellevue. She said she could be slow in response. Vacation until May 21, 2013. She supports the NW plants. Will likely hand set up off to local folks. Also has California plants: Sacramento and San Leandro', 9, 'LOCAL - Portland, Wilsonville; TRIP - WA', 315, '0000-00-00', '0000-00-00'),
(50, 1, 131, 'Clark PUD - Sam Walker - Larry Blaufus', 'SET UP FOR OCTOBER. Returned pre audit letter info. Busy in the summer. Fall would be a good time for an audit.  Sam forward correspondence on 4/22 between them and Larry. COPY BOTH ON CORRESPONDENCE', 9, 'LOCAL - Portland Area', 225, NULL, NULL),
(51, 1, 609, 'EWEB - Alan Fraser ', 'Told Al I could serve them in the fall. (He called 4/24/13)', 2, 'LOCAL - Eugene ', 315, '0000-00-00', '0000-00-00'),
(52, 1, 761, 'EWEB - Josh Ruddick', 'Sent Pre-Audit letter. Bill James there - Called after getting email from Josh Ruddick at EWEB. Targeting Summer or Fall. 24-7 Operation. 2-300 Employees. Make granola and cereal.', 9, 'LOCAL - Eugene', 225, NULL, NULL),
(53, 1, 763, 'PSE - Andreas Winardi', 'Still need to speak directly to them. Sent Pre Audit. Andreas sent lead - LVM and sent an EM. MacDonald bun baker. For June trip.\n', 9, 'Tacoma Area', 0, NULL, NULL),
(54, 1, 764, 'SME-IAC', 'Criteria established. Awaiting scheduling.', 9, 'LOCAL - Hillsboro, OR', 225, NULL, NULL),
(55, 1, 765, 'SME-IAC', 'Talked to Ian and his annual energy bills are only 430,000. This is dead as an IAC.', 3, '', 0, NULL, NULL),
(57, 1, 516, 'SME-IAC', 'They are backing off of an audit, doing their own thing, and will be getting back to us if it doesn\\\'t work.', 2, 'LOCAL - Woodburn', 325, NULL, NULL),
(58, 1, 768, 'PSE - Andreas Winardi', 'Sent intro email based on Andreas suggestion', 9, 'Seattle North', 225, NULL, NULL),
(59, 1, 771, 'Tracy - OSU Tour- K. Carlo Sampson', 'Send Pre-audit to Scott S.\nTracy met K Carlo Sampson - Regional Sales Manger while hosting a tour at OSU', 2, 'LOCAL - Canby', 225, '0000-00-00', '0000-00-00'),
(60, 1, 780, 'Website', 'Emailed their general Contact list. Received an email from their Brewmaster, Jim Kelter, who indicated he is interested in receiving more information about our program and wants to talk more when he returns next week.', 2, 'LOCAL-Hood River', 321, '0000-00-00', '0000-00-00'),
(61, 1, 385, 'Diana Knous', 'Diana emailed on 9/4/13 to see if we could serve them Well over 100k in electrical bills she says', 2, 'SOUTH TRIP - Coos Bay area', 225, '0000-00-00', '0000-00-00'),
(62, 1, 787, 'Michael-Friend-Trevor Cochran', 'Friend of Michael Dexter: Trevor Cochran works at Cascade Gaskets and talked with him about an energy audit during a get together and he expressed interest. Trevor recently(9/25/13) emailed me and asked for more information so I gave him the basic run down and sent him the pre-assessment documents.', 3, 'TRIP NORTH - Seattle area', 320, '0000-00-00', '0000-00-00'),
(63, 1, 5, 'Client contacted us', 'Greg,\n \nSouth Coast Lumber Co in Brookings Or and Pacific Wood Laminates in Brookings Or are two plant sites under one ownership in the wood products industry.\nWe are privately owned with less than 500 employees.\nWe are interested in learning more about your energy auditing and possibly having an audit done.\n \nIf you are not the correct contact for this, could you steer me in the right direction please?\n \nBrian Bay\nSouth Coast Lumber Co\nBrookings Or\n541 661-2586\nGreg,\n ', 9, 'Brookings', 225, '2014-03-01', '2014-07-01'),
(64, 1, 791, 'Website', 'Was told Jennifer Olsen was in charge of scheduling.', 9, 'LOCAL SOUTH - Eugene', 341, '2016-07-25', '2016-07-29'),
(65, 1, 789, 'Friend of employee', '(Brad) Got the number of Mike Mercado, a manufacturing engineer, from a friend who is working here as an intern. Called and left Mike a voicemail.', 3, 'LOCAL - Halsey', 315, '0000-00-00', '0000-00-00'),
(66, 1, 790, 'Contacted management email list', 'Lisa sent an email to the management list requesting an assessment. After the pre-assessment paperwork was completed, it was determined that energy use is too little to qualify for an IAC assessment. Unless this facility can be covered on a grant besides IAC, we cannot assess.', 3, 'LOCAL - Salem', 315, '0000-00-00', '0000-00-00'),
(67, 1, 291, 'Website', 'Called corporate office and left a message. Emailed general contact list, will follow up by Nov. 25th', 3, 'LOCAL- Portland', 321, '0000-00-00', '0000-00-00'),
(68, 1, 0, '', '', 0, '', 0, NULL, NULL),
(69, 1, 794, 'Website', 'Called from website information, talked to Doug in production. Received his email, he will pass information onto management. Attempting to line this up with Coca-Cola for a spring break assessment.\n\nFollowed up with Doug today (1/2/14). Still trying to line them up with Coca-Cola', 3, 'Bellevue', 321, '0000-00-00', '0000-00-00'),
(70, 1, 795, 'Website', 'Manufacturers of strapping systems. Called and left a message for Patrick in production. No email provided. Patrick called back, they moved from Bellevue and are no longer manufacturing, just an import/export office. Dead.', 3, 'Bellevue', 321, '0000-00-00', '0000-00-00'),
(71, 1, 796, 'Website', 'Called facility, did not have an operator to talk to. Emailed general contact site', 3, 'LOCAL- Beaverton', 321, '0000-00-00', '0000-00-00'),
(72, 1, 797, 'Website', 'Called general office, was forwarded to Tony who is the production manager. I left a message with Tony with my information.', 3, 'LOCAL- Beaverton', 321, '0000-00-00', '0000-00-00'),
(73, 1, 798, 'Website', 'Called general contact number. Was put in contact with Dave Pofahl in production. Contact info from dave was provided and an initial email was sent to him. ', 3, 'LOCAL- Beaverton', 321, '0000-00-00', '0000-00-00'),
(74, 1, 799, 'Website', 'Called Perfect Blend in Bellevue, was given production managers (Sheldon Milner) contact information and email. Sent email with information and pre-assessment package, informed that we would be interested during spring break.', 3, 'Bellevue', 321, '0000-00-00', '0000-00-00'),
(75, 1, 800, 'Website', 'Called Aero-plastics in Renton (WA), was forwarded to general manager (Mike) who I left a message for and sent an email with our information. ', 3, 'Bellevue', 321, '0000-00-00', '0000-00-00'),
(76, 1, 801, 'Website', 'Called PM Industries, put in contact with facility manager Jim Morehead. Jim was out of the office, so I left a message with him and sent him an email with our pre-assessment information. ', 3, 'LOCAL- Beaverton', 321, '0000-00-00', '0000-00-00'),
(77, 1, 802, 'Website', 'Called King Estate, put into contact with Tom Maxwell, who seems very interested in an assessment this winter/spring. Sending him information, hopefully the ball with get rolling. ', 2, 'SOUTH LOCAL- Eugene', 321, '0000-00-00', '0000-00-00'),
(78, 1, 803, 'Website', 'Called company, was put into contact with Kirk who is a production manager. Out of office--- emailed with information.', 3, 'LOCAL- Eugene', 321, '0000-00-00', '0000-00-00'),
(79, 1, 805, 'Website', 'Called Capital. Was put in contact with someone in production Ray who I left a voicemail for. Will follow up', 3, 'Seattle', 321, '0000-00-00', '0000-00-00'),
(81, 1, 809, 'Personal Contact', 'I know one of the project enegineers at Murphy plywood\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'s eugene location and he mentioned that they would be interested in an assessment. I sent him the pre-assessment letter on 2/24/14.', 9, 'LOCAL- Eugene', 320, '0000-00-00', '0000-00-00'),
(82, 1, 810, 'Clean Water - Janet Gillaspie', 'Sent pre audit doc. Looking at spring term audit on a Thursday preferably.', 9, 'LOCAL - Rickreall', 225, '2014-04-01', '2014-06-15'),
(83, 1, 811, 'Miles Naughton', 'In contact with Dathan Bathan, who we worked with previously at the Clatskanie mill and now works at Tillamook. Very interested, new management so he said June may be slightly early. Pre-assessment info sent to him to be filled out. Also giving me the Forest Grove contact information.', 9, 'WEST LOCAL - Tillamook', 321, '0000-00-00', '0000-00-00'),
(84, 1, 813, 'Met at PPRC Sustainable Brewing Event', 'Could go Spring term, ok with summer 2014', 9, 'LOCAL - Portland', 225, '2014-04-01', '2014-08-01'),
(85, 34, 814, 'Dave Kunz - ODEQ', '', 9, '', 0, '0000-00-00', '0000-00-00'),
(86, 1, 817, 'Joe met client', 'Joe met Bruce C. at NWFPA Energy Leaders Summit in Jan 2014', 3, 'LOCAL - Portland', 225, '0000-00-00', '0000-00-00'),
(87, 34, 818, 'Met Nate at NWFPA conf, Jan 2014', 'Joe Met Nate at NWFPA conf, Jan 2014', 9, '', 0, '0000-00-00', '0000-00-00'),
(88, 1, 331, 'Karl H.', '6/18/14 DEQ issues bogging them down. Shoot for a fall audit. Call in August\n4/11/14 Karl introduced us, sent info, they sound interested', 9, 'LOCAL - Portland', 225, '0000-00-00', '0000-00-00'),
(89, 1, 819, ' Alan Meyer - Pacific Power', 'Two mills actually - Lebanon and Sweet Home.\n4/14/14 Alan contacted me for our introductory information. I sent it and he sent it on to the Weyerhaeuser Santiam Mill', 9, 'EAST LOCAL - Lebanaon?', 225, '0000-00-00', '0000-00-00'),
(91, 1, 545, 'Ellen Porter - RFP Corporate', 'Sawmill and Plywood and Powerhouse. (Sawmill too recent - perhaps on direct contract). Also a particle board plant on site. Not sure if they want it to be included with rest in one MEGA MACT report. Wants to have all RFP plant assessed for Boiler MACT rules', 9, 'SOUTH LOCAL - Dillard -2-3 audit sites', 225, '0000-00-00', '0000-00-00'),
(92, 1, 521, 'Ellen Porter RFP Corporate', 'Wants to have all RFP plant assessed for Boiler MACT rules', 9, 'TRIP - Coquille', 225, '0000-00-00', '0000-00-00'),
(93, 1, 548, 'Ellen Porter - RFP Corporate', 'Wants to have all RFP plant assessed for Boiler MACT rules', 9, 'TRIP/LOCAL - Riddle', 225, '0000-00-00', '0000-00-00'),
(94, 1, 554, 'Dianna Knous - Pacific Power and Ellen Porter - RFP Corporate', 'Dianna said they just overahauld and would like a new audit. Ellen Wants to have all RFP plant assessed for Boiler MACT rules', 9, 'TRIP/LOCAL - Riddle', 225, '0000-00-00', '0000-00-00'),
(95, 1, 314, 'ORNL', 'Early January 2018', 10, 'East-TRIP- Bend', 225, '0000-00-00', '0000-00-00'),
(96, 35, 820, 'Met Anita at Energy Summit', '', 0, '', 0, NULL, NULL),
(97, 35, 631, 'Lisa Parriott', 'While on our King County CSC assessment Lisa expressed strong interest in having us come up and look at individual systems. She mentioned that she could easily do a PO for <$5000/yr.', 0, '', 0, NULL, NULL),
(98, 1, 821, 'Kristina Kruger- PPL Medford area', 'They want us to visit in summer 2015. They have made x-ray film. Moving to touch screen film. NEED TO FIND TWO MORE ', 9, 'SOUTH TRIP - Medford Area - White City', 225, '0000-00-00', '0000-00-00'),
(99, 1, 822, 'Jeff Johnson there called me', 'Target for summer 2015 Trip', 2, 'ALASKA', 225, '2015-07-01', '2015-09-15'),
(100, 1, 823, 'Brian Switzer there contacted us', 'Ready to be audited after August 14. On Fred Meyer Campus. ', 9, 'Portland', 225, '2014-08-15', '2014-09-01'),
(101, 1, 431, 'ORNL', '', 7, 'North - LOCAL - Portland', 225, '0000-00-00', '0000-00-00'),
(102, 1, 826, 'OSU IAC Web Form', 'Targeting fall audit. Recently joined the DOE Better Plants program and committed to reducing energy usage by 25% over the next 10 years.\nWould like an energy assessment conducted to help identify conservation\nopportunities.\n', 9, 'Local - Albany', 225, '0000-00-00', '0000-00-00'),
(103, 1, 828, 'Web Site Form', 'Ready to just have us come the next day - need to prep them for more up front work \n\nFood Processing, Major Products: Jams, Jellies, and Syrups, Problems: Heating/Cooling, Motors, Pumps, and Compressors\n', 2, 'NORTH LOCAL Portland', 225, '0000-00-00', '0000-00-00'),
(104, 1, 831, 'Tracie Contact', 'Filled out pre-assessment and ready for a winter term audit on a Tue/Wed/Thur. ', 9, 'LOCAL - Springfield', 321, '2015-01-27', '2015-03-29'),
(105, 1, 832, 'Contacted us', 'Kumar is located back east. Has arranged IAC audits in other locations.  - Set for a Tue in February or March.', 9, 'LOCAL - Portland', 225, '2015-02-01', '2015-03-20'),
(106, 1, 833, 'Contacted us', 'Kumar is on the east coast and has set up other BIMBO assessments with IACs.', 3, 'NORTH TRIP - Kent', 321, '0000-00-00', '0000-00-00'),
(107, 1, 834, 'Carley  Lettero', 'DOE wants us to pick on only one (this or the Wastewater plant) I think we should go with the Wastewater plant. ', 2, 'LOCAL-Corvallis', 0, '0000-00-00', '0000-00-00'),
(108, 1, 835, 'Carley Lettero', 'DOE wants us to pick on only one (this or Taylor Water plant) I think we should go with this one.  Wastewater plant = $333k electricity\n', 9, 'LOCAL-Corvallis', 225, '0000-00-00', '0000-00-00'),
(109, 1, 836, 'Karl - Jeff Mason ', 'Jeff put us in touch with Andy Tobin there to set up an assessment', 9, 'LOCAL - Tualatin', 225, '0000-00-00', '0000-00-00'),
(110, 1, 838, 'Carly Lettero', 'Wastewater plant = $333k electricity\n', 3, '', 0, '0000-00-00', '0000-00-00'),
(111, 1, 839, 'Jeffrey Mason', 'Putting info together. PGE and NWNG ~$120K - spring term would be ideal. Lets shoot for April. Want to make sure Jeff and Fred Stevens can be there. Best Days: Mon, Tue or Wed \n \n', 9, 'LOCAL (Cornelius?)', 225, '2015-04-15', '0000-00-00'),
(112, 1, 840, 'Mike Bierren - worked at Atlas when we audited them', 'Michael Birren - was wihy Atlas Cylinder - now with Fujimi corportaion - in Tualatin and Wilsonville  Office :503-972-5573   Cell: 503-539-5573 ', 9, 'Local - Portland', 225, '0000-00-00', '0000-00-00'),
(113, 1, 841, 'Implementation Call', 'Audited previous Chemtrade, source would like us to visit the anacortes plant', 3, 'TRIP NORTH - Anacortes', 321, '0000-00-00', '0000-00-00'),
(114, 1, 842, 'Kroger Bakery - Brian Switzer', '(This used to be the FredMeyer Dairy - we have been there in the past)', 9, 'LOCAL NORTH - Portland', 341, '2016-05-09', '2016-05-20'),
