(569, 6114, 6, 'Direct Fire Heating of Electrolyte', NULL, '222211', 0, 493000, 493000, 200000, 'Currently you plant spends $2.3 million annually on natural gas for the copper refining plant.  Most of the gas is used to generate steam for the electrolyte heating system.  Replacing the steam system with submerged combustion heating units will increase heating efficiency by 12%.  Implementing this recommendation would reduce annual natural gas use by approximately 11% in the refinery.', 0, 0, 0, NULL, 493000, 200000, '0000-00-00', 6, '', 1, 0, NULL),
(570, 6115, 7, 'Diaphragm Pumps', NULL, '465201', 0, 426960, 426960, 149400, 'The current cost to maintain the diaphragm pumps in the precious metals plant is approximately $230.000 per year.  Replacing these pumps with high-capacity peristaltic pumps will reduce pump maintenance and save 64% of maintenance costs.  Additional savings in operating energy are possible. but are not being considered in this recommendation.', 0, 0, 0, NULL, 426960, 149400, '0000-00-00', 22, '', 1, 0, NULL),
