(835, 6378, 5, 'Notched V-Belts', NULL, '241111', 0, 0, 0, 4360, 'Replace standard V-belts on 74 motors with higher efficiency\r notched V-belts. The use of notched belts has been demonstrated to yield energy savings through\r reduction of belt losses due to friction. bending. and slippage.', 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 4360, '2006-09-01', 0, 'Started last fall. Some metric belts not available in notched version.', 1, 0, NULL),
(836, 6379, 6, 'Fresh Air for Winter Space Cooling', NULL, '242323', 0, 3150, 3150, 3637, 'During winter and other seasons when\r outdoor temperature is below 60? F. we recommend using outdoor air for space cooling in the spinning area rather than running chiller compressors. Installing five small intake fans in the outer west wall will help regulate indoor air temperature. This will save 75% of energy currently used to cool this space during those hours with outdoor temperature below 60? F.', 0, 0, 0, NULL, 3150, 3637, '2006-11-01', 0, 'Turned out they did not have to install intake fans. Were able to open louvers use existing fans. and turn off the chillers.', 1, 0, NULL),
(837, 6380, 7, 'Reduce Basement Lighting', NULL, '271353', 0, 2000, 2000, 2100, 'Install occupancy sensors in the basement to turn off lights when unoccupied and remove 37 fixtures. This will result in a 95% energy use reduction for lighting the basement.', 0, 0, 0, NULL, 104000, 80000, '2006-12-01', 0, 'Brought in lighting specialist to look at it and worked with utility to get 20% rebate. Went at it a little differently. removed some fixtures. changed a number of fixtures to T8s. addressed more areas. decided against the occupancy sensors and went with manual control instead.', 1, 0, NULL),
(838, 6381, 8, 'Use Load-Unload Controls', NULL, '242242', 0, 600, 600, 1500, 'We recommend implementing load-unload controls when installing the 100 hp compressor. Unload controls will allow the compressor to operate at lower power when system demand decreases. reducing power costs by 5.7%.', 0, 0, 0, NULL, 600, 1500, '0000-00-00', 16, 'Vendor steered them away from unloading control.', 1, 0, NULL),
