(3726, 8874, 1, 'Fuel Dryer', NULL, '21116', 0, 405450, 405450, 257883, 'Install a closed-loop fuel drying system to increase electrical generation capacity by 21%.', 0, 0, 0, NULL, 405450, 257883, '0000-00-00', 11, 'Complications with fuel dryer, permitting, etc. DEQ likes to work within existing permits instead of new sources. Last time we had to model for close to a year and get meteorological data at a cost of $60K. You were dead on regarding thinking about the boiler\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'s winter load. We are now thinking about co-firing with natural gas.  Nothing sure though. One question: what part of energy could be considered green then?. Cost savings from our analysis is pretty applicable. ', 1, 0, NULL),
(3727, 8875, 2, 'Boiler Fan VFD', NULL, '21223', 0, 37100, 37100, 32115, 'Install Variable Frequency Drives (VFD) on the Forced Draft and Induced Draft boiler fans. A VFD will control airflow by automatically adjusting fan motor speed. reducing fan energy use by 28.7%.', 0, 0, 0, NULL, 37100, 32115, '0000-00-00', 2, 'Want to do this. Variable vane dampers work ok. Do not want to make the investment right now. Will change it out if have to touch. ', 1, 0, NULL),
