(3735, 8883, 1, 'Reduce Discharge Pressure. Plants 4 and 5', 0, '22621', 1, 2965, 0, 6602, 'Lower the minimum ammonia condensing (discharge) pressure to 93 psig (60 F) on the Plant 4 and 5 compressors and improve the condensing approach temperature. This may require descaling or mechanical repair of the evaporative condensers. The resulting pressure reduction will reduce the energy cost of the refrigeration system by an average of 5%.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 6602, '2011-04-01', 0, 'Kind of compromised - did not go that low but lowered it. Will need to look at system. put in new tower.', 1, 0, 10),
(3736, 8884, 2, 'Air Leaks Reduction', 0, '24236', 1, 7102, 0, 7102, 'Reduce the leak load from 142 acfm (45% of the peak plant demand) to 52 acfm (30%). Maintaining this level will save 29% of current compressor electricity costs.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 7102, '2011-02-01', 0, 'Agressively reduced leaks. Winter to June', 1, 0, 4),
(3737, 8885, 3, 'Compressed Air Pressure Reduction', 0, '24231', 1, 4935, 2467, 1320, 'Reduce compressed air system pressure from 120 psi to 110 psi. Maintaining a pressure greater than the system requires provides no benefits and reducing pressure will effectively lower conpressor energy by 5%.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 2467, 1320, '2011-04-01', 0, '', 1, 0, 5),
(3738, 8886, 4, 'Upgrade Lighting and Install Motion Sensors', 0, '27135', 1, 120911, 45039, 14738, 'Replace existing lighting throughout the Main Plant with higher efficiency lighting. Use motion sensors to reduce operating hours for existing T-8 fixtures and proposed T-5 replacement fixtures. These changes are expected to reduce energy cost for lighting by 56.1%.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 45039, 14738, '2011-05-01', 0, 'Added additional lighting. freezers  with MS- added. packageing. bean room. still working on it.', 1, 0, 7),
(3739, 8887, 5, 'Photovoltaic Array', 0, '29114', 1, 379829, 136605, 25798, 'Install a photovoltaic array on building roofs. This will provide an alternative source for 2.8% of the facility\\\'s electrical energy consumption and reduce CO2 emissions associated with electrical generation.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 136605, 25798, '0000-00-00', 1, 'Looked into it. payback not good enough.', 1, 0, 4),
(3740, 8888, 6, 'Reduce Discharge Pressure. Main Plant', 283, '22621', 1, 0, 0, 930, 'Reduce the main plants minimum ammonia discharge pressure from 100 psig (63.4 F)  to 93 psig (60 F) on the high stage refrigeration compressors during the fresh pack and repack season when not defrosting. This will lower refrigeration energy costs 0.4% by reducing compressor energy use.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 930, '0000-00-00', 19, 'Decided not to. System did not work as well when they ran the pressure downs. Needs the pressure to run. Might try to go at it again next year. Would have to add in refrigerant pumps.', 1, 0, 10),
(3741, 8889, 1, 'Lighting', 0, '27135', 1, 36315, 27055, 25044, 'Replace existing lighting throughout the plant with higher efficiency lighting. Use motion sensors to reduce operating hours for existing T-8 fixtures and proposed T-5 replacement fixtures. These changes are expected to reduce energy costs for lighting in specified areas by 77.6%.  ', 0, 0, 0, 0, 27055, 25044, '0000-00-00', 0, '', 1, 0, 9),
(3742, 8890, 2, 'Cooler Tower Water', 0, '22692', 1, 6712, 6712, 7300, 'Route the condensate drain water coming from the washdown heat exchanger to the cooling towers to save freshwater and wastewater costs. This will reduce total annual water use by 1.8%.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 6712, 7300, '0000-00-00', 0, '', 1, 0, 2),
(3743, 8891, 3, 'VFD Runtime', 0, '24226', 1, 0, 0, 2126, 'Operate the VFD compressor when air is required. By running the VFD compressor during all hours of operation, energy consumption associated with air use can be reduced by 10%.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 2126, '0000-00-00', 0, '', 1, 0, 7),
