(4156, 9776, 2, 'Install Efficient Pulp Refiners', 320, '2.4322', 1, 57000, 41834, 41834, 'Upgrade both pulp refiners to a splined hub rotor design. This will lower the energy consumption while yielding the same fiber production, reducing associated annual energy consumption costs by 15%.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 41834, 41834, '0000-00-00', 18, 'We probably spent the most amount of time investigating the feasibility for this one. Reps from GL&V came out to our plant and then submitted a proposal and quotes. When one of the more tenured reps found out what we were planning, he cautioned us NOT to do it even though it would mean they would lose that sale. He said that tests performed at one of our other plants as well as actual results from a similar production plant led him to the conclusion that we would have major longevity issues with the new refiner design. We do not use fresh water for our refining process. The process water we use is high PH and contains a lot of calcium. The process water also contains small amounts of debris even after the strainers. The concern was that these would bind up the movement of the splines. It was decided to table this for now.\n\nComments on receipt of report:\nThis is one I think we gave you incorrect information on. Our existing refiners are of the splined hub rotor design. We are looking into changing how we control our refiners. Although the main reason for the possible change is for increased product quality, it will also probably result in more efficient use of the refiners. I see the report listed the upgrade cost at $26,000 per refiner It said that was based on a quote from the manufacturer. Based on the cost of the major parts from the manufacturer, I would think that quote was very low for our size refiners. At this point, I think all of our plants are using the splined hub rotor design refiners but I will contact the other plants to be sure.', 1, 1, 4),
(4157, 9213, 1, 'AR No. 3 - Heating Upgrade', 311, '2.7232', 3, 10580, 0, 1289, 'When the facility installs a heating system, we recommend installing electric heat pumps. This will reduce the associated annual energy required to heat spaces by 62%.', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 0, 6),
(4158, 9172, 0, 'Lighting Retrofit', 315, '-', 3, 875, 875, 565, 'Reduce motion sensor shut-off time, and install motion sensors in areas that currently are only served by light switches. This will reduce lighting operation hours, reducing associated annual energy consumption by 13%.', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 0, 14),
(4159, 9211, 3, 'Plastic Extruder Replacement', 313, '-', 1, 5572, 5572, 5478, 'Replace hydraulic pumps and motors on the plastic extruders with an electrically driven system to reduce annual electrical energy use, lower the overall maintenance costs for the machines, and increase production output for plastic parts. ', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 0, 5),
(4160, 9669, 1, 'UPS Controls', 320, '4.6310', 2, 20880, 20880, 393360, 'Install an Online Uninterruptible Power Supply for the boiler and refrigeration controls computer system. This will eliminate system restarts of the control system due to momentary power glitches, which cause a cascading failure in the manufacturing process. System failures due to momentary power glitches will be reduced by 100%.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 20880, 393360, '0000-00-00', 14, 'Looking into this. Still having power glitch problems. Just got shut down. Looking into micro turbines. 5 Million to install. Looking at another option. ', 1, 0, 4),
(4161, 9509, 2, 'Condensate Recovery', 311, '2.2127', 2, 19925, 19925, 26558, 'Install a condensate collection tank and additional piping to capture the condensate from the evaporator and return it to the boiler. This will result in a 4% annual reduction in boiler fuel usage and a 3% annual reduction in fresh water usage.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 19925, 26558, '0000-00-00', 22, '', 1, 0, 5),
(4162, 9319, 3, 'AR No. 3 - Electric Forklifts', 318, '2.8227', 1, 29000, 29000, 16839, 'Convert the leased forklifts from propane to electric powered. This will decrease fuel usage, operation costs, and emissions that are potentially hazardous in confined areas.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 29000, 16839, '0000-00-00', 22, '', 1, 0, 4),
(4163, 9324, 6, 'Heat Recovery', 311, '2.243', 1, 19701, 19701, 7796, 'Install a heat exchanger to recover heat on the discharge streams from the juice resin columns. This recovered energy can be used to pre-heat the incoming water used to clean the same columns, which will save 1.7% of boiler fuel usage.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 19701, 7796, '0000-00-00', 22, '', 1, 0, 5),
(4164, 9322, 4, 'HP Water Accumulator', 320, '', 4, 27000, 27000, 12631, 'Install an accumulator system on the high pressure water system used for spray down. This will allow the RotoJet pump and associated 100 hp electric motor to be turned off during periods of no demand. Resulting in an energy savings of 83%.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 27000, 12631, '0000-00-00', 22, '', 1, 0, 6),
