(4192, 9767, 5, 'Replace Venturi Generators', 315, '2.4232', 2, 6711, 6711, 15326, 'Replace Venturi generators on the box erector units with regenerative blowers. This will reduce the load on the air compressors, reducing associated annual energy use by 42%.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 6711, 15326, '0000-00-00', 22, 'Still looking at for 2014. ', 1, 0, 8),
(4193, 9778, 1, 'Reduce Compressed Air Leaks', 315, '2.4236', 2, 9480, 9480, 8480, 'Reduce the compressed air system leak load, or minimum sustained air flow, from 400 acfm (45% of peak, non-leak plant demand) to 269 acfm (30% of peak, non-leak plant demand). Maintaining this leak load will decrease associated energy costs by 13%.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 9480, 8480, '2012-12-21', 0, 'We performed a full air leak audit during our scheduled winter down !2/21/2012 to 12/28/2012. We identified many of the leaks and submitted work requests to eliminate the leaks. We discovered that most of the major leaks were from deteriorated nylon air tubing. We have slowly been replacing all of the old and cracked tubing. We recently completed the tubing replacement in the autoclave area and are working on other areas of the plant. Although we are sure we have greatly reduced the are leaks, it is difficult to give any specific numbers since we performed the repairs over time while also adding some more equipment that increased the compressor load.\n\nComments on receipt of report:\nThis is always at the top of my list for energy conservation. I combine this with looking for opportunities by changing from less efficient, air-powered devices to more efficient devices whenever practical. As far as air leaks, we have found that direct, physical inspection of the plant during production outages have worked best to locate the leaks. We have tried using ultra-sonic leak detectors while the lines are running with only minimal success. Unfortunately, during the last couple of plant outages, we failed to supply the manpower to do this. I need to make it clear to the group just how important these inspections are, even if the actual leak repairs canÃƒÆ’Ã†â€™Ãƒâ€ Ã¢â‚¬â„¢ÃƒÆ’Ã¢â‚¬Å¡Ãƒâ€šÃ‚Â¢ÃƒÆ’Ã†â€™Ãƒâ€šÃ‚Â¢ÃƒÆ’Ã‚Â¢ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â‚¬Å¡Ã‚Â¬Ãƒâ€¦Ã‚Â¡ÃƒÆ’Ã¢â‚¬Å¡Ãƒâ€šÃ‚Â¬ÃƒÆ’Ã†â€™Ãƒâ€šÃ‚Â¢ÃƒÆ’Ã‚Â¢ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â‚¬Å¡Ã‚Â¬Ãƒâ€¦Ã‚Â¾ÃƒÆ’Ã¢â‚¬Å¡Ãƒâ€šÃ‚Â¢t be performed at that time.', 1, 0, 11),
