ÃƒÆ’Ã†â€™ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã…Â¡ÃƒÆ’Ã¢â‚¬Å¡Ãƒâ€šÃ‚Â¬ÃƒÆ’Ã†â€™Ãƒâ€ Ã¢â‚¬â„¢ÃƒÆ’Ã¢â‚¬Â ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢ÃƒÆ’Ã†â€™ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã‚Â ÃƒÆ’Ã‚Â¢ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â‚¬Å¡Ã‚Â¬ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â‚¬Å¾Ã‚Â¢ÃƒÆ’Ã†â€™Ãƒâ€ Ã¢â‚¬â„¢ÃƒÆ’Ã‚Â¢ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â‚¬Å¡Ã‚Â¬Ãƒâ€¦Ã‚Â¡ÃƒÆ’Ã†â€™ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã…Â¡ÃƒÆ’Ã¢â‚¬Å¡Ãƒâ€šÃ‚Â¢ÃƒÆ’Ã†â€™Ãƒâ€ Ã¢â‚¬â„¢ÃƒÆ’Ã¢â‚¬Â ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢ÃƒÆ’Ã†â€™ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã…Â¡ÃƒÆ’Ã¢â‚¬Å¡Ãƒâ€šÃ‚Â¢ÃƒÆ’Ã†â€™Ãƒâ€ Ã¢â‚¬â„¢ÃƒÆ’Ã¢â‚¬Å¡Ãƒâ€šÃ‚Â¢ÃƒÆ’Ã†â€™Ãƒâ€šÃ‚Â¢ÃƒÆ’Ã‚Â¢ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã…Â¡Ãƒâ€šÃ‚Â¬ÃƒÆ’Ã¢â‚¬Â¦Ãƒâ€šÃ‚Â¡ÃƒÆ’Ã†â€™ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã…Â¡ÃƒÆ’Ã¢â‚¬Å¡Ãƒâ€šÃ‚Â¬ÃƒÆ’Ã†â€™Ãƒâ€ Ã¢â‚¬â„¢ÃƒÆ’Ã‚Â¢ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â‚¬Å¡Ã‚Â¬Ãƒâ€šÃ‚Â¦ÃƒÆ’Ã†â€™ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã…Â¡ÃƒÆ’Ã¢â‚¬Å¡Ãƒâ€šÃ‚Â¾ÃƒÆ’Ã†â€™Ãƒâ€ Ã¢â‚¬â„¢ÃƒÆ’Ã¢â‚¬Â ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢ÃƒÆ’Ã†â€™Ãƒâ€šÃ‚Â¢ÃƒÆ’Ã‚Â¢ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã…Â¡Ãƒâ€šÃ‚Â¬ÃƒÆ’Ã¢â‚¬Â¦Ãƒâ€šÃ‚Â¡ÃƒÆ’Ã†â€™Ãƒâ€ Ã¢â‚¬â„¢ÃƒÆ’Ã‚Â¢ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â‚¬Å¡Ã‚Â¬Ãƒâ€¦Ã‚Â¡ÃƒÆ’Ã†â€™ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã…Â¡ÃƒÆ’Ã¢â‚¬Å¡Ãƒâ€šÃ‚Â¢s budget but was not started due to other budget priorities. The first part of the project is in this year\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'s budget again.  I cannot give an estimate as I don\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'t know when the start date may be.  The first phase is to replace some spinning and winding equipment to determine capacity requirements.  The building and infrastructure replacement would not come until the 3rd or 4th year.\n', 1, 0, 8),
(4508, 11088, 0, '', 0, '', 0, 30000, 0, 8000, '', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0),
(4509, 11089, 2, 'Shut off Exhaust Fans', 336, '2.6242', 3, 936, 0, 2193, 'Install programmable logic controllers (PLCs) to shutoff the five Finish Bay baghouse exhaust fans when the nappers and shears are not operating. This will reduce associated annual energy consumption by 13%.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 2193, '0000-00-00', 14, 'We have not installed PLC controls on the baghouse fans due to production priorities.', 1, 0, 4),
(4510, 11091, 5, 'Install Alternative Water Heating', 325, '2.1392', 2, 81000, 0, 7930, 'Install an alternative water heating device in place of the current steam heat exchanger. This will reduce steam and, natural gas use, reducing associated annual energy consumption by 20.4%.', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 0, 5),
(4511, 11092, 4, 'Upgrade Lighting', 330, '2.7142', 3, 30178, 0, 4363, 'Install occupancy sensors in the dyehouse basement and upgrade outdoor lighting to LED lighting. This will reduce operation hours and increase lighting efficiency, reducing associated annual energy consumption by 3%.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 30178, 4363, '2014-06-11', 0, 'The exterior lighting upgrade to LED fixtures has been completed.  The dyehouse basement motion sensors has not due to the need to rewire the lighting circuits to accommodate the sensors. ', 1, 0, 16),
(4512, 11094, 6, 'Convert Forklifts', 332, '2.8227', 1, 40732, 0, 1279, 'Incrementally purchase electric forklifts instead of propane forklifts when the propane forklifts need to be replaced. This will decrease propane fuel use, operating costs, and emissions that are potentially hazardous in confined areas. Implementation will reduce energy and ancillary costs by 13.7%. ', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 0, 8),
(4513, 11099, 3, 'Interconnect Air Dams', 320, '2.4236', 2, 1600, 0, 3834, 'Interconnect air dams with the chip conveyors to reduce minimum sustained compressed air system air flow, from 85 acfm (43% of peak, non-leak plant demand) to 30 acfm (15% of peak, non-leak plant demand). Maintaining the proposed Minimum air flow will decrease associated annual energy use by 27%.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 3834, '0000-00-00', 14, 'Not implemented', 1, 0, 4),
(4514, 11102, 2, 'Install Ductwork', 321, '2.2628', 4, 11815, 0, 5751, 'Duct filtered air from the baghouses back into the building. This will reduce the number of air exchanges across the building and lower the load on the HVAC system, reducing associated annual energy consumption by 2.0%.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 5751, '0000-00-00', 14, 'Not implemented', 1, 0, 5),
(4515, 11103, 5, 'Reduce Compressed Air Pressure', 333, '2.4231', 2, 0, 0, 5528, 'Reduce compressed air system pressure from 118 psig to 90 psig. Maintaining a pressure greater than that required by the system provides little added benefit. Reducing pressure will decrease associated annual energy use by 35%.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 5528, '0000-00-00', 14, 'Not implemented ', 1, 0, 7),
(4516, 11104, 1, 'Reduce Horizontal Cell Idling', 331, '2.6218', 1, 1000, 0, 11654, 'Shut off the five large horizontal cells during idle periods. This will reduce electricity used to power the cells, decreasing associated energy consumption by 71.3%.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 11654, '0000-00-00', 14, 'Not implemented', 1, 0, 5),
(4517, 11098, 6, 'Install DCS Controls', 320, '2.5123', 2, 11200, 0, 2097, 'Reduce air flow in the debur and saw dust collection system (DCS). Install motorized gates on the DCS drops and a control system to operate the gates. Install variable frequency drives (VFDs) to control the fan capacity. This will reduce the fan\\\'s air flow, lowering the power demand on the fan motor and reducing associated annual energy consumption by 44%.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 2097, '0000-00-00', 14, 'Not implemented', 1, 0, 3),
(4518, 11100, 0, '', 0, '', 1, 40000, 0, 480000, '', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0),
(4519, 11101, 0, '', 0, '', 1, 20000, 0, 5889, '', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0),
(4520, 11105, 4, 'Install Photovoltaic Array', 331, '2.9114', 3, 178080, 178080, 5889, 'Install a photovoltaic array on the building roof. This will provide an alternative energy production source for 4.4% of the facility\\\'s energy consumption and reduce carbon dioxide emissions associated with electrical generation.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 178080, 5889, '0000-00-00', 14, 'Not implemented', 1, 0, 9),
(4521, 11093, 1, 'Upgrade Air Compressor Controls', 330, '2.4224', 2, 45000, 0, 8251, 'Install VFD controls on the 100 hp air compressor. This will reduce associated annual energy use by 27%.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 8251, '0000-00-00', 2, 'We have not upgraded the air compressor controls due to other budget priorities.', 1, 0, 8),
(4546, 11129, 2, 'Reduce Compressed Air Pressure', 310, '2.4231', 2, 1000, 1000, 1945, 'Reduce the compressed air system pressure from 110 psig to 100 psig. Maintaining a pressure greater than required by the system provides little added benefit. Reducing pressure will decrease associated annual energy use by 8%.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 1000, 1945, '0000-00-00', 14, 'Lacking engineering resources to implement. Focus is on projects to sustain operations.', 1, 0, 10),
(4547, 11130, 4, 'Upgrade Air Compressor Controls', 310, '2.4224', 2, 5500, 5500, 7138, 'Implement a lead-lag sequencing strategy to control the load on compressors #5 and #8. This will reduce associated annual energy use by 27%.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 5500, 7138, '0000-00-00', 14, 'Lacking engineering resources to implement. Focus is on projects to sustain operations.', 1, 0, 8),
(4548, 11124, 3, 'Install Boiler Fan VFD with O2 Controls', 334, '2.1116', 1, 7219, 7219, 11422, 'Install an oxygen (O2) sensor in the boiler stack of Boiler 2 and a variable frequency drive (VFD) on the forced draft fan to control fan speed based on oxygen content. This will increase combustion efficiency by optimizing the air-fuel ratio and reduce natural gas consumption by 6.8%. Additionally, it will reduce fan electrical consumption by 78%.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 7219, 11422, '0000-00-00', 14, 'Lacking engineering resources to implement. Focus is on projects to sustain operations.', 1, 0, 10),
(4549, 11127, 7, 'Install LED Lights in Freezers', 315, '2.7142', 3, 22910, 3437, 3463, 'Install LED light fixtures with occupancy sensors in Freezers 1, 2, and 3. This will increase lighting efficiency and reduce the refrigeration load, reducing associated annual energy consumption by 86%.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 3437, 3463, '0000-00-00', 14, 'Lacking engineering resources to implement. Focus is on projects to sustain operations.', 1, 0, 11),
(4550, 11125, 1, 'Recover Condensate', 334, '2.1243', 2, 6792, 6792, 18202, 'Capture condensate water from the aseptic line blanchers and use it as feed water for the two process boilers. This will reduce steam required to preheat the makeup water, reducing associated annual energy consumption by 35%.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 6792, 18202, '0000-00-00', 14, 'Lacking engineering resources to implement. Focus is on projects to sustain operations.', 1, 0, 3),
(4551, 11132, 8, 'Improve Pump Efficiency', 335, '2.6242', 4, 13250, 6625, 1925, 'Install a second pipe in the high pressure pump to reduce friction losses, allowing for a reduction in discharge pressure and pump energy costs by 63%.', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 0, 3),
(4552, 11136, 6, 'Insulate Boilers', 334, '2.2511', 2, 11317, 5659, 3138, 'Insulate the surfaces of both Cleaver &amp; Brooks process boilers. This will reduce heat loss from hot surfaces, reducing annual energy consumption by 1.4% per year.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 5659, 3138, '0000-00-00', 14, 'Lacking engineering resources to implement. Focus is on projects to sustain operations.', 1, 0, 9),
(4553, 11204, 0, '', 0, '', 0, 1000, 0, 1000, '', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0),
(4554, 11205, 0, 'Consolidate Finger Jointer Air ', 335, '2.4231', 2, 7522, 0, 12082, 'Consolidate Finger Jointing building compressed air system. This will reduce the energy used to operate the finger jointing building, reducing associated annual energy consumption by 12.5%.', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 5),
(4556, 11207, 5, 'Improve Lighting System', 325, '2.7142', 3, 2586, 1293, 2875, 'Install high output T5 fluorescent lighting in place of T12 fluorescent and metal halide lighting in primary production spaces and replace incandescent lamps with compact fluorescent lamps (CFL) where they exist throughout the facility. This will increase lighting efficiency, reducing associated annual energy consumption by 28%.', 1, 0, 0, 0, 1293, 2875, '0000-00-00', 2, 'They have brought this recommendation up with the utility representative several times but the payback period was way too long. ', 1, 0, 26),
(4557, 11208, 1, 'Install Natural Gas Heaters', 320, '2.1311', 1, 17353, 17353, 44216, 'Replace electric heaters with natural gas heaters on the prime line. Using a less expensive energy source will reduce the prime line operating cost, resulting in a 68.9% cost savings.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 17353, 44216, '0000-00-00', 3, 'The talked to natural gas providers and looked into the price of the heaters. It was not implemented due to the expense of the heaters ', 1, 0, 5),
(4558, 11209, 6, 'Install Roll Cases', 320, '2.4325', 2, 11206, 0, 20000, 'Install pull pockets in the rip shed. This will allow standard forklifts to pick up stacks of ripped lumber rather than using a straddle carrier, resulting in an annual labor savings of $20,000.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 20000, '0000-00-00', 3, 'They have looked into it and have wanted to implement but cash flow is the problem ', 1, 0, 2);
INSERT INTO `Recommendations` (`RecommendationId`, `TaskId`, `Number`, `Title`, `EmployeeId`, `ARC`, `APPCodeId`, `TotalCost`, `CapitalCost`, `Savings`, `Summary`, `Rebate`, `Incremental`, `BPT`, `BPToolId`, `ImplementationCost`, `ImplementationSavings`, `ImplementationDate`, `ImplementationCode`, `ImplementationComments`, `Final`, `EarlyPA`, `Pages`) VALUES
(4559, 11211, 4, 'Eliminate Moulding Fan and Hog', 336, '4.652', 2, 4810, 4810, 25006, 'Install a dump bin in place of the 100 hp hog chipper and use the 40 hp material handling fan for the moulding machines instead of the 200 hp material handling fan. These actions will reduce the chipper and 200 hp fan associated annual energy consumption by 100%.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 4810, 25006, '0000-00-00', 16, 'A study was done on this recommendation. The study concluded that it was cheaper to keep it idling then to start/stop', 1, 0, 4),
(4560, 11212, 3, 'Pay Bills On Time', 325, '4.821', 4, 0, 0, 3198, 'Reduce late fees by paying all of your utility bills on time. Savings will occur by avoiding late fees, which will reduce utility costs by 0.3%.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 3198, '0000-00-00', 22, 'Have not looked into it since there is a shortage of staff', 1, 0, 2),
(4561, 11213, 2, 'Insulate Paint Room', 336, '2.2515', 2, 3528, 828, 3869, 'Insulate the four paint room walls using 3.5 inch R11 Fiberglass Blanket insulation. This will reduce heat loss from hot surfaces, lowering annual energy consumption by 85% per year.', 1, 0, 0, 0, 828, 3869, '0000-00-00', 3, '', 1, 0, 8),
(4562, 11133, 5, 'Recover Jacket Water Heat', 335, '2.2446', 2, 16256, 6461, 5445, 'Install a heat exchanger to recover heat from the generator jacket water. This recovered energy can be used to preheat the incoming water used to clean the equipment in Plants 1 and 3 instead of using steam. This will reduce boiler energy use for heating CIP water saving 2.5% of total boiler use.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 6461, 5445, '0000-00-00', 14, 'Lacking engineering resources to implement. Focus is on projects to sustain operations.', 1, 0, 6),
(4563, 11183, 2, 'Shut Off Old Primary Scrubber', 331, '2.6218', 2, 40000, 0, 54087, 'Turn off one of the old primary sedimentation scrubbers and install a cover over the small centrate tank to minimize scrubbed air. This will reduce the electrical consumption and demand used to power the old primary scrubbing system, decreasing the associated energy consumption by 50%.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 54087, '2015-04-01', 0, 'One of them is turned off, and one of them is turned on.  Similar to the estimates.  No cost to do!', 1, 0, 3),
(4564, 11186, 5, 'Improve Pump Efficiency', 331, '2.4131', 1, 23300, 0, 21245, 'Optimize pumping of the influent and intermediate pumps by rebuilding damaged pumps. The influent pumping efficiency can be improved from the current efficiency of 35% to a reasonable average of 74% and the intermediate pumping efficiency can be improved from the current efficiency of 20% to a reasonable average of 74%. Rebuilding the influent and intermediate pumps that were operating during the facility visit on December 16, 2013 will reduce associated energy consumption by 63%.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 21245, '0000-00-00', 2, 'Have not done a lot there. Have replaced two influent motors with high efficiency motors. Working on systematically changing all big pumps to that. Use green energy grant (90,000 per year) Already have 14 big ones, 1/3 of the way.  Measurements for whats best to come.', 1, 0, 6),
(4565, 11185, 6, 'Install VFD on Dewatering Centrifuge', 331, '2.4144', 1, 22011, 0, 10770, 'Install a variable frequency drive (VFD) on the 300 hp dewatering centrifuge motor to decrease peak electrical demand during startup. This will reduce the associated annual peak demand by 50.8%.\n', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 10770, '0000-00-00', 6, 'They want all of their service providers to match.', 1, 0, 4),
(4566, 11184, 3, 'Reduce Scrubber Fans During Winter', 331, '4.6320', 2, 0, 0, 30875, 'Reduce the south scrubber, foul air scrubber, and chemical scrubber fan motor speeds by 50% of current speed during the six winter months. This will reduce the energy used to power the scrubber fans, decreasing the associated energy consumption by 43.8%.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 30875, '2015-06-01', 0, 'The scrubber fans for the E. Primaries building are set up for winter mode.  There are three conditions that must be met to lower the fan output: outside temperature less than 50 degrees, that the occupancy sensor has not been tripped, she could not remember the last condition.', 1, 0, 4),
(4567, 11181, 9, 'Install Premium Plus Motors', 310, '2.4133', 1, 4602, 0, 2631, 'Install NEMA premium plus motors in place of the current NEMA premium motors in the anoxic basins. Install the proposed motor system as the current motors need to be replaced. This will increase the full load efficiency of the mixer motors from 90% to 93%, reducing associated annual energy consumption by 3%.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 2631, '0000-00-00', 6, 'Havent done that, attempted to do just the shutting off of the mixer motors.  That whole basin going to come offline with project to get new blowers. Wants to abandon old motors and look at new technology.', 1, 0, 6),
(4568, 11180, 1, 'Shut Down Anoxic Basin Mixers', 310, '2.6218', 1, 0, 0, 28066, 'Turn off half of the mixers used in the first anoxic basin and one-third of the mixers in the second anoxic basin when the trains are in use. Doing so will reduce associated annual energy consumption by 45%.\n', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 7017, '2015-07-21', 0, 'Attempted that. Worked our way through the mixers to see what we could shut off and work. Shut them off temporarily and not completely. Savings: whatever estimated. Like a quarter of that. Still waiting on the feedback and will know exactly soon. At about a 5% total energy savings. No cost to implement.  Shutting power down and just leaving it alone. Turning off the drives in summer.', 1, 0, 4),
(4569, 11182, 8, 'Install Turbo Aeration Blower', 315, '2.4322', 2, 129750, 0, 32937, 'Replace the positive displacement aeration Blower #1 with a new, properly sized turbo aeration blower. This will improve blower efficiency, and reduce the volume of wasted air and associated annual energy consumption by 16%.\n', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 32937, '0000-00-00', 12, 'We have not done that. Project coming up in 2018 where that would happen. Incorporating that into the project.', 1, 0, 14),
(4570, 11178, 10, 'Install Efficient Interior Lighting', 310, '2.7134', 3, 7191, 0, 3741, 'Install occupancy sensors in allowable areas and replace Utilidor lights with LEDs. This will increase lighting efficiency and minimize operating hours, reducing associated annual energy consumption by 70%.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 3741, '2015-07-01', 0, 'We have done the majority of that. Just got a grant to do offsite facilities, so that has been completed.', 1, 0, 40),
(4571, 11179, 11, 'Install Efficient Exterior Lighting', 310, '2.7142', 3, 39597, 0, 10856, 'Replace exterior high pressure sodium and incandescent lights with LEDs. This will increase lighting efficiency, reducing associated annual energy consumption by 80%.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 10856, '2015-04-01', 0, 'Did exterior lighting, need to do a few high dollar explosion proofs and picking those off one by one. Working our way to finishing that one by one.', 1, 0, 71),
(4572, 11174, 7, 'Upgrade Air Compressor Controls', 333, '2.4224', 2, 17350, 0, 10323, 'Install additional receiver capacity and adjust the controls on both air compressors to operate as load-unload. These actions will reduce associated annual energy use by 17%.\n', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 10323, '2015-06-19', 0, 'Just happened last Friday.  No real feedback on that yet.  Will see at least 17%, but possibly more since shut off unnecessary compressed air uses on their own. Was running 70-80% and now 40-50% running.', 1, 0, 9),
(4573, 11176, 4, 'Reduce Compressed Air Pressure', 333, '2.4231', 2, 1000, 0, 7799, 'Reduce compressed air system pressure from 116 psig to 96 psig. Maintaining a pressure greater than required by the system provides little added benefit. Reducing pressure will decrease associated annual energy use by 16%.\n', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 7799, '2015-06-01', 0, 'We did do that. Also shut off some other unnecessary air demand. May have even recognized other issues and caught more problems and turned off the other uses.', 1, 0, 10),
(4574, 11236, 4, 'Replace Boiler System', 332, '2.1224', 2, 3403664, 2695644, 481167, 'Replace the Compartment House process heat boiler with a direct fire anox system, similar to the heating system in the Flex House.  This will increase process heating efficiency, reducing associated energy consumption by 1.9%.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 2695644, 481167, '2015-05-01', 0, 'Still need cost/savings details for this implementation, but it was completed May of 2015', 1, 0, 3),
(4575, 11237, 3, 'Recirculate Attemperation Water', 333, '3.4115', 4, 95638, 47819, 58681, 'Recirculate attemperation water using local pumps and implement new nozzles. This will reduce the flow through the well and house pumps, atomizing the water more effectively, and reducing associated annual energy consumption by 89.2%.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 47819, 58681, '0000-00-00', 11, 'Still considering implementation - assessing costs', 1, 0, 5),
(4576, 11238, 2, 'Capture Compartment House Heat', 321, '2.2443', 4, 38930, 33180, 38621, 'Capture and reintroduce the heated air exiting the germination processes in the Compartment Houses. This will lower the load on the boiler system, reducing associated annual energy consumption by 57,496 MMBtu annually.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 33180, 38621, '0000-00-00', 11, 'Still considering implementation - assessing costs', 1, 0, 4),
(4578, 11263, 7, 'Install Dedicated Air Compressor', 335, '2.4226', 2, 4920, 2460, 9718, 'Install a dedicated air compressor for the finger jointing dry fire sprinkler system to eliminate the operating hours of the 25 hp finger jointing compressor. This will reduce associated annual energy consumption by 98%.', 1, 0, 0, 0, 2460, 9718, '2015-06-15', 22, 'They implemented 5hp compressors on each of the sprinkler systems in each of the departments. The approximated total cost was 1,200 USD', 1, 0, 3),
(4579, 11264, 9, 'Replace Air Motors', 325, '2.4324', 1, 1352, 676, 948, 'Replace the air motors on the primer totes with electric motors and shut the Moulding air compressor off during nonproduction hours. These actions will eliminate a continuous compressed air use, reducing associated annual energy consumption by 57.1%.', 1, 0, 0, 0, 676, 948, '0000-00-00', 3, 'They have not implemented because the electrician said they would need to have a hoist system to pull the motors out of the totes. It would be too time consuming and not to mention the cost to rent out a hoist system', 1, 0, 2),
(4580, 11254, 8, 'Reduce Compressed Air Pressure', 325, '2.4231', 2, 500, 500, 877, 'Reduce compressed air system pressure in the Moulding building from 95 psig to 70 psig. Maintaining a pressure greater than that required by the system provides little added benefit. Reducing pressure will decrease associated annual energy use by 20%.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 500, 877, '0000-00-00', 18, 'The pressure has not been reduced since the paint line is backed up on that compressor air system. The paint line requires high pressure, reducing the air pressure will cause problems in the paint line because it has a high pressure demand ', 1, 0, 10),
(4581, 11314, 1, 'Bypass Stripping Towers', 333, '2.5121', 4, 21000, 10500, 37907, 'Bypass both Stripping Towers at ground level. This will reduce the hydraulic horsepower needed from the well pumps by reducing the elevation head. Doing so will reduce associated annual energy consumption by 45.5%.', 1, 0, 0, 0, 10500, 37907, '2014-02-01', 0, 'Still need full cost/savings details for this implementation, but it was completed February of 2014', 1, 0, 8),
(4582, 11315, 0, '', 0, '', 0, 200000, 0, 45000, '', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0),
(4583, 11317, 0, '', 0, '', 0, 75000, 0, 15000, '', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0),
(4584, 11318, 0, '', 0, '', 0, 100000, 0, 24000, '', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0),
(4585, 11319, 2, 'Improve Combustion Efficiency', 339, '2.1133', 2, 1500, 0, 1503, 'Tune the combustion system for the aluminum and steel hot dip tanks and the steamer to lower excess oxygen. This will increase combustion efficiency by optimizing the air-fuel ratio, and reduce natural gas consumption by 17.8%.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 3003, '0000-00-00', 12, 'Had a 3rd party come out. They looked at steamers and dip tanks. Steamers were able to get hotter after tuner, dip tanks unsure of efficiency increase. Company is looking at replacement of dip tanks rather than improving efficiency on tanks. Will probably take 2 years to replace tanks (optimistically), probably 3 more realistically. Will keep in mind energy efficiency during this tank replacement process (both combustion efficiency and insulating the lids, as mentioned in OMC)', 1, 0, 8),
(4586, 11320, 3, 'Install Efficient Lighting', 336, '2.7143', 3, 296553, 0, 29588, 'Install 215 watt high bay LED fixtures with distributed control technology throughout the facility. This will increase lighting efficiency and reduce operation hours, reducing associated annual energy consumption by 48%.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 29588, '2015-06-01', 0, 'Doing pilot project at North Base (different facility) for high bay lights. Concerns about sensitivity to lights. Probably will implement lighting in 2015-16. Technology is evolving fast, may not implement exactly but will take this concept.', 1, 0, 36),
(4587, 11321, 4, 'Reduce Compressed Air Pressure', 331, '2.4231', 2, 500, 0, 1626, 'Reduce compressed air system pressure from 150 psig to 100 psig. Maintaining a pressure greater than that required by the system provides little added benefit. Reducing pressure will decrease associated annual energy use by 11%.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 500, 3600, '2014-12-01', 0, 'Started this process. Interrupted by BPA. Rebuilt the VFD controls on the compressor. In Dec of 2014 they ran 25 hp compressor (unknown controls) at 120 psig. Only one complaint with this pressure - resolved it after one equipment replacement. Had to turn pressure back up to 150 psig due to re-shifted focus and BPA, but this seemed to work great. Estimated savings at 5,000 kWh per month based on meter. At 6 cents per kWh, this is an estimated savings of  $3,600 annually.\n\nLisa will follow through with an estimate of noticed energy savings from this measure.', 1, 0, 10),
(4589, 11323, 1, 'Optimize Compressor Sequencing', 332, '2.6221', 2, 500, 0, 4792, 'Reduce the operation hours of the low-unload compressor to operate only during maintenance periods of the primary VFD compressor. This will reduce annual low-unload compressor operation hours by 4,015 hours, reducing associated annual energy use by 48%.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 4605, '2015-10-01', 0, 'Will implement within 6 months, after BPA audit. Agrees with analysis. ', 1, 0, 4),
(4590, 11324, 5, 'Install Heat Recovery on Air Compressor', 332, '2.2434', 3, 9133, 0, 1074, 'Capture waste heat rejected by the air compressor, and use this waste heat to heat the main building. This rerouted waste heat from the air compressors will reduce the heat load on the HVAC system during cold months. This will reduce HVAC annual natural gas consumption by 4.4%.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 9133, 1074, '0000-00-00', 11, 'This has been delayed due to BPA audit. ', 1, 0, 4),
(4592, 11329, 1, 'Refrigeration Discharge Pressure', 340, '2.2621', 2, 250, 0, 11360, 'Lower the minimum ammonia condensing (discharge) pressure on the refrigeration compressors to 100 psig (63.5Â°F). This will decrease refrigeration system energy cost by 22%.\n', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 11360, '2014-06-24', 0, 'We implemented this the week after the energy assessment. We saved what estimated and it did not cost us anything with the exception of our labor since we just went and did it. No incentives were received for this project.', 1, 0, 7),
(4593, 11331, 0, '', 0, '', 0, 4000, 0, 2000, '', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0),
(4594, 11332, 0, '', 0, '', 0, 5000, 0, 1317, '', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0),
(4595, 11333, 3, 'Install Premium Plus Motors', 339, '2.4133', 1, 3268, 1634, 1567, 'Incrementally install NEMA premium plus motors in place of the current  motors on fill line one. This will increase the full load efficiency of the fill line motors from 83% to 89%, reducing associated annual energy consumption by 4%.\n', 1, 1, 0, 0, 1634, 1567, '2015-10-01', 0, 'We are replacing motors on conveyors with more efficient ones. This project was started on Line 1 and Line 2. Our approach to this has changed. At the end of last year we were informed that two of our lines are possibly going to be replaced with brand new turnkey lines that would have blow molding. Due to this we moved our motor replacements to the other lines. Currently we are replacing motors on the lines with more efficient motors. We have a downtime period in October where we will be installing several new motors actually. Cost does impact this project since there are several motors.', 1, 0, 7),
(4596, 11334, 0, '', 0, '', 0, 4000, 0, 2000, '', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0),
(4597, 11335, 4, 'Insulate Condensate Return', 340, '2.2131', 2, 417, 0, 800, 'Insulate the condensate return piping that is exposed with a fiber glass all-service jacket. This will reduce heat loss from hot surfaces, lowering annual energy consumption by 89% per year.\n', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 800, '2014-07-17', 0, 'We implemented this within one month after the energy assessment. This is something that we do now as on-going projects due to steam and condensate leaks. We saved what was estimated and the cost was close to estimated. No incentives were received for this project.', 1, 0, 11),
(4598, 11336, 0, '', 0, '', 0, 45000, 0, 10000, '', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0),
(4599, 11338, 0, '', 0, '', 0, 4000, 0, 1500, '', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0),
(4600, 11339, 2, 'Shut off Air Knives', 336, '2.4236', 2, 5544, 0, 6168, 'Install electronic flow control (EFC) to shut off fill line air knives on the weekends and during production down time. Doing so will decrease compressed air system annual energy use by 10%.\n', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 6168, '0000-00-00', 5, 'Although we did not implement the project from the assessment we would not have found this without the OSU Energy Assessment. We did reduce our air leaks and use of the air compressors. While investigating this project we came across a few things that we were not aware of that changed this project around. One thing we did was remove air knives that were on the lines or add air blowers that were tied to the line controls to run only when the line was running. The other part was we found out that an air line was run to our pH neutralization system to mix the waste water up. This was an added feature and run off a ball valve. The purpose was to open the compressed air line when an agitator failed. We found that this had been left on always. We have added controls to this that when an agitator faults a solenoid valve is opened and compressed air is sent to the system.', 1, 0, 7),
(4601, 11341, 3, 'Recover Air Compressor Heat', 334, '2.2434', 4, 2574, 1287, 2285, 'Recover heat from air compressor hot oil and air and send it to the high efficiency water heater. This will reduce wasted heat energy, reduce additional energy needs for the water heater, and reduce fan energy. This will reduce associated heat loss from the compressors by 87%.', 1, 0, 0, 0, 1287, 2285, '0000-00-00', 1, 'The facility did not implement this because the project was not prioritized above others due to difficulty of implementation and low saving.', 1, 0, 4),
(4602, 11342, 5, 'Upgrade Air Compressor Controls', 334, '2.4224', 2, 25801, 13066, 2833, 'Retrofit the 50 hp Quincy air compressor numbered Compressor 2 with variable frequency drive (VFD) controls and implement a VFD trims sequencing strategy to control the load on the compressors. These actions will reduce associated annual energy use by 37%.', 1, 0, 0, 0, 13066, 2833, '0000-00-00', 6, 'Facility is going through a massive air compressor upgrade. Spinoff', 1, 0, 7),
(4603, 11343, 4, 'Reduce Compressed Air Pressure', 334, '2.4231', 2, 500, 500, 870, 'Reduce compressed air system pressure from 115 psig to 90 psig. Maintaining a pressure greater than that required by the system provides little added benefit. Reducing the system pressure will decrease associated annual energy use by 7%.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 500, 870, '2014-04-01', 0, 'Facility implemented this and were pleased with results', 1, 0, 10),
(4604, 11344, 0, '', 0, '', 0, 1000, 0, 1000, '', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0),
(4605, 11346, 2, 'Install Efficient Lighting Controls', 339, '2.7135', 3, 3562, 2837, 2497, 'Install occupancy sensors and photosensors to use daylight whenever possible instead of artificial light. This will increase lighting efficiency and reduce operating hours, reducing associated annual energy consumption by 28%.', 1, 0, 0, 0, 2837, 2497, '2014-09-01', 0, 'Facility implemented this recommendation. Very satisfied.', 1, 0, 31),
(4606, 11347, 1, 'Install Fan VFD with O2 Controls', 331, '2.1116', 1, 4103, 2052, 3802, 'Install an oxygen (O2) sensor in the boiler stack and a variable frequency drive (VFD) on the forced draft fan to control fan speed based on oxygen content of the exhaust. This will increase combustion efficiency by optimizing the air-fuel ratio and reduce natural gas consumption by 10.1%. Additionally, it will reduce fan power draw causing a 53% decrease in annual fan electrical consumption.', 1, 0, 0, 0, 2052, 3802, '0000-00-00', 6, 'The facility is replacing this boiler in the next 12 to 14 months, so they did not implement this. Spinoff', 1, 0, 6),
(4607, 11408, 0, '', 0, '', 0, 500, 0, 1500, '', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0),
(4608, 11409, 2, 'Reduce Drag Out Losses', 333, '3.1161', 1, 4000, 4000, 2589, 'Reduce chemical drag out losses on antiquing lines. This will reduce the volume of chemical used and reduce the water treatment load on the ion exchange system, reducing hazardous waste generation. Associated annual expenses will be reduced by 31.4%.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 4000, 2589, '0000-00-00', 0, '', 1, 0, 4),
(4609, 11410, 1, 'Reduce Wire Kitting ', 333, '3.1161', 1, 10000, 10000, 73388, 'Move the seven most commonly used wires from inventory to final assembly. This will reduce kitting time, eliminate batches, and reduce associated annual labor expenses by 18.9%.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 10000, 73388, '0000-00-00', 0, '', 1, 0, 6),
