(4661, 11601, 6, 'Shut Down Idle Material Handling Fans', 336, '4.652', 2, 13800, 13800, 40207, 'Install programable logic controls (PLC) for the four dust collection systems to shut down idle material handling fans throughout production, during breaks, and on the weekends. These actions will reduce associated annual fan energy consumption by 22%.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 13800, 40207, '0000-00-00', 12, 'The facility believes that this is the best recommendation. They hope to implement this soon (this year). They like the payback time.', 1, 0, 12),
(4662, 11602, 2, 'Install Efficient Fan Blades', 0, '2.7243', 1, 27375, 27375, 28255, 'Replace the material handling radial fan blades with higher efficiency radial-tip fan blades. Efficiency can be improved from the current average of 60% to a reasonable average of 70%, reducing fan operation costs by 14%.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 27375, 28255, '0000-00-00', 13, 'They have looked into this and began analyzing the number of fan blades that they want to implement. They agree with our analysis and they like the payback time.', 1, 0, 14),
(4663, 11603, 5, 'Reduce Chipper Run Time', 336, '4.652', 2, 9020, 9020, 11008, 'Install programmable logic controls (PLC) on the three green end lathe chippers and set them to shut down when their respective lathe is not operating. Include motor soft starts on the eight and ten foot lathe chippers to help motors ramp up to speed in the event of a plug-up. These actions will reduce annual associated chipper energy consumption by 60%.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 9020, 11008, '0000-00-00', 12, 'The facility agrees that this should be implemented and hope to do it in 2016 with the right funding.', 1, 0, 7),
(4664, 11604, 3, 'Install Engineered Air Nozzles', 341, '2.4236', 2, 8550, 8550, 8466, 'Replace existing air nozzles with engineered air nozzles. This will decrease air used by blowdown wands, reducing associated annual energy consumption by 29%.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 8550, 8466, '0000-00-00', 6, 'This is not being implemented because they are trying to get away from using house air. ', 1, 0, 4),
